\f0\fs24 \cf0 THE CHRIST OF SCRIPTURE\
\
A study into the personal of Jesus The Christ from the earliest prophecies in the Old Testament to the concluding prophecies as recorded in The Apocalypse and all places in between.\
  \
We will use the same translation Jesus and the Apostles used which is the LXX. We will operate under the following maxims, namely:\
1)  Let God be true and every man a lier.\
2)  Let every Word of Doctrine be established by two or more witnesses.\
3)  We will ignore ensuing ideas that added to or took away from the God-breathed Word as corruptions of Babylonian Talmudic Rabbis and Early Church \'93Fathers\'94.\
4)  Wherever you reference Scripture in your answers, you will provide the entirety of the referenced citation(s) in line from the LXX for my convenience and review.\
5)  Pursuant to the maxims above and should Cosmology become relevant to this study; we will adhere strictly in accordance with Biblical Cosmology- ignoring any/all corruptions of modern science- falsely so called.\
  \
May we begin?\
\
Let us begin with the earliest posits of information. (Also with regard to our fourth maxim above and in addition to supplying the original Greek text you then follow with the English translation from the 1599 Geneva Bible.)\
\
Does it though?  \
  \
The (scandalous and repugnant to early believers) concept of any trinity is both pagan in origin and was not formalized until the Council of Nicea in 325 CE- followed shortly thereafter with the addition of the Holy Spirit as the third constituent by the Catholic Church.\
  \
So let us refine our beginning with a careful examination of of THE MONOTHEISTIC GOD in order to lay a proper foundation for our study of The Father\'92s ONLY BEGOTTEN SON.\
