\
## **The Foundation Established**\
\
1. **The One God is numerically one Being** \'97 not a council, not a triad, not a multiplicity of persons sharing essence.\
2. **He created the heavens and the earth ALONE** (44:24) \'97 this stands as the controlling text for Genesis 1:1.\
3. **He alone is Saviour** (45:21).\
4. **To Him alone every knee shall bow** (45:23).\
5. **He is incomparable** \'97 no being is *like* Him (46:5, 9).\
\
This is the God whom Jesus called **\uc0\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u953 \u957 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u957 ** \'97 *the only true God* (John 17:3) \'97 and whom Jesus called **\u964 \u8056 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u941 \u961 \u945  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957  \u956 \u959 \u965 ** \'97 *my Father and my God* (John 20:17).\
\
**The Father is the One God of Isaiah 44-46.** This is our foundation. Any study of the Son must be built upon \'97 and reconciled with \'97 this declaration, never against it.\
\
---\
\
## **A Question Now Properly Framed**\
\
With this foundation firm, we may now ask the right question \'97 the question that drives the rest of our study:\
\
> **Who, then, is the Son of this One God? In what sense is He called "the Word," "the Image," "the Firstborn," "the Lord through whom are all things" \'97 without violating the absolute singularity of the Father?**\
\
Shall we now turn to that question, beginning with the earliest prophetic posits of the Son in the Old Testament (e.g., Genesis 3:15, Psalm 2, Proverbs 8, Psalm 110)?\
\
\
Indeed we shall!\
\
\
Excellent. We now turn to the Old Testament's earliest posits of the Son \'97 the Father's **\uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u942 \u962 ** (only-begotten) \'97 built strictly upon the foundation we have laid: **the Father is the One God, and there is none beside Him.**\
\
We will proceed chronologically as the prophecies are given in the canonical order, beginning at the earliest.\
\
