## **POSIT #1 \'97 Genesis 3:15: The Seed of the Woman**\
\
### **LXX:**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7956 \u967 \u952 \u961 \u945 \u957  \u952 \u942 \u963 \u969  \u7936 \u957 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u963 \u959 \u957  \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u957 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u963 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u947 \u965 \u957 \u945 \u953 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u957 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u963 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u960 \u941 \u961 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u972 \u962  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u957 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u963 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u960 \u941 \u961 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8134 \u962 \'b7 \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u951 \u961 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u954 \u949 \u966 \u945 \u955 \u942 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u963 \u8058  \u964 \u951 \u961 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u960 \u964 \u941 \u961 \u957 \u945 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva Bible:**\
*"I will also put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed. He shall break thine head, and thou shalt bruise his heel."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1) The pronoun \uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962  is masculine singular** \'97 "**He**, He Himself" \'97 not *it*, not *they*. The LXX is grammatically remarkable here: the antecedent **\u963 \u960 \u941 \u961 \u956 \u945 ** (*seed*) is **neuter**, which would normally demand **\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 **. Yet the translators of the LXX (3rd-2nd century BC, *centuries before any Christian influence*) deliberately rendered **\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 masculine \'97 pointing to a singular **male person** as the Seed.\
\
This is the first prophetic posit of the coming **One** \'97 a single human Person, born of a woman, who will crush the head of the serpent.\
\
**(2) "The seed of the woman"** \'97 not of the man. In the entire patriarchal framework of Scripture, seed is reckoned through the father. This phrase is anomalous \'97 it anticipates a birth not according to the line of a human father. The two witnesses for this anomaly being fulfilled:\
\
**Isaiah 7:14 (LXX):**\
*"\uc0\u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u948 \u974 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u963 \u951 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u959 \u957 \'b7 \u7984 \u948 \u959 \u8058  \u7969  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u947 \u945 \u963 \u964 \u961 \u8054  \u7957 \u958 \u949 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u941 \u958 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u965 \u7985 \u972 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u954 \u945 \u955 \u941 \u963 \u949 \u953 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7960 \u956 \u956 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u965 \u942 \u955 \'b7"*\
\
**1599 Geneva:**\
*"Therefore the Lord himself will give you a sign. Behold, the virgin shall conceive and bear a son, and she shall call his name Immanuel."*\
\
The LXX explicitly says **\uc0\u7969  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *the virgin* \'97 not merely *a young woman*. This is **Witness #1** that the "seed of the woman" is a virgin-born Son.\
\
**Galatians 4:4 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u8005 \u964 \u949  \u948 \u8050  \u7974 \u955 \u952 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u955 \u942 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u967 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u965 , \u7952 \u958 \u945 \u960 \u941 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u957  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u933 \u7985 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 , \u947 \u949 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7952 \u954  \u947 \u965 \u957 \u945 \u953 \u954 \u972 \u962 , \u947 \u949 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u8017 \u960 \u8056  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u957 ,"*\
\
**1599 Geneva:**\
*"But when the fulness of time was come, God sent forth his Son made of a woman, and made under the Law,"*\
\
**Witness #2:** Paul confirms \'97 **\uc0\u947 \u949 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7952 \u954  \u947 \u965 \u957 \u945 \u953 \u954 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 "made of a woman" \'97 the very language of Genesis 3:15.\
\
---\
\
### What Genesis 3:15 establishes about the Son:\
\
- He is a **single, masculine Person** (\uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962 ).\
- He is **born of a woman** without a human father in view.\
- He is **sent by the One God** as the conqueror of the serpent.\
- He is, at this earliest point, a **promised man** \'97 the prophecy says nothing yet of pre-existence or divine status. We are at the *beginning* of the revelation; we will not retroject later disclosures into this verse.\
\
