### Observations of the utmost weight\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u940 \u952 \u951 \u957  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u8058 \u962  \u8017 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"I was established as king BY HIM."* The Son does not crown Himself; He is **made** king **by the Father**. This is again the language of dependence and appointment, not co-equality.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u933 \u7985 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u949 \u7990  \u963 \u973 , \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u963 \u942 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u957  \u947 \u949 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u957 \u951 \u954 \u940  \u963 \u949 ** \'97 *"My Son art Thou; I, today, have begotten Thee."*\
\
This is the **first explicit declaration in the Psalter** of the Father-Son relation, and it tells us two crucial things:\
\
**(a)** The Son is **begotten** (**\uc0\u947 \u949 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u957 \u951 \u954 \u945 **) \'97 He has an origin in the Father. This is the very meaning of **\u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u942 \u962 ** (only-begotten) \'97 *singularly brought forth from the Father.*\
\
**(b)** This begetting is fixed to a **day** \'97 **\uc0\u963 \u942 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u957 ** (*today*) \'97 a definite moment.\
\
