### Observation\
\
The Son **asks**; the Father **gives**. This is the consistent pattern: the Father is the Source (**\uc0\u7952 \u958  \u959 \u8023 **, 1 Cor 8:6), the Son is the Recipient and Agent. The nations are **given** to the Son as an inheritance \'97 He does not possess them by inherent right of independent deity; they are **granted** to Him by the Father.\
\
This is identical to the language of:\
\
**Matthew 28:18 (Greek):**\
*"...\uc0\u7960 \u948 \u972 \u952 \u951  \u956 \u959 \u953  \u960 \u8118 \u963 \u945  \u7952 \u958 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945  \u7952 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u961 \u945 \u957 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u960 \u8054  \u947 \u8134 \u962 ."*\
\
**1599 Geneva:**\
*"...All power is given unto me, in heaven, and in earth."*\
\
**\uc0\u7952 \u948 \u972 \u952 \u951 ** \'97 *"was given."* By whom? By the Father. The Son receives universal authority as a **gift** from the One God.\
\
