### Note on the textual difference\
\
The LXX reads **\uc0\u948 \u961 \u940 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u960 \u945 \u953 \u948 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u962 ** \'97 *"lay hold of instruction/discipline"* \'97 where the Hebrew has *"kiss the Son."* This is a notable variant. Either reading, the climactic line is the same: **\u956 \u945 \u954 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u953  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u959 \u7985  \u960 \u949 \u960 \u959 \u953 \u952 \u972 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 ** \'97 *"Blessed are all who trust in Him."* Trust is to be placed in the Anointed Son **whom the Father has set up** \'97 yet this trust does not violate Isaiah 45:22 ("Look unto Me, and be ye saved") because the Son is the Father's appointed channel of salvation; trusting the Son is trusting the Father's provision.\
\
