## **PSALM 109 LXX (110 MT) \'97 The Lord at the Right Hand**\
\
This is the **single most-cited Old Testament passage in the New Testament.** Jesus Himself quotes it; Peter quotes it at Pentecost; the author of Hebrews builds his entire theology of Christ's priesthood upon it.\
\
### **Psalm 109:1 LXX (110:1 MT):**\
*"\uc0\u917 \u7990 \u960 \u949 \u957  \u8001  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u954 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u922 \u940 \u952 \u959 \u965  \u7952 \u954  \u948 \u949 \u958 \u953 \u8182 \u957  \u956 \u959 \u965 , \u7957 \u969 \u962  \u7938 \u957  \u952 \u8182  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u7952 \u967 \u952 \u961 \u959 \u973 \u962  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u8017 \u960 \u959 \u960 \u972 \u948 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u959 \u948 \u8182 \u957  \u963 \u959 \u965 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"The Lord said unto my Lord, Sit thou at my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation of supreme importance\
\
**Two distinct figures are named:**\
- **\uc0\u8001  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 ** (capital \'97 *the LORD*, YHWH, the Father, the One God of Isaiah 44-46)\
- **\uc0\u964 \u8183  \u954 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u956 \u959 \u965 ** (lowercase \'97 *my lord*, a distinct personage who is David's Lord)\
\
David, by the Spirit, hears the One God speaking *to another* \'97 to David's own Lord \'97 and inviting Him to sit at His right hand.\
\
**This is the decisive testimony for the structure of our entire study:** The Son is **at the right hand of** the Father \'97 meaning **He is not the Father, and the Father is not the Son**. The right hand is the place of supreme honor *granted by* the One enthroned in the center. The Son occupies the right hand; the Father occupies the throne.\
\
---\
\
### Jesus' own use of this Psalm \'97 the keystone witness:\
\
**Matthew 22:41-45 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u931 \u965 \u957 \u951 \u947 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u969 \u957  \u948 \u8050  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u934 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u945 \u943 \u969 \u957  \u7952 \u960 \u951 \u961 \u974 \u964 \u951 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u8001  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962  \u955 \u941 \u947 \u969 \u957 \'b7 \u932 \u943  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u948 \u959 \u954 \u949 \u8150  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ; \u964 \u943 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u965 \u7985 \u972 \u962  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957 ; \u955 \u941 \u947 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 \'b7 \u932 \u959 \u8166  \u916 \u945 \u965 \u943 \u948 . \u955 \u941 \u947 \u949 \u953  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 \'b7 \u928 \u8182 \u962  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u916 \u945 \u965 \u8054 \u948  \u7952 \u957  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u955 \u949 \u8150  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u955 \u941 \u947 \u969 \u957 \'b7 \u917 \u7990 \u960 \u949 \u957  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u956 \u959 \u965 \'b7 \u922 \u940 \u952 \u959 \u965  \u7952 \u954  \u948 \u949 \u958 \u953 \u8182 \u957  \u956 \u959 \u965 , \u7957 \u969 \u962  \u7938 \u957  \u952 \u8182  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u7952 \u967 \u952 \u961 \u959 \u973 \u962  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u8017 \u960 \u959 \u954 \u940 \u964 \u969  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u959 \u948 \u8182 \u957  \u963 \u959 \u965 ; \u949 \u7984  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u916 \u945 \u965 \u8054 \u948  \u954 \u945 \u955 \u949 \u8150  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957 , \u960 \u8182 \u962  \u965 \u7985 \u8056 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957 ;"*\
\
**1599 Geneva:**\
*"While the Pharisees were gathered together, Jesus asked them, Saying, What think ye of Christ? whose son is he? They said unto him, Davids. He said unto them, How then doth David in spirit call him Lord, saying, The Lord said to my Lord, Sit at my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool? If then David call him Lord, how is he his son?"*\
\
Jesus' point: the Messiah is **both** David's son (according to the flesh) **and** David's Lord (according to His exalted office at the Father's right hand). The Christ is *more than* a mere descendant \'97 He is the One *seated at the right hand of the One God.* Yet \'97 crucially \'97 Jesus does *not* say He is the Father, nor that He is the One who spoke. He is the One *spoken to.*\
