### **Psalm 109:5 LXX (110:5 MT):**\
*"\uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u7952 \u954  \u948 \u949 \u958 \u953 \u8182 \u957  \u963 \u959 \u965 , \u963 \u965 \u957 \u941 \u952 \u955 \u945 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u941 \u961 \u8115  \u8000 \u961 \u947 \u8134 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u8150 \u962 \'b7"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"The Lord, that is at thy right hand, shall wound Kings in the day of his wrath."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation \'97 a remarkable inversion\
\
In v. 1 the Son sits at the Father's right hand. In v. 5 *the Lord is at* **the Son's** *right hand*. This is **not** a contradiction; it is the picture of the **Father and the Son operating in perfect coordination** \'97 wherever the Son acts in judgment, the Father stands with Him; wherever the Father is enthroned, the Son sits at His right.\
\
The Father and Son are **two distinct figures**, working together \'97 never collapsed into one Person, never elevated to two Gods. **One God, the Father; one Lord, His Christ \'97 at one another's right hand.**\
\
