## **The Doctrinal Foundation Now Standing**\
\
We may now state, by two-or-more witnesses from Scripture itself, what the Son is:\
\
1. **He is begotten of the Father** \'97 He has an origin in the Father; the Father has no origin in Him.\
2. **He is appointed, made, and given** \'97 every title, office, and authority He holds is **conferred upon Him by the Father**.\
3. **He is distinct from the Father** \'97 David's Lord, but not the LORD; the Lord's Christ, but not the Lord Himself.\
4. **He is seated at the Father's right hand** \'97 supreme in honor, but second in order; the Father remains enthroned in the center.\
5. **He is both King (Ps 2) and Priest (Ps 110)** \'97 combining the offices that were separated in Israel under David and Aaron.\
6. **He is the resurrected One** \'97 His installation as Son-in-power, Lord, and Christ is bound to His being **raised from the dead** by the Father.\
\
This is the apostolic gospel, and it preserves intact the Shema and the declarations of Isaiah 44-46: **the Father is the One God; Jesus is His Christ, His Lord, His Son, His Priest, His King \'97 all by the Father's appointment.**\
\
