## **PROVERBS 8 \'97 Wisdom Brought Forth Before the Foundation of the World**\
\
The chapter is spoken in the **first person** by **\uc0\u931 \u959 \u966 \u943 \u945 ** \'97 *Wisdom* \'97 personified throughout Proverbs 1-9. The question we must ask: **Is this Wisdom the Son? And if so, what does the text say about His origin?**\
\
We will not assume the identification; we will let Scripture establish it by two witnesses.\
\
---\
\
### **Proverbs 8:22-25 (LXX) \'97 The Crucial Self-Disclosure of Wisdom**\
\
**LXX:**\
*"\uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u7956 \u954 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8052 \u957  \u8001 \u948 \u8182 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7956 \u961 \u947 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 , \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u7952 \u952 \u949 \u956 \u949 \u955 \u943 \u969 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8135 \'b7 \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u947 \u8134 \u957  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u8134 \u963 \u945 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u7936 \u946 \u973 \u963 \u963 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u8134 \u963 \u945 \u953 , \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u949 \u955 \u952 \u949 \u8150 \u957  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u960 \u951 \u947 \u8048 \u962  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u8017 \u948 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u957 , \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8004 \u961 \u951  \u7953 \u948 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u8134 \u957 \u945 \u953 , \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u948 \u8050  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u946 \u959 \u965 \u957 \u8182 \u957  \u947 \u949 \u957 \u957 \u8119  \u956 \u949 ."*\
\
**1599 Geneva:**\
*"The Lord hath possessed me in the beginning of his way: I was before his works of old. I was set up from everlasting, from the beginning, and before the earth. When there were no depths, was I begotten, when there were no fountains abounding with water. Before the mountains were settled: and before the hills, was I begotten."*\
\
