\
### Observations of decisive importance\
\
**(1)** The LXX reads **\uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u7956 \u954 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949 ** \'97 *"The Lord created/founded me."* The verb is **\u954 \u964 \u943 \u950 \u969 **. The Geneva follows the Hebrew *qanah*, which can mean *possess, acquire, or beget.* This is the verse over which the great Arian controversy raged in the 4th century \'97 and it is one of the texts the post-Nicene party labored most strenuously to suppress or reinterpret, precisely because the LXX (which Jesus and the Apostles used \'97 per our maxims) reads **\u7956 \u954 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949 **.\
\
**Let God be true.** The LXX says: **The Lord brought-forth/founded Wisdom as the beginning (\uc0\u7936 \u961 \u967 \u942 \u957 ) of His ways, for His works.**\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u7952 \u952 \u949 \u956 \u949 \u955 \u943 \u969 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8135 ** \'97 *"Before the age He established me in the beginning."* Wisdom is founded by the Lord **before time itself**, before the **\u945 \u7984 \u974 \u957 **.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u960 \u961 \u8056  \u948 \u8050  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u946 \u959 \u965 \u957 \u8182 \u957  \u947 \u949 \u957 \u957 \u8119  \u956 \u949 ** \'97 *"Before all hills He BEGETS me."* The verb **\u947 \u949 \u957 \u957 \u940 \u969 ** \'97 *to beget* \'97 is the same root as **\u947 \u949 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u957 \u951 \u954 \u940  \u963 \u949 ** of Psalm 2:7 and **\u7952 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u957 \u951 \u963 \u940  \u963 \u949 ** of Psalm 109:3 LXX. **Three witnesses now agree on the same vocabulary**: the Son is **begotten** of the Father.\
\
