**(2)** **\uc0\u7972 \u956 \u951 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u7937 \u961 \u956 \u972 \u950 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u945 ** \'97 *"I was beside Him, fitting [things] together / harmonizing."* The Son, as Wisdom, is the Father's *Agent of arrangement* in creation. This now begins to reconcile Isaiah 44:24 ("I stretched out the heavens **alone**") with 1 Cor 8:6 ("through whom are all things"): **the Father alone is the Source; the Son is His Wisdom by whom He fits the works together.** The Father does it; He does it *by* His Wisdom \'97 His Wisdom is not a second God, but His own Begotten One acting as His instrument.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u8125  \u7969 \u956 \u941 \u961 \u945 \u957  \u948 \u8050  \u949 \u8016 \u966 \u961 \u945 \u953 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u951 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u974 \u960 \u8179  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"daily I was rejoicing in His face/presence."* The mutual delight between the Father and His Begotten One **before** the world was made.\
