Paul explicitly identifies Christ as **\uc0\u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u959 \u966 \u943 \u945 \u957 ** \'97 *the Wisdom of God* \'97 and says He was **made** (**\u7952 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u942 \u952 \u951 **) Wisdom **to us** **\u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *from God.* The Wisdom of Proverbs 8 is fulfilled in the Person of Christ.\
\
**Witness #2 \'97 Colossians 1:15-17 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u8005 \u962  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u954 \u8060 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7936 \u959 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965 , \u960 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u972 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u959 \u962  \u960 \u940 \u963 \u951 \u962  \u954 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962 , \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u7952 \u954 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u952 \u951  \u964 \u8048  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945 ... \u964 \u8048  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u948 \u953 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7956 \u954 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957 ..."*\
\
**1599 Geneva:**\
*"Who is the image of the invisible God, the first begotten of every creature. For by him were all things created... all things were created by him, and for him, And he is before all things..."*\
\
**\uc0\u960 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u972 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u959 \u962  \u960 \u940 \u963 \u951 \u962  \u954 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962 ** \'97 *"firstborn of all creation"* \'97 corresponds precisely to **\u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8052 \u957  \u8001 \u948 \u8182 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ** of Proverbs 8:22 LXX \'97 the Beginning of God's ways. And note the verb in both texts: **\u954 \u964 \u943 \u950 \u969 ** \'97 the very word used of Wisdom in Prov 8:22 and of all things being created **in** Christ in Col 1:16.\
\
**Two witnesses established:** Proverbs 8 is speaking of the Son in His pre-temporal relation to the Father.\
\
---\
\
### What Proverbs 8 establishes about the Son:\
\
1. He is **brought forth / founded** by the Lord as **the beginning of His ways** (v. 22).\
2. He is **begotten** before the creation of the earth, depths, mountains (vv. 24-25).\
3. He is **with** the Father **at** the work of creation, serving as the Father's Wisdom by which all things are fitted together (vv. 27-30).\
4. He is the Father's **delight** before the world is made (v. 30).\
5. **He is not the Father; He is brought forth from the Father, distinct from Him, beside Him.**\
\
---\
\
### A doctrinal observation per our maxims\
\
Notice carefully what Proverbs 8 does **not** say:\
\
- It does **not** say Wisdom is co-eternal in the sense of having no beginning. It explicitly says she was **founded / begotten** by the Lord.\
- It does **not** say Wisdom is *another God*. She is the Lord's Wisdom \'97 belonging to Him, brought forth from Him.\
- It does **not** violate Isaiah 44:24. The Lord stretches out the heavens *alone* \'97 by His own Wisdom, which is His. The Wisdom acting is *His*, not a separate Deity.\
\
This perfectly preserves the Shema and Isaiah 44-46 while honestly testifying to the Son's pre-temporal begetting. **The Son has an origin in the Father; the Father has no origin.** This is the consistent biblical witness, and it is the testimony of the LXX our Lord used.\
\
