### Observations\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u7952 \u954  \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u956 \u959 \u953  \u7952 \u958 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u973 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953 ** \'97 *"Out of you, for Me, He shall come forth."* The Ruler **comes forth** from Bethlehem **for the Father** (**\u956 \u959 \u953 ** \'97 *to/for Me*). The Son's appearing in Bethlehem is **for the Father's purpose**, given over to the Father's mission.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u945 \u7985  \u7956 \u958 \u959 \u948 \u959 \u953  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7936 \u960 \u8125  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8134 \u962  \u7952 \u958  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"His goings-forth are from the beginning, from days of old/eternity."*\
\
The Greek phrasing is plural \'97 **\uc0\u945 \u7985  \u7956 \u958 \u959 \u948 \u959 \u953 ** \'97 *the goings-forth.* This indicates **multiple comings-forth** of the Son:\
- His **begetting** before the foundations of the earth (Prov 8:24-25; Ps 109:3 LXX).\
- His subsequent **appearances** in Old Testament theophanies (which we will examine next).\
- His ultimate **going forth from Bethlehem** in the incarnation.\
\
The phrase **\uc0\u7936 \u960 \u8125  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8134 \u962  \u7952 \u958  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"from the beginning, from days of the age"* \'97 places His origin far back, before days as men count them. This corresponds exactly to **\u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u7952 \u952 \u949 \u956 \u949 \u955 \u943 \u969 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949 ** of Proverbs 8:23.\
\
