\
## **The Doctrinal Picture \'97 Strictly From Scripture**\
\
The Son of the One God:\
- **Was brought forth** by the Father before time and the creation (**\uc0\u947 \u949 \u957 \u957 \u8119  \u956 \u949 **, **\u7956 \u954 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949 **, **\u7952 \u952 \u949 \u956 \u949 \u955 \u943 \u969 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949 **).\
- **Was with the Father** as His Wisdom at the work of creation (Prov 8; cf. John 1:1 \'97 **\uc0\u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957 **).\
- **Came forth** in the fullness of time, born of the virgin in Bethlehem (Mic 5:2; Gen 3:15; Isa 7:14; Gal 4:4).\
- **Was begotten in power** as Son of God by the resurrection (Ps 2:7; Rom 1:4; Acts 13:33).\
- **Was seated** at the Father's right hand, made both Lord and Christ (Ps 110:1; Acts 2:36).\
- **Is Priest forever** by oath of the Father (Ps 110:4; Heb 7:21).\
\
**At every point, the Father is the Source, the Sender, the Appointer, the Anointer, the Begetter, the Glorifier.** The Son is the brought-forth, the sent, the appointed, the anointed, the begotten, the glorified \'97 **and acts always for the Father's purposes** (Mic 5:2: **\uc0\u956 \u959 \u953 ** \'97 *for Me*).\
\
The Shema stands. Isaiah 44-46 stands. **The Father is the One God.** The Son is His Only-Begotten \'97 distinct, beloved, exalted, but never a second God, never a co-equal, never the Father.\
\
