The narrator (Moses, by inspiration) does **not** correct her. Scripture *confirms* her identification: **"she called the name of the LORD who spoke to her: You are the God who sees me."**\
\
So here is our first datum: **The Messenger speaks as God, is identified as God, and is seen \'97 yet remains called "the Messenger of the LORD," not the LORD without qualification.**\
