### The reconciliation, by Scripture itself:\
\
- **No man has ever seen the Father.** Hagar did not see the Father. Abraham did not see the Father. Jacob did not see the Father. Moses did not see the Father. *Period.*\
- **The One whom they all saw \'97 and called "God" \'97 was the Only-Begotten Son**, the visible Image (**\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u954 \u8060 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7936 \u959 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965 **, Col 1:15) of the invisible Father.\
\
The Son **bears the Father's Name** (cf. Ex 23:21: *"My Name is in Him"* of the Angel; **John 17:11**: *"keep them in Thy Name which Thou hast given Me"*). The Son acts **for** the Father (Mic 5:2 \'97 **\uc0\u956 \u959 \u953 **), speaks **for** the Father, swears **by** the Father, blesses **for** the Father. When Hagar sees Him, she sees the **Image** of the unseen God \'97 not the Father Himself.\
\
**Therefore Isaiah 44-46 is not violated.** The Father remains unseen, unique, the sole God. The Son is the visible Messenger of that God \'97 His Begotten, sent forth from the Father from of old, bearing the Father's authority, Name, and message.\
