**Honest assessment:** The NT cites Micah 5:2 for the **birthplace** of the Christ \'97 *"out of Bethlehem"* \'97 but does **not** explicitly handle the second part of the verse: *"whose goings-forth are from of old, from days of eternity."* That second clause is in the OT text; the NT cites only the Bethlehem portion explicitly.\
\
**Status:** The **Bethlehem prophecy** is solidly established by Matt 2:5-6. The **"goings-forth from of old"** clause is **in the LXX text** but is **not explicitly cited or interpreted** in the NT. We can note the text; we should not lean on it as definitively interpreting pre-existence apart from explicit NT handling.\
