## **SUMMARY OF THE AUDIT**\
\
### Solidly established by explicit NT citation:\
\
1. **The Father is the One God** (Shema; Isa 44-46; John 17:3; 1 Cor 8:6; etc.)\
2. **Psalm 2** speaks of the Father's Anointed Son, fulfilled in Jesus (Acts 4:25-27; 13:33; Heb 1:5; 5:5)\
3. **Psalm 110** speaks of the Father and the Lord at His right hand, fulfilled in Jesus (Matt 22:44; Acts 2:34-36; Heb 1:13; 5:6; 7:17, 21)\
4. **Micah 5:2 (Bethlehem clause)** prophesies the Christ's birthplace, fulfilled in Jesus (Matt 2:5-6)\
5. **Genesis 22** is typological of the Father offering His Son (Heb 11:17-19 \'97 *"in a parable"*)\
\
### Plausible but NOT strictly established by explicit NT citation:\
\
6. **Genesis 3:15** \'97 the masculine **\uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u962 ** posits a male Person; the *fulfillment* in Jesus is thematic, not by direct citation.\
7. **Genesis 49:10** \'97 messianic in tone; no direct NT citation.\
8. **Numbers 24:17** \'97 messianic in tone; no direct NT citation.\
9. **Psalm 109:3 LXX** ("before the morning star") \'97 in the LXX text; no direct NT citation.\
10. **Micah 5:2 (goings-forth clause)** \'97 in the LXX text; the NT cites only the Bethlehem portion.\
11. **Proverbs 8** \'97 parallels Christ thematically; no direct NT citation identifying it.\
\
### Withdrawn:\
\
12. **The Angel of the LORD = the pre-incarnate Son** \'97 withdrawn for lack of explicit NT identification.\
\
