\
### Honest assessment of vv. 1-3:\
\
The Prologue, **strictly read**, can be understood in either of two ways consistent with the grammar:\
\
**Reading A:** **\uc0\u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 ** is a pre-existent *Person* distinct from the Father, who was "with" the Father and was "divine in nature" (\u920 \u949 \u972 \u962  qualitatively), and through whom the Father created.\
\
**Reading B:** **\uc0\u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 ** is the Father's own *expressed Word / creative utterance / plan*, "with Him" in the sense that His Word is always His own, "divine" in the sense that it is God's own Word, and the means by which He created \'97 exactly as Psalm 33:6 says.\
\
**Up to v. 3, both readings fit the Greek.** John has not yet decided the question for us.\
