## **JOHN 1:14 \'97 The Decisive Verse**\
\
Let us jump to the verse that *does* clarify John's intent:\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u922 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962  \u963 \u8048 \u961 \u958  \u7952 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u959  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u963 \u954 \u942 \u957 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8150 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u952 \u949 \u945 \u963 \u940 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 , \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u8033 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u8166 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8048  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u972 \u962 , \u960 \u955 \u942 \u961 \u951 \u962  \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And that Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we saw the glory thereof, as the glory of the only begotten Son of the Father) full of grace and truth."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962  \u963 \u8048 \u961 \u958  \u7952 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u959 ** \'97 *"the Word became flesh."* This is the decisive turning point. The Word \'97 whatever its prior mode of existence \'97 *became* flesh. The verb is **\u7952 \u947 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u959 ** (came to be, became).\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u8033 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u8166 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8048  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 *"glory as of the Only-Begotten from the Father."* John now explicitly connects the Word-become-flesh to **the Only-Begotten of the Father** \'97 the title used elsewhere of Jesus.\
\
**(3)** Notice the careful word: **\uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u8048  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 *"from beside the Father."* The Only-Begotten is *from* the Father \'97 consistent with everything Scripture has said about the Son being begotten of the Father.\
\
---\
\
### What v. 14 establishes:\
\
The Word that *was* in the beginning, was with God, and was qualitatively God \'97 **became flesh** and was the Only-Begotten of the Father. John is identifying the Word with the Son.\
\
**However \'97 observe carefully:** John does NOT say the Word *was* a Person before becoming flesh. He says the Word *became* flesh. This is consistent with either:\
\
**Reading A:** A pre-existent personal Word *took on* flesh (a personal Being clothed Himself in humanity).\
\
**Reading B:** The Father's eternal Word/plan/expression *was enacted as / became* flesh in the person of Jesus \'97 i.e., what was previously the Father's Word now took human form.\
\
Both readings honor v. 14.\
\
