### Observations\
\
**(1) Textual note:** There is a manuscript variant \'97 *"only-begotten God"* vs. *"only-begotten Son."* The earlier manuscripts (Sinaiticus, Vaticanus) read **\uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u8052 \u962  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962 **; the later Byzantine tradition reads **\u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u8052 \u962  \u933 \u7985 \u972 \u962 **. The Geneva, following the Textus Receptus, reads "only begotten Son."\
\
Per our maxims, we follow the LXX for the OT but the NT text is what it is. The Geneva text is what you have specified. Let us proceed with **"only begotten Son."**\
