**(2)** **\uc0\u920 \u949 \u8056 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u948 \u949 \u8054 \u962  \u7953 \u974 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u949 \u957  \u960 \u974 \u960 \u959 \u964 \u949 ** \'97 *"No man hath seen God at any time."* This is the absolute statement. **No one has ever seen God** (the Father). This is consistent with Ex 33:20, 1 Tim 6:16, and Isa 44-46's declaration that the Father is uniquely sovereign and (in this verse) unseen.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u8001  \u956 \u959 \u957 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u8052 \u962  \u933 \u7985 \u8056 \u962 ... \u7952 \u958 \u951 \u947 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u959 ** \'97 *"the only-begotten Son... has declared/explained Him."* The Son is the One who has made the Father known. **\u7952 \u958 \u951 \u947 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u959 ** is the root of our word "exegesis" \'97 *He has unfolded, explained, expounded* the Father.\
\
