**(2)** Their being born "of God" parallels \'97 and is contrasted with \'97 the Word's own relation to the Father. The believer is **born of God**; the Word *was with* God from the beginning. The relationships are not the same kind.\
\
**(3)** The phrase **\uc0\u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"believing in His Name"* \'97 is highly significant. Recall Ex 23:21: *"My Name is in Him."* Faith in the Name of the Sent One is faith in the Father whose Name He bears.\
