**(2)** **\uc0\u959 \u8016 \u967  \u7937 \u961 \u960 \u945 \u947 \u956 \u8056 \u957  \u7969 \u947 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u959  \u964 \u8056  \u949 \u7990 \u957 \u945 \u953  \u7988 \u963 \u945  \u920 \u949 \u8183 ** \'97 *"did not regard being equal with God a thing to be grasped/seized."* The phrase is contested in translation. Reading carefully:\
- **\uc0\u7937 \u961 \u960 \u945 \u947 \u956 \u972 \u962 ** = a thing seized, plunder, something to be grasped or held onto.\
- **\uc0\u964 \u8056  \u949 \u7990 \u957 \u945 \u953  \u7988 \u963 \u945  \u920 \u949 \u8183 ** = *"the being equal with God."*\
