**(4)** **\uc0\u956 \u959 \u961 \u966 \u8052 \u957  \u948 \u959 \u973 \u955 \u959 \u965  \u955 \u945 \u946 \u974 \u957 , \u7952 \u957  \u8001 \u956 \u959 \u953 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u969 \u957  \u947 \u949 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"taking the form of a servant, becoming in the likeness of men."* The *taking* and *becoming* imply a transition from a prior state.\
