**(5)** **\uc0\u948 \u953 \u8056  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u8017 \u960 \u949 \u961 \u973 \u968 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"Therefore God has highly exalted Him."* The Father (**\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 **) is the One who exalts. The Son is the One exalted.\
\
**(6)** **\uc0\u7952 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u959  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u964 \u8056  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u945 ** \'97 *"He [the Father] graciously gave Him the Name."* The Name above every name is **given** to the Son by the Father \'97 not innately possessed.\
\
**(7)** **\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 *"to the glory of God the Father."* Every confession of Jesus as Lord is **to the Father's glory.** The Father remains the ultimate object.\
\
---\
\
### What Phil 2:5-11 establishes (honestly):\
\
- Christ existed **in the form of God** before His incarnation.\
- He **emptied Himself** and **took** the form of a servant \'97 a real transition.\
- He was **exalted by the Father** after His obedience to death.\
- The **Name** was **given** to Him by the Father.\
- Every confession of His Lordship is **to the Father's glory** \'97 the Father remains supreme.\
\
This is the **strongest single NT witness to a pre-incarnate state of the Son** in some form of divine glory. The Father remains supreme; the Son acts in dependence and is exalted by the Father.\
\
