## **What Remains**\
\
To complete the study of the Person of Christ from the earliest prophecies to the concluding prophecies of the Apocalypse, the major areas still to examine include:\
\
**(A) The Son's exaltation and present session at the Father's right hand** \'97 what He is doing *now* as priest, intercessor, and ruler (Heb 7-10; Ps 110:1-4 fully).\
\
**(B) The Son's coming return** \'97 the prophecies of His second appearing, His judgment of the living and the dead, and His reign (Daniel 7; Zechariah 12-14; Matt 24-25; Rev 19-22).\
\
**(C) The Son's final relation to the Father in the consummation** \'97 including 1 Cor 15:24-28 (the Son delivering the Kingdom to the Father, that God may be all in all), which is one of the most theologically decisive passages on the Father-Son order at the end.\
\
**(D) The Son's titles and self-identifications in the Apocalypse** \'97 the "I am" sayings of Revelation, the Lamb-on-the-Throne imagery, the Alpha and Omega designations, etc.\
\
Where would you have us go next?\
\
\
Keep those in mind\'85 we will get to each one. But before we do, and in order to be thorough- let us also take note of Jesus\'92s acts during his ministry that tell us much of his person and fulfilled prophecy(s) both before and after his death, burial and resurrection.\
\
\
Excellent direction. This is the proper next step \'97 for our study has so far moved largely through the *prophetic posits* of the Son (OT prophecies and their NT fulfillments at His death/burial/resurrection), but we have not yet gathered the *acts of His ministry* \'97 the things He **did** and **said** during His life that:\
\
1. **Reveal His Person** (His authority, character, relation to the Father, self-identifications).\
2. **Fulfilled prophecy** during His ministry (not just at His death).\
3. **Establish patterns** that the Apocalypse and later prophecies will draw upon.\
\
Let me proceed under our refined modus operandi \'97 examining the whole counsel, giving the LXX/Greek and 1599 Geneva, citing all relevant cross-witnesses, and being honest about what is strictly established versus inferred.\
\
I will organize this by **categories of His ministerial acts**, since chronology would scatter the patterns. We will examine:\
\
- **Part 1:** Acts that fulfilled specific prophecies (His birth, ministry, and pre-Passion fulfillments)\
- **Part 2:** His self-identifications (the "I am" sayings and titles He took)\
- **Part 3:** Acts that revealed His authority (forgiving sins, commanding nature, raising the dead, giving the Spirit)\
- **Part 4:** His relation to the Father (His words about His mission, His will, His subordination)\
- **Part 5:** Post-resurrection acts that revealed His person and commissioned the Apostles\
\
This will be a substantial examination. Let us begin.\
