\
### Observation of significant weight\
\
**Isaiah 40:3 says: "Prepare the way of the LORD (\uc0\u954 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965 )."** The Gospels apply this to John the Baptist preparing the way of **Jesus**. This is a strong identification: Jesus is the One *whose* way is prepared, and the One being prepared for is called **\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962 ** in Isaiah.\
\
This does not automatically mean Jesus is identical with **YHWH** \'97 but it does mean **the One coming in the LORD's name and authority**, **bearing the LORD's Name** (cf. Phil 2:9: the Name above every name given to the Son). The way of the LORD is prepared because the LORD is acting *through* His Christ.\
\
