### Observation of supreme importance\
\
**Jesus' first recorded sermon in His own town** consists of:\
1. Reading Isaiah 61:1-2 LXX.\
2. Declaring: **"This day is this Scripture fulfilled in your ears."**\
\
This is **Jesus' own direct self-identification** as the Spirit-anointed Servant. He stops reading at *"the acceptable year of the LORD"* \'97 *not* continuing to *"the day of vengeance of our God,"* because that day is yet future. His first coming is the year of grace; the day of vengeance belongs to His return.\
\
This is *Jesus' own claim* that the prophet's *"Spirit of the LORD is upon Me"* is *His own voice*. He is the Anointed.\
\
