### Observation of great weight\
\
**Two NT witnesses** (John 19 and Rev 1) bind **Zechariah 12:10** directly to Jesus' piercing on the cross and to His future return. This is one of the most important prophetic texts in our study because **it appears at both ends \'97 fulfilled at the crucifixion AND to be fulfilled at His return.**\
\
**A critical note on the Greek:** The LXX of Zech 12:10 reads **\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u953 \u946 \u955 \u941 \u968 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u949 ** \'97 *"they shall look upon Me"* \'97 and **\u954 \u972 \u968 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u957 ** \'97 *"they shall mourn for Him."* The shift from *"Me"* to *"Him"* within the same verse is striking. The LORD speaks (*"they shall look upon Me"*) \'97 yet they mourn for *Him* (a third person). This is the kind of Father-Son interplay we have been noting throughout: the LORD's piercing is the piercing of His Sent One, and the mourning is for that Sent One.\
\
