### Observation\
\
**Jesus' confession before the high priest combines:**\
- **Psalm 110:1** (*"sitting at the right hand of power"*)\
- **Daniel 7:13** (*"coming on the clouds of heaven"*)\
\
This is **Jesus' own claim of identity**: He is the **Son of Man** of Daniel 7, who will be enthroned and given universal dominion by the **Ancient of Days** (the Father). His title **Son of Man** is therefore not merely a humble human designation \'97 it is a claim to the **prophesied Heavenly Figure** who will receive eternal dominion from the Father.\
\
This is also the **second witness alongside Psalm 110** for the Son's enthronement at the Father's right hand.\
\
**An important note for our study:** In Daniel 7, the **Son of Man** is *brought before* the **Ancient of Days** \'97 He is *not* the Ancient of Days. He is a *distinct figure* who *receives* dominion *from* the Ancient of Days. This perfectly preserves our foundation: the Father is the One God on the throne; the Son receives all authority from Him.\
\
