### Observations on Melchizedek\
\
**(1)** Melchizedek is **\uc0\u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u8058 \u962  \u931 \u945 \u955 \u8052 \u956 ** (*King of Salem*) and **\u7985 \u949 \u961 \u949 \u8058 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8017 \u968 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u965 ** (*Priest of God Most High*) \'97 both **King** *and* **Priest** in one person.\
\
**(2)** He appears suddenly in the narrative without genealogy, predecessor, or successor.\
\
**(3)** Abraham \'97 the patriarch of Israel \'97 **tithes to him** and **receives his blessing.**\
\
**(4)** Salem = Jerusalem (cf. Ps 76:2).\
