### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For such an high Priest it became us to have, which is holy, harmless, undefiled, separate from sinners, and made higher than the heavens: Which needeth not daily as those high Priests to offer up sacrifice, first for his own sins, and then for the people's: for that did he once when he offered up himself. For the Law maketh men high Priests, which have infirmity: but the word of the oath that was since the Law, maketh the Son, who is consecrated forevermore."*\
