### Observations\
\
**(1)** The Son is **holy, harmless, undefiled, separated from sinners** \'97 fulfilling Isa 53:9 (*"He had done no violence, neither was any deceit in His mouth"*).\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7952 \u960 \u959 \u943 \u951 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u966 \u940 \u960 \u945 \u958 ** \'97 *"this He did once for all."* The Son's sacrifice of Himself is **once for all** \'97 never to be repeated. This will become a key theme of chapter 10.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u933 \u7985 \u8056 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945  \u964 \u949 \u964 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u969 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u957 ** \'97 *"the Son, perfected forever."* The Son has been **perfected** (**\u964 \u949 \u964 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u969 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u957 ** \'97 completed, brought to His full appointed state) **forever.** This is His present condition.\
