### Observation of foundational weight\
\
**1 Timothy 2:5 is decisive for our entire study.** Paul declares:\
- **\uc0\u949 \u7991 \u962  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 *one God* (the Father, per our foundation).\
- **\uc0\u949 \u7991 \u962  \u956 \u949 \u963 \u943 \u964 \u951 \u962 ** \'97 *one Mediator* \'97 between God and men.\
- **\uc0\u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962 ** \'97 *the Man Christ Jesus*.\
\
**The Mediator is the Man Christ Jesus.** Paul, even after His exaltation, calls Him **\uc0\u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *Man*. The mediation is **between God [the Father] and men** \'97 and the Mediator stands between as **a Man**.\
\
This is a critical text in our study because it preserves both:\
- **The Father as the One God** (per the Shema and Isa 44-46).\
- **The Son as the exalted Man** who mediates between God and men.\
\
The Son's **mediation** at the Father's right hand is **as Man** \'97 bearing the humanity He assumed in incarnation forever, now glorified.\
\
