## **What This Establishes About His Person \'97 Carefully**\
\
**(1)** **The Son is, *now*, a living Man** \'97 exalted, glorified, but still **the Man Christ Jesus** (1 Tim 2:5). He did not shed His humanity at the resurrection; He took it with Him into heaven.\
\
**(2)** **He bears the marks of His suffering even now.** The risen Christ appeared with pierced hands and feet and side (John 20:25-27); the Lamb in the Apocalypse appears **as having been slain** (Rev 5:6). The crucified Man is the enthroned Priest.\
\
**(3)** **He acts always in dependence on and submission to the Father.** Even at the Father's right hand, He waits *for the Father to subdue His enemies*. His enthronement does not erase the order: the Father is the One supreme God; the Son rules **at His right hand** by His appointment.\
\
**(4)** **He is the only Mediator** between the Father and humanity. No priest stands beside Him. No Mary, no saint, no apostle, no minister mediates between God and men \'97 **only the Man Christ Jesus.** This is critical doctrine, and it is firmly established.\
\
**(5)** **His ministry is *for us*.** Every act of His present session \'97 His appearing, His interceding, His waiting, His opening the way \'97 is **\uc0\u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ** (*on our behalf*). The Son's enthronement is not a private glory; it is an active ministry for those who come to the Father through Him.\
\
---\
\
## **A Critical Observation Preserving Our Foundation**\
\
Notice that throughout Hebrews 7-10, the Father remains **\uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 *the God* \'97 to whom:\
- The Son offered Himself (9:14: **\uc0\u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 **).\
- The Son sat down at His right hand (10:12: **\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u948 \u949 \u958 \u953 \u8119  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 **).\
- We come through the Son (7:25: **\uc0\u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 **).\
- The Father's house is overseen by the Son (10:21: **\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u8054  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u959 \u7990 \u954 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 **).\
- The Father swore the oath establishing the Son's priesthood (7:21).\
- The Father prepared the body for the Son's incarnation (10:5).\
- The Father's will is what the Son came to do (10:7-9).\
- The Father is the One who will make the Son's enemies His footstool (10:13).\
\
**The foundation we established at the beginning \'97 the Father as the One God \'97 is preserved unbroken throughout the Son's high-priestly ministry.** The Son is never a rival to the Father, never an independent Deity, never "another God" \'97 He is **the appointed and beloved Son**, **the eternal Priest by the Father's oath**, **the Mediator between God and men as the Man Christ Jesus**.\
\
