### Observations of supreme importance for our study\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u8033 \u962  \u965 \u7985 \u8056 \u962  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u959 \u965 ** \'97 *"as a Son of Man."* The figure is described as **like a son of man** \'97 i.e., **in the form of a Man.** This corresponds with everything we have established about the Son: He is the exalted Man Christ Jesus (1 Tim 2:5; Heb 9:24).\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u8054  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u957 \u949 \u966 \u949 \u955 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u959 \u8016 \u961 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"coming on the clouds of heaven."* The mode of His coming is on the clouds \'97 fulfilled in:\
- Acts 1:9-11 (a cloud received Him; He shall so come)\
- Matt 24:30; 26:64\
- Rev 1:7\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u8033 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u953 \u8056 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8134 \u957 ** \'97 *"He came as far as the Ancient of Days."* The Son of Man **approaches** the Ancient of Days. **He is brought *before* the Ancient of Days \'97 He is *not* the Ancient of Days.** This is decisive for our foundation. Two distinct figures: the Father enthroned, and the Son of Man brought before Him.\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u7952 \u948 \u972 \u952 \u951  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u7952 \u958 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 ** \'97 *"authority was given to Him."* **By whom?** The text's structure makes it clear: by the Ancient of Days (the Father). This is the same passive language we have seen throughout \'97 **the Father gives; the Son receives.** Matches Matt 28:18 (*"All authority has been given to Me"*) \'97 explicitly received from the Father.\
\
**(5)** **\uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u964 \u8048  \u7956 \u952 \u957 \u951  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u947 \u8134 \u962 ... \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u955 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u949 \u973 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u945 ** \'97 *"all the nations of the earth... serving/worshipping Him."* The verb **\u955 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u949 \u973 \u969 ** is the verb for **divine worship/service** \'97 used of worship rendered to God. The Son of Man receives the divine service of all nations **by the Father's grant**.\
\
This perfectly fulfills the pattern of Isa 45:23 \'97 *"unto Me every knee shall bow"* \'97 which Paul applies to Jesus in Phil 2:10-11, **"to the glory of God the Father."** The worship rendered to the Son is by the Father's will and to the Father's glory.\
\
**(6)** **\uc0\u7952 \u958 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945  \u945 \u7984 \u974 \u957 \u953 \u959 \u962 ... \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u945  \u7973 \u964 \u953 \u962  \u959 \u8016  \u956 \u8052  \u966 \u952 \u945 \u961 \u8135 ** \'97 *"eternal authority... a kingdom that shall not be destroyed."* The Son's reign, granted by the Father, is everlasting.\
\
