### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And in that day will I seek to destroy all the nations that come against Jerusalem. And I will pour upon the house of David, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem the Spirit of grace and of compassion, and they shall look upon me, whom they have pierced, and they shall lament for him, as one mourneth for his only son, and be sorry for him as one is sorry for his firstborn."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation of supreme importance \'97 the *Father's* voice and the *Son's* piercing\
\
This is one of the most theologically rich verses in all of Scripture for our study.\
\
**The speaker is the LORD** (the Father, the Creator of v. 1).\
\
**The Father says:**\
- **\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u953 \u946 \u955 \u941 \u968 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u949  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u8125  \u8039 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u969 \u961 \u967 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 ** \'97 *"they shall look upon **Me** whom they have pierced."*\
- Then immediately: **\uc0\u954 \u972 \u968 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957 ** \'97 *"they shall mourn for **Him**"* (third person).\
\
**The Father speaks of the piercing as if it were done to *Him* \'97 and yet the mourning is for *another* (Him).** This is the very paradox of the Father-Son union we have been carefully tracking: **what is done to the Son is felt by the Father.** The piercing of the Son is the piercing of the Father in some real sense \'97 yet the Son is distinct (mourned *as a beloved Son*, *as a firstborn*).\
\
The phrase **\uc0\u8033 \u962  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u951 \u964 \u8183 ** \'97 *"as for a beloved son"* \'97 uses the same Greek term as Genesis 22:2 LXX (*"Take your beloved son"*), Matt 3:17 (*"My beloved Son"*), and 2 Pet 1:17 \'97 establishing the typology. The pierced one is **the Father's beloved Son.**\
\
