### Critical observation for our foundation\
\
**Zech 14:5 says: "The LORD my God shall come."** Yet the return is fulfilled in **Jesus' coming.** Does this collapse Jesus into being the Father?\
\
**No.** The pattern is consistent with everything we have established: **the LORD acts through His Sent One.** When the Son comes, the LORD comes \'97 because the Son comes in the Father's Name (Ex 23:21 \'97 *"My Name is in Him"*), with the Father's authority (Matt 28:18), and at the Father's appointed time (Mark 13:32; Acts 1:7).\
\
The Father does not personally descend to the Mount of Olives; **the Son does** \'97 but His coming is **the LORD's coming**, because He bears the Father's Name and acts as the Father's Representative.\
