### **1599 Geneva (Ps 110:1):**\
*"The Lord said unto my Lord, Sit thou at my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool."*\
\
---\
\
### Critical observation\
\
**In Psalm 110:1, it is the Father who promises: "until I make thine enemies thy footstool"** \'97 the Father is the One subduing the enemies for the Son.\
\
**In 1 Cor 15:25, Paul writes: "He must reign until He has put all enemies under His feet."** Paul appears to attribute the subduing to the Son \'97 yet Paul immediately clarifies in v. 27 that **the One subduing all things is the Father.** So **"He must reign until He has put"** in v. 25 means: *the Son must reign **until** the moment when **all** things have been put (by the Father) under His feet.* The Son's reign continues *until* this subjugation is complete.\
\
The harmony is preserved: **the Father subdues, by His own power and through His Son's reign, all things under the Son's feet** \'97 and then the Son hands the Kingdom back to the Father.\
\
