### **Clause 9: \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8086  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u7952 \u957  \u960 \u8118 \u963 \u953 \u957  \'97 *"that God may be all in all"***\
\
This is the **ultimate purpose clause** (**\uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945 ** \'97 *in order that*) of the entire consummation.\
\
**\uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962 ** \'97 *the God* (with the article) \'97 = the Father (consistent with v. 24, where God is identified as the Father).\
\
**\uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u7952 \u957  \u960 \u8118 \u963 \u953 \u957 ** \'97 *"all in all"* \'97 that is, **the Father will be everything in everything.** The Father's universal supremacy will be unmediated, unrivaled, and absolute. Every creature, every place, every reality \'97 **God will be all and in all.**\
\
The Son's entire mission \'97 His incarnation, His suffering, His resurrection, His enthronement, His reign, His judgment, His subjugation of enemies, and even His own final subjection \'97 is **toward this end: that the Father may be all in all.**\
\
This is the consummation of:\
- **Phil 2:11**: *"every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, **to the glory of God the Father**."*\
- **Zech 14:9**: *"and the LORD shall be King over all the earth: in that day shall there be **one LORD, and His Name one**."*\
- **Isaiah 45:23**: *"unto Me every knee shall bow, every tongue shall swear by Me."*\
- **John 17:3**: *"that they might know thee, the only true God, and Jesus Christ whom thou hast sent."*\
