### Observation of foundational importance\
\
The very first verse establishes the **chain of revelation**:\
\
1. **\uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ** (the God = the Father) \'97 **gives** the revelation\
2. **to \uc0\u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u962 ** (Jesus Christ)\
3. who **sends His angel**\
4. **to His servant John**.\
\
**The Father is the Source.** Even at the climax of all prophecy, the chain begins with the Father. The Apocalypse is not Jesus' independent vision \'97 it is **what the Father gave Him.** This perfectly continues the pattern we established throughout: *"the Son can do nothing of Himself"* (John 5:19); *"the Father showeth Him all things"* (John 5:20); *"only the Father knows"* (Mark 13:32).\
\
This single verse is the **interpretive key** for the entire book. Whatever the Apocalypse reveals about the Son, it begins with the Son **receiving** from the Father what He then communicates.\
