## **REVELATION 1:8 \'97 A CRITICAL TEXT REQUIRING CAREFUL EXAMINATION**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u7960 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u964 \u8056  \u7948 \u955 \u966 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8056  \u8046 , \u955 \u941 \u947 \u949 \u953  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 , \u8001  \u8034 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7974 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 , \u8001  \u928 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u961 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the ending, saith the Lord, Which is, and Which was, and Which is to come, even the Almighty."*\
\
---\
\
### **Honest examination \'97 who is speaking?**\
\
This verse is crucial because it is often cited as evidence that Jesus is Alpha and Omega. Let us read it carefully.\
\
**The speaker identifies Himself as:**\
- **\uc0\u964 \u8056  \u7948 \u955 \u966 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8056  \u8046 ** \'97 *"the Alpha and the Omega"* (the first and the last letters of the Greek alphabet \'97 meaning *"the First and the Last"*)\
- **\uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 *"the Lord God"* \'97 combining the divine titles\
- **\uc0\u8001  \u8034 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7974 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"the One who is, was, and is to come"* \'97 **the exact title of the Father given in v. 4**\
- **\uc0\u8001  \u928 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u961 ** \'97 *"the Almighty / All-Sovereign"* \'97 the LXX standard rendering of **YHWH Sabaoth**, the LORD of Hosts\
\
**Honest assessment:** The titles in v. 8 are **identical to those given to the Father in v. 4**, especially **\uc0\u8001  \u8034 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7974 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 .** The most natural reading is that **the Father Himself is speaking in v. 8** \'97 interrupting briefly to declare His own eternal identity, before the narrative continues with John's vision.\
\
Some interpreters take this as Jesus speaking (because Jesus also uses **"Alpha and Omega"** in Rev 22:13). But:\
- **v. 4** has just identified **"the One who is, was, and is to come"** as distinct from **Jesus Christ** (named after "Him").\
- **\uc0\u8001  \u928 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u961 ** is the LXX title for **YHWH Sabaoth** \'97 the Father.\
- Throughout Revelation, **\uc0\u8001  \u928 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u961 ** is consistently used of the Father (Rev 4:8; 11:17; 15:3; 16:7; 19:6; 21:22).\
\
**Therefore, by careful reading, v. 8 is the Father speaking.** This is the Father's self-identification as the Alpha and Omega, the Almighty, the One who eternally is, was, and is to come.\
\
This **does not preclude** the Son from also being called "Alpha and Omega" in Rev 22:13 \'97 but we will examine that text carefully on its own when we reach it, and we will not pre-commit to identification.\
\
