## **REVELATION 1:17-18 \'97 THE FIRST AND THE LAST, THE LIVING ONE**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"...\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7956 \u952 \u951 \u954 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u948 \u949 \u958 \u953 \u8048 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u960 \u8125  \u7952 \u956 \u8050  \u955 \u941 \u947 \u969 \u957 \'b7 \u924 \u8052  \u966 \u959 \u946 \u959 \u8166 \'b7 \u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u8001  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7956 \u963 \u967 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u950 \u8182 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u951 \u957  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7984 \u948 \u959 \u8058  \u950 \u8182 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 \u962  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u974 \u957 \u969 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7956 \u967 \u969  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u954 \u955 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8069 \u948 \u959 \u965 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"...and he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not: I am that first and that last, And am alive, but I was dead: and behold, I am alive for evermore, Amen: and I have the keys of hell and of death."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of foundational importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u8001  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7956 \u963 \u967 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"I am the First and the Last."* This is a direct echo of **Isaiah 44:6 LXX** and **48:12 LXX** \'97 which we examined at the foundation of our study:\
\
**Isaiah 44:6 LXX:**\
*"...\uc0\u7960 \u947 \u8060  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u945 \u8166 \u964 \u945 , \u960 \u955 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8166  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ."*\
\
**1599 Geneva:** *"...I am the first, and I am the last, and without me is there no God."*\
\
**Isaiah 48:12 LXX:**\
*"...\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 ."*\
\
**1599 Geneva:** *"...I am, I am the first, and I am the last."*\
\
**Honest theological assessment:** In Isaiah, **"the First and the Last"** is the LORD's own self-identification. Here, **Jesus** declares Himself **"the First and the Last."**\
\
This is a significant text. We must read it carefully and honestly, neither overstating nor understating.\
\
**What is established:** The Son takes the LORD's self-identifying title onto Himself. He speaks the Father's own self-disclosure formula.\
\
**What is *not* established:** That the Son is the Father, or that the Son's "First and Last" identity erases His distinction from the Father, or that the Shema is overthrown.\
\
**How are we to understand this consistently with our foundation?**\
\
The pattern we have established throughout is that **the Son bears the Father's Name** (Ex 23:21; John 17:11-12; Phil 2:9). When the Son speaks the LORD's words and bears the LORD's titles, **He does so as the One in whom the Name dwells.** This is the consistent biblical witness \'97 *not* that the Son is identical to the Father in Person, but that **the Father's Name, glory, and self-disclosure are entrusted to and manifested through the Son.**\
\
So when Jesus says *"I am the First and the Last,"* He is \'97 by the Father's appointment and the Name He bears \'97 exercising the LORD's self-identification as the One in whom the LORD is fully revealed. The Father's "I am the First and the Last" is now spoken through the Son's mouth, because the Son is the Father's full self-expression to the creation.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u8001  \u950 \u8182 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u949 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u951 \u957  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7984 \u948 \u959 \u8058  \u950 \u8182 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 \u962 ** \'97 *"the Living One \'97 I became dead, and behold I am alive forever and ever."*\
\
**This is the decisive distinguishing mark.** The First and the Last who speaks here is **the One who died and is now alive forevermore**. The Father did not die. **Only the Son** can speak these words. So the Son speaks the Father's title as **the One who died for the Father's purposes and was raised to bear His Name forever.**\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7956 \u967 \u969  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u954 \u955 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u8069 \u948 \u959 \u965 ** \'97 *"I have the keys of Death and of Hades."* The Son, by His own death and resurrection, has **been given** (consistent with our pattern) the keys over death and the unseen realm. This is His present authority.\
\
