### A note of careful observation \'97 Revelation 3:14\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u922 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8183  \u7936 \u947 \u947 \u941 \u955 \u8179  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u923 \u945 \u959 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u949 \u943 \u8115  \u7952 \u954 \u954 \u955 \u951 \u963 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u947 \u961 \u940 \u968 \u959 \u957 \'b7 \u932 \u940 \u948 \u949  \u955 \u941 \u947 \u949 \u953  \u8001  \u7944 \u956 \u942 \u957 , \u8001  \u956 \u940 \u961 \u964 \u965 \u962  \u8001  \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u953 \u957 \u972 \u962 , \u7969  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8052  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 \'b7"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And unto the Angel of the Church of the Laodiceans write, These things saith Amen, the faithful and true witness, that beginning of the creatures of God:"*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
**\uc0\u7969  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8052  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"the Beginning of the creation of God."* This title echoes **Proverbs 8:22 LXX** (*"the LORD created/founded me as the beginning of His ways"*) and **Colossians 1:15-18** (*"the firstborn of all creation... the beginning, the firstborn from the dead"*).\
\
**Honest reading per our maxims:**\
- **\uc0\u7936 \u961 \u967 \u942 ** can mean *"beginning,"* *"first principle,"* or *"ruler/origin."*\
- **\uc0\u964 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 ** = *"of the creation of God"* (i.e., of God's creation).\
\
This title applied to the Son is consistent with what we established carefully: the Son is the one **through whom** the Father created all things (1 Cor 8:6; Col 1:16; Heb 1:2; John 1:3), the **firstborn over all creation** (Col 1:15), and so the **\uc0\u7936 \u961 \u967 \u942 ** \'97 the originating principle and ruler \'97 of the Father's creation.\
\
This **also** is consistent with the broader picture of the Son's pre-existence and creative agency that we established by direct witness in our refined study \'97 without requiring the specific identification of Wisdom in Proverbs 8 (which we noted was a parallel, not a witnessed citation).\
\
