### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"...behold, a throne was set in heaven, and one sat upon the throne. And he that sat, was to look upon, like unto a Jasper stone, and a Sardine, and there was a rainbow round about the throne, in sight like to an Emerald... And the four beasts had each one of them six wings about him, and they were full of eyes within, and they ceased not day nor night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, Lord God almighty, Which Was, and Which Is, and Which Is to come... Thou art worthy, O Lord, to receive glory and honor, and power: for thou hast created all things, and for thy will's sake they are, and have been created."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of foundational weight\
\
**(1)** **The throne is the Father's throne.** The One on the throne is identified by the same titles as Rev 1:4, 8: **\uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u8001  \u928 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u961 , \u8001  \u7974 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u8034 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"Lord God Almighty, who was and is and is to come."* **This is the Father.**\
\
**(2)** **The worship of the Father is:** *"Worthy art Thou... for **Thou hast created all things**, and **for Thy will's sake** they are and were created."*\
\
The Father is worshipped as the Creator \'97 *"for Thy will they were created."* This is consistent with Isa 44:24 (*"I stretched out the heavens alone"*) and 1 Cor 8:6 (*"the Father, of whom are all things"*). **The Father's will is the origin and end of creation.**\
\
