### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And I saw in the right hand of him that sat upon the throne, a Book written within, and on the back side, sealed with seven seals. And I saw a strong Angel which preached with a loud voice, Who is worthy to open the Book, and to loose the seals thereof?... And one of the Elders said unto me, Weep not: behold, that Lion which is of the tribe of Judah, that root of David, hath obtained to open the Book, and to loose the seven seals thereof. Then I beheld, and lo, in the midst of the throne, and of the four beasts, and in the midst of the Elders, stood a Lamb as though he had been killed... And he came, and took the Book out of the right hand of him that sat upon the throne."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of decisive importance\
\
**(1)** **The Lamb is distinct from the One on the throne.** The Lamb **comes** and **takes** the scroll **from the right hand of Him who sits on the throne.** Two distinct figures: the Father on the throne, the Lamb approaching to receive the scroll.\
\
This is the **fulfillment of Daniel 7:13-14** \'97 the Son of Man brought before the Ancient of Days to receive dominion. Daniel's vision finds its Apocalyptic counterpart here.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u7952 \u957 \u943 \u954 \u951 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u8001  \u955 \u941 \u969 \u957  \u8001  \u7952 \u954  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u966 \u965 \u955 \u8134 \u962  \u7992 \u959 \u973 \u948 \u945 , \u7969  \u8165 \u943 \u950 \u945  \u916 \u945 \u965 \u943 \u948 ** \'97 *"the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has conquered."* This fulfills **Genesis 49:9-10** (the Lion of Judah, the scepter) and **Isaiah 11:1, 10** (the Root of Jesse / David).\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7944 \u961 \u957 \u943 \u959 \u957  \u7953 \u963 \u964 \u951 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u8033 \u962  \u7952 \u963 \u966 \u945 \u947 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u957 ** \'97 *"a Lamb standing as having been slain."* He stands \'97 He is risen. He bears the marks of His slaughter \'97 eternally. The **slain and risen Lamb** is the eternal form of the exalted Son. This is **the Man Christ Jesus**, the Mediator, the slain and risen Servant.\
\
