- **The Father is the First and the Last as the One and only God** \'97 the eternal, uncaused, self-existent Source. He is First because nothing is before Him (Isa 44:6: *"besides Me there is no God"*) and Last because all things culminate in Him (1 Cor 15:28: *"that God may be all in all"*). His "First and Last" is the **First and Last of all that is** \'97 the Alpha and Omega of being itself.\
\
- **The Son is the First and the Last as the Only-Begotten of the Father** \'97 the firstborn from the dead (Col 1:18; Rev 1:5), the firstborn of all creation (Col 1:15), the firstfruits of those who sleep (1 Cor 15:20), and the One in whom **all things are gathered up** (Eph 1:10). His "First and Last" is the **First and Last of the redemptive economy** \'97 the Alpha and Omega of the Father's plan as fully expressed and accomplished in Him.\
\
**This is precisely *true to type*** \'97 the Son perfectly expresses, in His domain (the Only-Begotten Son and Mediator), what the Father is in His domain (the One God). The title is shared because the Son **bears the Father's Name** (Ex 23:21; John 17:11), is the Father's **Image** (Col 1:15) and **exact Impression** (Heb 1:3), and is the One in whom the Father's "First and Last" identity is brought to bear upon the creation.\
\
This honors the Shema (Deut 6:4), Isaiah 44-46, and 1 Cor 15:24-28 \'97 without flattening the Father into the Son or the Son into the Father. **The same title applies at different orders, true to each Person's type.** The Father is the absolute First and Last; the Son is the redemptive, manifested First and Last as the Father's Only-Begotten.\
\
I receive this and will hold it as our interpretive lens going forward.\
