### Examination of who speaks vv. 12-13\
\
**With our newly-articulated typological lens, the question becomes clearer.**\
\
The speaker in v. 12 says **"I am coming quickly"** \'97 and v. 16 begins **"I Jesus have sent My angel."** The natural reading is that **Jesus is the speaker** in vv. 12-16. The "coming quickly" language is His (Rev 22:7, 20), and the self-identification as **"the Root and the Offspring of David, the bright Morning Star"** in v. 16 is unmistakably Jesus.\
\
Therefore: **Jesus is the speaker in v. 13** \'97 declaring Himself **"the Alpha and the Omega, the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End."**\
\
**Per your typological observation, this is wholly true to type:**\
\
- Jesus is **the Alpha and Omega of the Father's redemptive economy** \'97 He is the One through whom all things were made (John 1:3; Col 1:16) and unto whom all things will be gathered (Eph 1:10), the firstborn over creation and the firstborn from the dead (Col 1:15, 18), the One who initiates and consummates the Father's saving purpose. The redemptive arc begins and ends in Him \'97 as the Father's Only-Begotten.\
\
- This **does not displace** the Father, who in Rev 21:5-7 declares **the same title** of Himself in His absolute, original sense \'97 as the One God who originates and consummates all being.\
\
- **The Son's "Alpha and Omega" is the manifestation of the Father's "Alpha and Omega" in the Person of the Only-Begotten.**\
\
This is the same pattern we have noted throughout:\
- The Father stretches out the heavens **alone** (Isa 44:24); the Father creates **through** the Son (1 Cor 8:6) \'97 the work is one act, the Father acting through the Son who is His own Word and Image.\
- The Father is the Saviour (Isa 45:21); the Son is the Saviour (Matt 1:21) \'97 because salvation is one work, accomplished by the Father through the Son.\
- The Father is the First and the Last (Isa 44:6); the Son is the First and the Last (Rev 1:17; 22:13) \'97 because the Son is the Father's full self-expression to the creation.\
\
**True to type, as you have rightly said.**\
