## **What Is Decisively Established by the Apocalypse**\
\
### **(1) The Father remains the One God on the throne throughout.**\
\
- The throne is His (Rev 4-5; 7; 21; 22).\
- He is **\uc0\u8001  \u928 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u969 \u961 ** \'97 the Almighty \'97 throughout (Rev 1:8; 4:8; 11:17; 15:3; 16:7; 19:6; 21:22).\
- He is **\uc0\u8001  \u8034 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7974 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u7952 \u961 \u967 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 the eternally being One (Rev 1:4, 8; 4:8).\
- He is worshipped as the Creator (Rev 4:11).\
- He gives the revelation to His Son (Rev 1:1).\
\
### **(2) The Son shares the Father's titles "true to type" \'97 as the Only-Begotten.**\
\
Per your beautifully articulated principle: **the Father is First and Last as the One God; the Son is First and Last as the Only-Begotten.** Each title applied to the Son in the Apocalypse reflects His role as **the manifestation, image, and full self-expression of the Father to and within the creation** \'97 never as a rival, never as a second God, never displacing the Father's unique supremacy.\
\
### **(3) The Lamb retains His humanity forever \'97 as the slain and risen Man Christ Jesus.**\
\
He is **the Lamb as having been slain** (Rev 5:6) \'97 eternally. He is **like a Son of Man** in His glorified appearance (Rev 1:13). He is **the Man Christ Jesus** as the one Mediator (1 Tim 2:5). The redeemed are forever in the presence of the slain and risen Lamb, who bears the marks of His suffering and through whom the Father is known.\
\
### **(4) The consummation is the joint reign of God and the Lamb \'97 the Father supreme, the Son at His right hand \'97 true to the eternal order Paul articulated in 1 Cor 15:28.**\
\
The throne is one. The worship is one. The Name is one. The Light is one \'97 the Father's glory shining through the Lamb to illuminate the eternal city. This is the consummation we examined in (C), now visualized in the Apocalypse: **God all in all, through His Beloved Son, with the redeemed gathered into the Father's presence through the Lamb's mediation.**\
\
### **(5) The Apocalypse gathers every prophetic thread from Genesis to the consummation.**\
\
From **Gen 3:15** (the seed of the woman who crushes the serpent \'97 fulfilled in Rev 12 and 20) to **Gen 22** (the beloved Son as Lamb \'97 fulfilled in the slain Lamb of Rev 5) to **Gen 49:10** (the Lion of Judah \'97 Rev 5:5) to **Num 24:17** (the Star \'97 Rev 22:16) to **Ps 2 and 110** (the Anointed at the right hand \'97 Rev 1, 5, 22) to **Dan 7** (the Son of Man before the Ancient of Days \'97 Rev 1, 5) to **Isa 53** (the slain Lamb \'97 Rev 5, 13) to **Zech 12:10** (the pierced One \'97 Rev 1:7) to **Mal 4:2** (the Sun of Righteousness \'97 Rev 22:16 the Morning Star) \'97 **every thread is gathered.**\
\
The Apocalypse is the **canonical consummation** of all prophecy concerning the Person of Christ.\
