## **WHAT WE CAN HONESTLY SAY (PER OUR MAXIMS)**\
\
Now let us be careful and honest about what is established and what is not.\
\
---\
\
### **Established by Cross-Witness (Two or More Honest Parallels):**\
\
**1. The "seven Spirits" are directly tied to the imagery of Zechariah 4** \'97 the seven lamps and the seven eyes of the LORD that range through all the earth.\
\
**2. The "seven Spirits" are directly tied to the Spirit of the LORD on the Messiah in Isaiah 11:2 LXX** \'97 which lists seven aspects/operations of the one Spirit of the Father.\
\
**3. The "seven Spirits" belong to the Father** (Rev 3:1; 4:5; 5:6 \'97 *"of God"*) \'97 they are His.\
\
**4. The "seven Spirits" are now held by the Son** (Rev 3:1) and represented as His **eyes** (Rev 5:6) \'97 meaning the Father's omniscient Spirit-vision is now exercised through the exalted Son.\
\
**5. The number "seven" in Apocalyptic usage is the number of completeness / fullness** \'97 seven churches (representing the whole Church), seven seals (representing the complete unfolding of judgment), seven trumpets (the complete proclamation), seven bowls (the complete outpouring of wrath), etc. Per this consistent symbolic usage, **"seven Spirits" most naturally signifies the *fullness* or *completeness* of God's Spirit** \'97 His Spirit in its perfect, complete operation.\
\
---\
\
### **The Most Honest Reading That Honors the Whole Counsel**\
\
**The "seven Spirits before the throne" are the Father's own Spirit in its sevenfold fullness \'97 the complete, perfect operation of the One Spirit of God \'97 now held and sent forth by the Lamb into all the earth.**\
\
This reading:\
- Honors the Shema (one God, the Father \'97 Deut 6:4) \'97 the Spirit is *His Spirit*, not seven separate Spirits.\
- Honors Isaiah 11:2 LXX \'97 seven aspects of the one Spirit of the LORD.\
- Honors Zechariah 4:6, 10 \'97 the LORD's Spirit and the LORD's seven eyes through the earth.\
- Honors the consistent Apocalyptic symbolism of "seven" as fullness/completeness.\
- Honors what we established in Part E \'97 the Father's Spirit is His omnipresent essential being.\
- Honors the Son's role \'97 the Lamb has the Spirit and pours it out (Acts 2:33; John 7:39; Rev 5:6).\
\
---\
\
### **What We Should NOT Say (Overreaching)**\
\
**1. We should not say** the seven Spirits are **seven distinct persons** of a sevenfold Spirit-Godhead. There is no Scriptural warrant for this. The text gives us *seven* as a symbol of fullness, not as a literal count of distinct personal entities.\
\
**2. We should not say** the seven Spirits are **the "Holy Spirit" of post-Nicene Trinitarian theology** \'97 that is, the supposed "Third Person of the Trinity, co-equal with the Father and the Son." Per maxim #3, we have set aside that formulation. Scripture itself uses *"Spirit of God,"* *"Spirit of the LORD,"* *"Holy Spirit,"* etc., to refer to the Father's own essential being and active presence \'97 not a separately-personal Deity.\
\
**3. We should not say** the seven Spirits are **seven angels** or **the seven archangels** of some intertestamental traditions. While some have proposed this (because the text says they are "sent into all the earth"), the cross-references to Isaiah 11 and Zechariah 4 establish them as **the Father's Spirit in His sevenfold operation**, not as created angelic beings.\
\
**4. We should not press the imagery beyond what it warrants.** The text uses *symbolic visual language*: seven lamps, seven eyes, seven horns. These are not to be flattened into mechanical literal descriptions. They are John's visionary representations of spiritual realities.\
\
---\
\
## **THE THEOLOGICAL COHERENCE**\
\
When we put this together with everything we have established in Part E, here is what we have:\
\
1. **The Father is Eternal Spirit** (John 4:24) \'97 invisible, omnipresent, uncontainable.\
\
2. **The Father's Spirit is His own essential being and active presence** throughout creation \'97 His omnipresent, all-seeing, all-knowing Presence.\
\
3. **The "seven Spirits of God"** in the Apocalypse are the symbolic representation of this Spirit in His **complete fullness** (per Isa 11:2 LXX) and **omnipresent operation through all the earth** (per Zech 4:10).\
\
4. **The seven Spirits are "before the throne"** \'97 i.e., they are the Father's own Spirit in His full operation, proceeding from His presence.\
\
5. **The Son has the seven Spirits** (Rev 3:1) and they are His **eyes** (Rev 5:6) \'97 meaning the exalted Son now holds and exercises the Father's omniscient Spirit-vision, having received the Father's Spirit at His exaltation (Acts 2:33) and now pouring it forth.\
\
6. **They are "sent into all the earth"** \'97 the Father's Spirit, through the Son, goes forth into all the creation to accomplish His purposes.\
\
---\
\
### **The Beautiful Picture**\
\
What emerges, when we read with the lens you have given us, is breathtaking:\
\
- **The Father (Spirit)** fills heaven and earth, but His throne is in heaven.\
- **The Lamb (the Man Christ Jesus)** sits at the right hand of the throne in glorified humanity.\
- **The Father's Spirit, in His sevenfold fullness**, proceeds from the throne \'97 symbolized as **seven lamps of fire** before the throne (the Father's Spirit-presence radiating outward) and as **the seven eyes of the Lamb** (the Father's Spirit now operating through the exalted Son).\
- **The Spirit is sent into all the earth** \'97 to convict, to seal, to indwell the redeemed, to accomplish the Father's saving purposes through the Son.\
\
**This is one God, the Father, acting through His Beloved Only-Begotten Son, by His own Spirit** \'97 the consistent pattern from Genesis to Revelation, now fully revealed at the climax of all prophecy.\
