# **JOHN 14:16-23 \'97 THE FATHER AND SON MAKING THEIR ABODE WITH US**\
\
## **The Context**\
\
Jesus is in the Upper Room, hours before His arrest. He has just told the disciples He is going to prepare a place for them (14:1-6) and that He is the Way, the Truth, and the Life. He has told Philip that *"He that hath seen Me hath seen the Father"* (14:9 \'97 which we already examined under Part E). He has promised that those who believe in Him will do greater works because He goes to the Father (14:12). And He has invited them to ask anything in His Name (14:13-14).\
\
Now He turns to the deepest disclosure: **what will happen after He is glorified \'97 how the Father and the Son will come to dwell in His disciples.**\
\
---\
\
## **JOHN 14:16-17 \'97 THE OTHER PARACLETE**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u969  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u941 \u961 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7940 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u961 \u940 \u954 \u955 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u948 \u974 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u956 \u949 \u952 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8086  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 , \u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u962 , \u8003  \u8001  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u959 \u8016  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u955 \u945 \u946 \u949 \u8150 \u957 , \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u959 \u8016  \u952 \u949 \u969 \u961 \u949 \u8150  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056  \u959 \u8016 \u948 \u8050  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u953 \'b7 \u8017 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 , \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u956 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And I will pray the Father, and he shall give you another Comforter, that he may abide with you forever, Even the Spirit of truth, whom the world cannot receive, because it seeth him not, neither knoweth him: but ye know him: for he dwelleth with you, and shall be in you."*\
\
---\
\
### Clause-by-clause examination\
\
**(1) \uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u969  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u941 \u961 \u945 ** \'97 *"And I will ask the Father."*\
\
**The pattern is preserved.** The Son **asks**; the Father **gives**. Even at the climax of His ministry, the Son does not give the Spirit unilaterally \'97 He **asks** the Father, and the Father **sends**. This is consistent with everything we have established:\
\
- The Father is the **Source** (1 Cor 8:6).\
- The Son is the **One who asks and receives** (Ps 2:8; John 11:42).\
- The Father **gives** in response to the Son's asking.\
\
This is also consistent with Acts 2:33 \'97 *"having received from the Father the promise of the Holy Spirit, He poured forth..."* The Father gives; the Son receives; the Son dispenses. **The chain is unbroken from the Father, through the Son, to the believer.**\
\
---\
\
**(2) \uc0\u7940 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u961 \u940 \u954 \u955 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u948 \u974 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 ** \'97 *"He will give you another Paraclete."*\
\
**\uc0\u928 \u945 \u961 \u940 \u954 \u955 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u962 ** is a rich term. Its root is **\u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u941 \u969 ** \'97 *"to call alongside,"* *"to summon to one's aid,"* *"to comfort,"* *"to encourage,"* *"to advocate for."* The **Paraclete** is therefore:\
- One called alongside to help.\
- A comforter.\
- An advocate.\
- A counselor.\
\
The Geneva translates *"Comforter"* \'97 capturing the consoling, strengthening dimension.\
\
**\uc0\u7940 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u957 ** \'97 *"another"* \'97 is critical. In Greek, **\u7940 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u962 ** typically means *"another of the same kind"* (as distinct from **\u7957 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u962 **, *"another of a different kind"*). Jesus is saying: **another Paraclete of the same kind as I am.** This implies that **Jesus Himself has been functioning as a Paraclete to the disciples** during His earthly ministry. He has been their Comforter, Advocate, Counselor. And now, when He goes, **another of the same kind** will come.\
\
This is profoundly important for our study. The Paraclete who comes is not a totally different reality from Jesus' own presence \'97 He is **of the same character, same purpose, same indwelling presence.** This is why John can later say that Christ is *in* the believer (Gal 2:20; Col 1:27) \'97 because the Spirit who comes is the Spirit of the Father, which is also identified as the Spirit of the Son (Rom 8:9-10; Gal 4:6).\
\
---\
\
**(3) \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u956 \u949 \u952 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8086  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 ** \'97 *"that He may be with you forever."*\
\
We already examined this in the previous discussion \'97 **forever.** Not for a season, not for a task, not until the next sin \'97 but **forever**, **\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u945 **. This is the radical permanence of the New Covenant indwelling. The OT pattern of temporary visitation has given way to the eternal abiding presence.\
\
---\
\
**(4) \uc0\u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u962 ** \'97 *"the Spirit of Truth."*\
\
This is the Paraclete's title. Why **"of Truth"**?\
\
- Because **the Father is Truth** in His essential being.\
- Because **the Son is Truth** \'97 *"I am the Way, the Truth, and the Life"* (John 14:6).\
- Because the Spirit **reveals truth** \'97 *"He will guide you into all truth"* (John 16:13).\
- Because the Spirit **opposes the spirit of error** (1 John 4:6).\
\
The Spirit of Truth is the Father's own essential Spirit, who knows the Father perfectly (1 Cor 2:10-11) and reveals what is true.\
\
---\
\
**(5) \uc0\u8003  \u8001  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u959 \u8016  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u955 \u945 \u946 \u949 \u8150 \u957 ** \'97 *"whom the world cannot receive."*\
\
This is a crucial point. **The world cannot receive the Spirit.** Why?\
\
- The world does not believe in the Son (John 16:9).\
- The world has no organ to perceive the things of the Spirit (1 Cor 2:14).\
- The Spirit is given only to those who are joined to the Son by faith.\
\
This shows that the indwelling Spirit is **not a universal gift** to all humanity \'97 it is the **specific possession of the elect** who believe in the Son. The Spirit's indwelling is bound up with union with Christ.\
\
---\
\
**(6) \uc0\u8005 \u964 \u953  \u959 \u8016  \u952 \u949 \u969 \u961 \u949 \u8150  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056  \u959 \u8016 \u948 \u8050  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u953 ** \'97 *"because it neither sees Him nor knows Him."*\
\
The world cannot see Him (because the Spirit is invisible \'97 as Spirit, per Part E) and cannot know Him (because spiritual knowing requires spiritual indwelling).\
\
---\
\
**(7) \uc0\u8017 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 , \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u956 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953 ** \'97 *"You know Him, for He dwells with you, and shall be in you."*\
\
**This is the pivot of the entire discourse.** Jesus distinguishes precisely:\
\
- **\uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u956 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u953 ** \'97 present tense \'97 *"He **dwells with** you."* Right now, in this moment, the Spirit is **with** them \'97 because He is in Jesus, who is with them. The Father's Spirit indwells the Son fully (John 14:10; Acts 10:38), and the Son is present with the disciples \'97 so the Spirit is *with* them through Jesus' presence.\
\
- **\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953 ** \'97 future tense \'97 *"He shall be **in** you."* After Jesus' glorification and the giving of the Spirit, **He will be in them** \'97 internally indwelling.\
\
**This is Jesus' own announcement of the shift you identified.** From OT-style "with/upon" to NT-style "within" \'97 and it happens at His glorification. The Spirit's location changes from "in the Son who is with us" to "in us, because the Son has given us His own Spirit through the Father."\
\
---\
\
## **JOHN 14:18 \'97 I WILL COME TO YOU**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u927 \u8016 \u954  \u7936 \u966 \u942 \u963 \u969  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u8000 \u961 \u966 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u973 \u962 \'b7 \u7956 \u961 \u967 \u959 \u956 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"I will not leave you fatherless: but I will come unto you."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation of decisive importance\
\
Jesus says: **\uc0\u7956 \u961 \u967 \u959 \u956 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962 ** \'97 *"**I** am coming to you."*\
\
But wait \'97 He has just said the *Paraclete* will come. Now He says **He Himself** will come. Are these two comings, or one?\
\
**The answer establishes a foundational truth:** **They are one coming.** When the Spirit comes, **Jesus Himself comes.** The Spirit's coming is Jesus' coming \'97 because the Spirit He sends is His own Spirit (the Father's Spirit, which fully indwelt Him and which He now pours forth).\
\
This is the basis for:\
- **2 Corinthians 3:17** \'97 *"Now the Lord is that Spirit, and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty."*\
- **Romans 8:9-10** \'97 *"Spirit of God"* and *"Spirit of Christ"* and *"Christ in you"* used interchangeably.\
- **Galatians 2:20** \'97 *"Christ liveth in me."*\
- **Colossians 1:27** \'97 *"Christ in you, the hope of glory."*\
\
**When the Spirit indwells, Christ indwells. When Christ indwells, the Father indwells (because the Father is in Christ). The mutual indwelling of the Father and Son is now extended to the believer through the Spirit.**\
\
---\
\
### A Note on *"Fatherless / Orphans"*\
\
**\uc0\u8000 \u961 \u966 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u973 \u962 ** \'97 *"orphans, fatherless."* Jesus' departure would normally leave the disciples bereft, like orphans without a parent. But He promises: **He will not leave them so.** He will come back to them \'97 through the Spirit who unites them to Himself and to the Father.\
\
