Let me unfold this with care:\
\
**\uc0\u7952 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u963 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945 ** \'97 *"We will come"* \'97 **first person plural future.** Not "I will come" but **"We will come."** Who is "We"? The verse identifies: **the Father and the Son.** Both come.\
\
**\uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u8052 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u951 \u963 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945 ** \'97 *"We will make Our abode with him."*\
\
The word **\uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u942 ** is critically important. It is the same word Jesus used in John 14:2 \'97 *"In My Father's house are many mansions [\u956 \u959 \u957 \u945 \u943 ]."* The word means **dwelling place, abode, residence.**\
\
So Jesus has earlier said: **"In My Father's house are many dwelling places, and I go to prepare a place [a \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u942 ] for you."** Now He says: **"We will come and make Our \u956 \u959 \u957 \u942  with you."**\
\
**This is breathtaking.** The disciples thought they were going to a \uc0\u956 \u959 \u957 \u942  in the Father's house. Jesus reveals that **the Father and the Son will come and make Their \u956 \u959 \u957 \u942  in them.** The order is inverted \'97 or rather, fulfilled in a way they did not expect.\
\
**Both are true:**\
- **There are dwelling places prepared for us in the Father's house** (John 14:2) \'97 the eschatological hope of dwelling with the Father.\
- **The Father and Son make Their dwelling in us NOW** through the indwelling Spirit (John 14:23).\
\
**The believer is both:**\
- **A destined dweller in the Father's house** (future eschatological reality).\
- **A present dwelling place of the Father and Son** (current indwelling reality).\
\
The eternal dwelling-together has begun \'97 already, here, in the believer's heart.\
\
---\
\
### **The "We" of John 14:23 \'97 A Critical Theological Point**\
\
Notice that John 14:23 does **not** say *"the Spirit will come and dwell."* It says **"WE will come."** The "We" is the **Father and the Son.**\
\
This is profoundly important because it shows us what the indwelling Spirit actually is:\
\
- The indwelling Spirit is **the means by which the Father and Son come to dwell in the believer.**\
- The Spirit is not a separate dwelling-presence apart from the Father and the Son \'97 He **is the dwelling-presence of the Father (who is Spirit) in and through the Son.**\
- When the Spirit comes to dwell, **the Father comes** (because the Spirit is His own essential being and presence) and **the Son comes** (because the Son is in the Father, and the Spirit is also called the Spirit of the Son \'97 Rom 8:9; Gal 4:6).\
\
**The Spirit's indwelling = the Father and Son making Their abode.**\
\
This is why Paul can interchange "Spirit of God in you," "Christ in you," and "Christ liveth in me" \'97 they all describe the same reality from different angles. **The Father (Spirit) and the Son are one indwelling Presence in the believer, mediated by the Spirit Christ has poured out.**\
\
---\
\
### **The Beautiful Coherence \'97 Putting It Together**\
\
Let me draw the threads together:\
\
1. **John 14:10** \'97 *"the Father that dwells in Me, He doeth the works."* The Father (Spirit) dwells in the Son.\
\
2. **John 14:11** \'97 *"I am in the Father, and the Father in Me."* Mutual indwelling \'97 eternal.\
\
3. **John 14:16-17** \'97 The Father will give another Paraclete, who is **with** the disciples now (because He is in Jesus) and **in** them later (after Jesus is glorified).\
\
4. **John 14:18** \'97 *"I will come to you."* When the Spirit comes, Jesus comes.\
\
5. **John 14:20** \'97 *"I am in My Father, and you in Me, and I in you."* The believer is brought into the Father-Son mutual indwelling.\
\
6. **John 14:23** \'97 *"We will come and make Our abode with him."* The Father and Son both come \'97 through the Spirit \'97 and make Their dwelling in the believer.\
\
**The arc is complete:** The Father (Spirit) who dwelt fully in the Son now, through the glorified Son's poured-out Spirit, comes to dwell in the believer \'97 bringing the Son with Him, so that **the eternal Father-Son mutual indwelling becomes the believer's indwelling reality**.\
\
The believer becomes **the habitation of God in Christ.**\
\
