## **CONNECTING TO YOUR EARLIER INSIGHTS**\
\
What you have noted about the OT-NT shift now finds its fullest expression:\
\
### **In the OT:**\
\
- The Spirit came **upon** chosen ones for tasks.\
- The Father dwelt in the **Tabernacle / Temple** as His symbolic earthly residence.\
- The Father's full indwelling of human persons was not yet possible (because the Son was not yet glorified \'97 John 7:39).\
- The pattern was: **God *with* His people, in a holy place, mediated through priests and sacrifices.**\
\
### **In the NT (Post-Pentecost):**\
\
- The Spirit dwells **in** the elect, permanently sealed unto the day of redemption.\
- **The believer himself is now the temple** (1 Cor 3:16-17; 6:19; Eph 2:21-22; 2 Cor 6:16).\
- **The Father and the Son make Their abode in the believer** (John 14:23).\
- The pattern is: **God *in* His people, in living temples, mediated through the one Mediator Jesus Christ.**\
\
This shift is the very **inauguration of the New Covenant indwelling** \'97 what Ezekiel 36:27 and Jeremiah 31:33 had promised.\
\
---\
\
## **THE SINGULAR THRONE \'97 REVISITED**\
\
You earlier noted that the singular throne of God and the Lamb in the Apocalypse is no oddity because the Father is Eternal Spirit. The same insight applies here:\
\
- The Father (Spirit) and the Son (the Man Christ Jesus) are **one in essence and operation** without spatial conflict.\
- They can **jointly** indwell the believer because Spirit and Image are not in spatial competition.\
- The Father's Spirit-Nature pervades the believer; the Son's living presence (mediated by the Spirit) fills the believer; **and there is no contradiction** \'97 because Spirit is uncontainable and pervasive.\
\
**The believer becomes a microcosm of the eternal throne-room reality:** the Father (Spirit) and the Son (Man) jointly dwelling, jointly reigning, jointly indwelling \'97 now in the believer's heart, and ultimately in the New Jerusalem.\
\
---\
\
## **A FINAL OBSERVATION \'97 WHY THIS IS THE CONSUMMATION OF THE FATHER'S PURPOSE**\
\
The Father's eternal purpose has been from the beginning **to dwell with His people.** This purpose runs through all of Scripture:\
\
- **Eden** \'97 God walking with man in the cool of the day (Gen 3:8).\
- **The Tabernacle** \'97 *"Let them make Me a sanctuary, that I may dwell among them"* (Ex 25:8).\
- **The Temple** \'97 Solomon's dedication, the cloud of glory (1 Kgs 8:10-11).\
- **The Son** \'97 *"the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us"* (John 1:14, **\uc0\u7952 \u963 \u954 \u942 \u957 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *tabernacled*).\
- **The Spirit at Pentecost** \'97 the Father and Son now coming to make Their abode in the believer.\
- **The New Jerusalem** \'97 *"Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men, and He will dwell with them"* (Rev 21:3).\
\
**John 14:23 is a key middle stage** \'97 the inauguration of the indwelling reality that will be consummated in the New Jerusalem. It is the **already** of what will become the **not yet** fully consummated in Revelation 21-22.\
\
The Father has always wanted to **dwell with His people**. The Son's whole work \'97 His coming, His suffering, His glorification, His pouring out of the Spirit \'97 is unto this end: **that the Father may dwell with and in His people forever**, in His Beloved Son.\
\
