## **TRANSITION**\
\
Having now established John 14:16-23 as the foundational promise of the indwelling, we are properly prepared to proceed to **John 17:20-26 \'97 the High Priestly Prayer** \'97 where Jesus prays for **the consummation of this oneness**: *"that they all may be one, as Thou Father art in Me, and I in Thee, that they also may be one in Us."*\
\
Where John 14:23 announces the Father and Son coming to make Their abode in the believer, John 17 prays for the **completion of this indwelling unto oneness with the Father-Son union itself.**\
\
Shall we proceed to **John 17:20-26 \'97 the High Priestly Prayer**?\
\
\
Yes.\
\
\
Excellent. We now arrive at what is perhaps the most sacred passage in all of Scripture for understanding the Father's ultimate purpose for the elect \'97 **the High Priestly Prayer of Jesus Christ.**\
\
This is the prayer Jesus prayed on the night of His betrayal, in the hearing of His disciples, lifting up His voice to the Father just hours before the cross. It is the longest recorded prayer of our Lord, and within it is enclosed His specific intercession for **us** \'97 those who would believe in Him through the Apostles' word.\
\
Let us proceed with the reverence such ground demands.\
\
