# **JOHN 17 \'97 THE CONTEXT**\
\
The chapter divides naturally:\
\
- **Vv. 1-5** \'97 Jesus prays for Himself (His own glorification).\
- **Vv. 6-19** \'97 Jesus prays for the Eleven (His immediate disciples).\
- **Vv. 20-26** \'97 Jesus prays for **all who would believe through their word** \'97 that is, **us.**\
\
Our focus is the final section \'97 but to understand it rightly, we must briefly note the trajectory established in vv. 1-19.\
\
---\
\
## **Key Foundational Verses Before Our Focus Passage**\
\
### **John 17:1-5** \'97 Jesus' opening:\
\
*"\uc0\u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961 , \u7952 \u955 \u942 \u955 \u965 \u952 \u949 \u957  \u7969  \u8037 \u961 \u945 \'b7 \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u972 \u957  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u933 \u7985 \u972 \u957 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8001  \u933 \u7985 \u8056 \u962  \u948 \u959 \u958 \u940 \u963 \u8131  \u963 \u941 ... \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u957 \u8166 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u972 \u957  \u956 \u949  \u963 \u973 , \u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961 , \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8048  \u963 \u949 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u8183  \u964 \u8135  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u8131  \u8087  \u949 \u7990 \u967 \u959 \u957  \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u957  \u949 \u7990 \u957 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u8048  \u963 \u959 \u943 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Father, that hour is come: glorify thy Son, that thy Son also may glorify thee... And now glorify me, thou Father, with thine own self, with the glory which I had with thee before the world was."*\
\
We already established under our pre-existence study that **v. 5 is Jesus' direct testimony to His pre-temporal glory with the Father.** The foundation is set.\
\
---\
\
### **John 17:3** \'97 The Foundational Definition:\
\
*"\uc0\u945 \u8021 \u964 \u951  \u948 \u941  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u7969  \u945 \u7984 \u974 \u957 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u950 \u969 \u942 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u963 \u8050  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u953 \u957 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8003 \u957  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u945 \u962  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And this is life eternal, that they know thee to be the only very God, and whom thou hast sent, Jesus Christ."*\
\
**This anchors everything.** Eternal life is knowing **the Father (the only true God)** and **the Son (whom He has sent)**. The Father remains supreme; the Son is the Sent One. **This is the same monotheistic framework we have held throughout.** Any reading of John 17:20-26 must preserve this foundation.\
\
---\
\
### **John 17:11** \'97 The Father's Name Given to the Son:\
\
*"...\uc0\u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961  \u7941 \u947 \u953 \u949 , \u964 \u942 \u961 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u8000 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u943  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u8103  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u953 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u7955 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"...Holy Father, keep them in thy Name, even them whom thou hast given me, that they may be one, as we are."*\
\
This is the first introduction of **"one as We are"** language. The Father's Name has been **given** (\uc0\u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962 ) to the Son \'97 and the disciples are to be kept in that Name. The oneness of the Father and the Son is the **prototype** for the oneness Jesus desires for His people.\
\
We must hold this verse carefully \'97 Jesus does **not** ask that the disciples be "one *with* Us" here (that comes in v. 21). He asks that they be "one **as** We are." The model is given; the application will be unfolded shortly.\
\
