# **JOHN 17:20-26 \'97 THE PRAYER FOR THE ELECT**\
\
---\
\
## **JOHN 17:20 \'97 The Scope Widens to Include Us**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u927 \u8016  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u948 \u8050  \u7952 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u8182  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u965 \u972 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u955 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u965  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7952 \u956 \u941 ,"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"I pray not for these alone, but for them also which shall believe in me, through their word,"*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of supreme weight\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u927 \u8016  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u948 \u8050  \u7952 \u961 \u969 \u964 \u8182  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957 ** \'97 *"I do not ask concerning these only."* Jesus' prayer now widens beyond the eleven physically present with Him.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u964 \u8182 \u957  \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u965 \u972 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u955 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u965  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7952 \u956 \u941 ** \'97 *"of those who believe in Me through their word."*\
\
**This is us.** Every believer from Pentecost forward who has come to faith **through the apostolic word** \'97 that is, the Gospel as proclaimed by the Apostles and preserved in their writings (the New Testament) \'97 is included in this prayer. The chain is:\
\
- The Father sends the Son (v. 3).\
- The Son trains and sends the Apostles (vv. 6-19; cf. v. 18).\
- The Apostles proclaim the Word.\
- Believers come to faith through the apostolic word.\
- These believers are who Jesus prays for here.\
\
**Per maxim #1, this prayer is Jesus' own intercession for *every* elect believer through the present age.** This is the prayer of the great High Priest \'97 His ongoing intercession (Heb 7:25; Rom 8:34) \'97 recorded for us so we may know what He prays.\
\
**(3) The present participle \uc0\u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u965 \u972 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957 ** \'97 *"those who are believing"* \'97 is significant. The believing is not a one-time historical event but the continuing posture of those who have received the Apostles' testimony.\
\
