## **JOHN 17:22 \'97 THE GLORY GIVEN**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u7971 \u957  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u953  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u7955 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u7957 \u957  \u7952 \u963 \u956 \u949 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And the glory that thou gavest me, I have given them, that they may be one, as we are one,"*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of foundational importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u964 \u8052 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u7971 \u957  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u953  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 ** \'97 *"the glory which Thou hast given Me, I have given them."*\
\
**Trace the chain:**\
- The Father **gave** glory to the Son (\uc0\u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \'97 perfect tense \'97 completed past with continuing effect).\
- The Son **gave** that same glory to the believers (\uc0\u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u945  \'97 perfect tense \'97 completed past with continuing effect).\
\
**Both verbs are in the perfect tense** \'97 denoting an action accomplished with abiding result. The glory has been **given**, and **continues to belong** to the recipients.\
\
**What glory is this?** Not the glory of inherent deity (which the Father has alone), but **the glory the Father gave the Son** \'97 the glory of being the Beloved Son, of being commissioned, of being indwelt by the Father's Spirit, of being the perfect Image of the invisible God. This is the glory **received** by the Son from the Father \'97 and this is the glory the Son passes on to the elect.\
\
**The elect receive glory by participation in the Son's glory.** Not the original, unshared glory of the Father (1 Tim 1:17 \'97 *"glory forever and ever"* \'97 uniquely His); but the **derived, given glory** that the Son received and now shares with His people.\
\
This is consistent with:\
- **Romans 8:17** \'97 *"if so be that we suffer with him, that we may be also glorified together."*\
- **Romans 8:30** \'97 *"whom he justified, them he also glorified."*\
- **2 Corinthians 3:18** \'97 *"we all... beholding... the glory of the Lord, are changed into the same image from glory to glory."*\
- **Colossians 3:4** \'97 *"when Christ, who is our life, shall appear, then shall ye also appear with him in glory."*\
- **2 Thessalonians 2:14** \'97 *"to the obtaining of the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ."*\
\
**The Son's glory becomes the believer's glory** \'97 given, not earned; received, not innate.\
\
---\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u7955 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u7957 \u957  \u7952 \u963 \u956 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"that they may be one, as We are one."*\
\
The purpose of the glory-giving is **oneness like Our oneness.** The glory of the Son (which He received from the Father and shares with us) is the **means** of our oneness. By being filled with the same glory, we become one as the Father and Son are one.\
\
This is the **mechanism** of indwelling and oneness: **shared glory.**\
\
---\
\
## **JOHN 17:23 \'97 THE PERFECTION OF ONENESS**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u963 \u8058  \u7952 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u943 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u964 \u949 \u964 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u969 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7957 \u957 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u8131  \u8001  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u963 \u973  \u956 \u949  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u7952 \u956 \u8050  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"I in them, and thou in me, that they may be made perfect in one, and that the world may know, that thou hast sent me, and hast loved them, as thou hast loved me."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of supreme weight\
\
**(1) The triple indwelling chain:**\
\
- **\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 ** \'97 *"I in them"* \'97 the Son in the believers.\
- **\uc0\u963 \u8058  \u7952 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u943 ** \'97 *"Thou [the Father] in Me"* \'97 the Father in the Son.\
\
**The structure is brilliant:** **Father \uc0\u8594  Son \u8594  Believers.** The Father is in the Son; the Son is in the believers. Therefore the Father is in the believers \'97 but **only through the Son**. The mediation is preserved at every level.\
\
This perfectly aligns with what we established in Part E about the Father (Spirit) indwelling the Son (Image). The same Father (Spirit) who indwells the Son is now extended through the Son to indwell the believers. **The Spirit who comes is the Spirit of the Father, who is also the Spirit of the Son** (Rom 8:9; Gal 4:6) \'97 one and the same indwelling Presence.\
\
---\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u964 \u949 \u964 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u969 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7957 \u957 ** \'97 *"that they may be perfected into one."*\
\
**\uc0\u964 \u949 \u964 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u969 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u953 ** \'97 perfect passive participle of **\u964 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u972 \u969 ** \'97 *"to bring to completion, to perfect, to consummate."*\
\
The oneness is to be **consummated, brought to perfection, made complete.** This is not a one-time event but a process moving toward perfection \'97 fulfilled progressively in this age and consummated in the New Jerusalem.\
\
**\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7957 \u957 ** \'97 *"into one."* Not "as one" but **"into one"** \'97 the believers are brought *into* the oneness of the Father-Son union.\
\
The trajectory is:\
- We were many, separated, lost, dead in sin.\
- We are being brought **into the oneness of God** \'97 by being placed in the Son, who is in the Father.\
- We are being **perfected** in this oneness \'97 moved progressively toward complete consummation.\
\
---\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u7952 \u956 \u8050  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u962 ** \'97 *"Thou hast loved them, as Thou hast loved Me."*\
\
**This is staggering.** The Father loves the believers **with the same love** with which He loves His Son.\
\
**\uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u974 \u962 ** \'97 *"in the same manner as."* The love is of the same kind, the same quality.\
\
How can this be? Because the believers are **in the Son.** The Father's love for the Son extends to all who are in the Son. We are loved **in the Beloved** (Eph 1:6 \'97 *"He hath made us accepted in the beloved"*).\
\
This is the deepest comfort the believer can know: **the Father loves me as He loves His Son** \'97 not because of my worth, but because **I am in Christ**, and the Father's love for Christ is undivided and unwithdrawn.\
\
