## **JOHN 17:24 \'97 THE FINAL DESTINY: SEEING THE SON'S GLORY**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961 , \u8003  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u953 , \u952 \u941 \u955 \u969  \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8005 \u960 \u959 \u965  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u954 \u7936 \u954 \u949 \u8150 \u957 \u959 \u953  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u8125  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8166 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u952 \u949 \u969 \u961 \u8182 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u8052 \u957  \u7971 \u957  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u953 , \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u949  \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u946 \u959 \u955 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u965 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Father, I will that they which thou hast given me, be with me even where I am, that they may behold that my glory which thou hast given me: for thou hast loved me before the foundation of the world."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u8003  \u948 \u941 \u948 \u969 \u954 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u959 \u953 ** \'97 *"those whom Thou hast given Me."* The elect are **the Father's gift to the Son.** They have been given by the Father into the Son's care. This is the consistent NT theme:\
\
- **John 6:37, 39** \'97 *"All that the Father giveth me, shall come to me... that of all which he hath given me, I should lose nothing."*\
- **John 10:28-29** \'97 *"My Father, which gave them me, is greater than all."*\
- **John 17:6, 9, 11** \'97 *"thine they were, and thou gavest them me."*\
\
**The believers belong to the Father first, then are given to the Son.**\
\
---\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u952 \u941 \u955 \u969  \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8005 \u960 \u959 \u965  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u954 \u7936 \u954 \u949 \u8150 \u957 \u959 \u953  \u8038 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u8125  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"I will that they whom Thou hast given Me, be with Me where I am."*\
\
**This is the Son's explicit will / desire** that the elect be **with Him where He is.** Where is He? He has just said in vv. 1-5 that He is going to be glorified at the Father's side with the glory He had before the world was. **He wills that we be with Him there.**\
\
This corresponds with:\
- **John 14:3** \'97 *"I will come again, and receive you unto myself, that where I am, there ye may be also."*\
- **1 Thessalonians 4:17** \'97 *"so shall we ever be with the Lord."*\
- **Colossians 3:1-4** \'97 *"set your affection on things above, where Christ sitteth on the right hand of God... when Christ, who is our life, shall appear, then shall ye also appear with him in glory."*\
\
**The final destiny of the elect is to be with the Son, in the Father's presence, in glory.** Not as gods, but as the beloved children of the Father who have been brought into the eternal Father-Son fellowship.\
\
---\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u952 \u949 \u969 \u961 \u8182 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u8052 \u957 ** \'97 *"that they may behold My glory."*\
\
The believers will **behold** (\uc0\u952 \u949 \u969 \u961 \u8182 \u963 \u953 \u957  \'97 to gaze upon, to contemplate) the Son's glory. This is consistent with:\
\
- **1 John 3:2** \'97 *"when he shall appear, we shall be like him: for we shall see him as he is."*\
- **2 Corinthians 3:18** \'97 beholding the glory and being transformed into the same image.\
- **Revelation 22:4** \'97 *"they shall see his face; and his name shall be in their foreheads."*\
\
**The final beatific vision** \'97 seeing the glorified Son in His full splendor, the glory the Father gave Him from before the world.\
\
---\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u949  \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u946 \u959 \u955 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u965 ** \'97 *"for Thou hast loved Me before the foundation of the world."*\
\
The Son's glory is the expression of the Father's eternal love for Him \'97 a love that pre-dates creation itself. **The Father loved the Son before the world was made**, and the Son's glory is the eternal fruit of that love.\
\
This anchors our pre-existence study under Part E \'97 Jesus' own testimony that the Father loved Him before the foundation of the world.\
\
