## **JOHN 17:25-26 \'97 THE CONCLUSION OF THE PRAYER**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961  \u948 \u943 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u949 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u963 \u949  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u947 \u957 \u969 , \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u948 \u941  \u963 \u949  \u7956 \u947 \u957 \u969 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u959 \u8023 \u964 \u959 \u953  \u7956 \u947 \u957 \u969 \u963 \u945 \u957  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u963 \u973  \u956 \u949  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u945 \u962 \'b7 \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u947 \u957 \u974 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u940  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u947 \u957 \u969 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u969 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u7969  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951  \u7971 \u957  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u8086  \u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"O righteous Father, the world also hath not known thee, but I have known thee, and these have known, that thou hast sent me. And I have declared unto them thy Name, and will declare it, that the love wherewith thou hast loved me, may be in them, and I in them."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of supreme importance \'97 the climax of the prayer\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u928 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u961  \u948 \u943 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u949 ** \'97 *"Righteous Father."* The address. The Father is **righteous** \'97 meaning, what He does and how He distinguishes between the world (which has not known Him) and the disciples (who have known Him through the Son) is **just** and **right.**\
\
**(2) The three-fold distinction:**\
- **"The world has not known Thee."**\
- **"I have known Thee."**\
- **"These have known that Thou hast sent Me."**\
\
The world's failure to know the Father is set against the Son's perfect knowledge of Him and the disciples' knowledge \'97 through the Son \'97 that the Father sent Him. The chain of knowing:\
\
- **The Son knows the Father directly** (because He is the only-begotten in the Father's bosom \'97 John 1:18).\
- **The disciples know that the Father sent the Son** \'97 and through this knowledge, they have access to the Father (because the Son is the Way \'97 John 14:6).\
- **The world does not know either** \'97 having no organ of spiritual perception.\
\
---\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u957 \u974 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u940  \u963 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u947 \u957 \u969 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u969 ** \'97 *"I have declared Thy Name to them, and will declare it."*\
\
**\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u957 \u974 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u945 ** \'97 aorist \'97 *"I have made known"* (the past work of His earthly ministry).\
**\uc0\u947 \u957 \u969 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u969 ** \'97 future \'97 *"I will make known"* (the continuing work after His glorification, through the Spirit).\
\
**The Son's declaration of the Father's Name is both completed and ongoing.** What He has done in His earthly ministry, He continues to do through the indwelling Spirit. The Spirit's work is to keep declaring the Father's Name to the believers' hearts \'97 leading them into ever-deeper knowledge of the Father.\
\
---\
\
**(4) The Final, Climactic Purpose: \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u7969  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951  \u7971 \u957  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u8086  \u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 **\
\
*"that the love wherewith Thou hast loved Me may be in them, and I in them."*\
\
**This is the crowning petition.** Let me unfold it slowly.\
\
**\uc0\u7969  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951  \u7971 \u957  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u940 \u962  \u956 \u949 ** \'97 *"the love with which Thou hast loved Me."* This is the **eternal love of the Father for the Son** \'97 the love we noted in v. 24 that pre-dates creation. The same love.\
\
**\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u8086 ** \'97 *"may be in them."* That this very love \'97 the Father's love for the Son \'97 may **be in** the believers.\
\
**\uc0\u954 \u7936 \u947 \u8060  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962 ** \'97 *"and I in them."* And the Son Himself in them.\
\
**Together:** **The Father's eternal love for the Son, AND the Son Himself, in the believers.**\
\
Stop and consider what this means. The Father has loved the Son with eternal, undivided, perfect love from before the foundation of the world. **That very love** is now poured into the believer. And the **Son Himself** \'97 the Beloved One \'97 is in the believer.\
\
This is the consummation of indwelling:\
- **The Father's love** \'97 the love that has always been between Father and Son \'97 is now poured into us.\
- **The Son** \'97 the Beloved \'97 is in us.\
- The two \'97 love and Lover \'97 together fill the believer.\
\
And how does this happen? **Through the indwelling Spirit**, which is the Father's own essential being and presence, poured out through the Son (Acts 2:33).\
\
