## **HOW THIS IS POSSIBLE \'97 Romans 5:5**\
\
Paul gives us the mechanism by which this prayer is answered:\
\
### **Greek (Rom 5:5):**\
*"...\uc0\u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7969  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u954 \u954 \u941 \u967 \u965 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u945 \u8150 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u945 \u953 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u7945 \u947 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u948 \u959 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8150 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva (Rom 5:5):**\
*"...because the love of God is shed abroad in our hearts by the holy Ghost, which is given unto us."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
**\uc0\u7969  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u954 \u954 \u941 \u967 \u965 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u945 \u8150 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u945 \u953 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ** \'97 *"the love of God has been shed abroad in our hearts."* The same verb as Acts 2:33 \'97 **\u7952 \u954 \u967 \u941 \u969 ** \'97 *to pour out, to shed abroad.*\
\
**The Father's love is poured into our hearts by the Holy Spirit.** This is the mechanism by which John 17:26's petition is answered. The Father's love for the Son becomes the believer's possession **through the Spirit** that was poured out by the glorified Son.\
\
**The whole circuit is complete:**\
1. The Father loves the Son eternally.\
2. The Father pours forth His own Spirit (His essential being and presence) through the glorified Son (Acts 2:33).\
3. The Spirit indwells the believer, bringing **the Father's love** and **the Son Himself** to dwell within.\
4. The believer is brought *into* the Father-Son union \'97 *"in Us"* (John 17:21).\
5. The believer is being perfected into oneness with the Father and the Son (John 17:23).\
6. The believer's final destiny is to behold the Son's glory and be with Him where He is (John 17:24).\
\
