### Observations of crowning importance\
\
**(1)** Paul prays **to the Father** for the believers.\
\
**(2)** That they be **strengthened by His Spirit** \'97 the Father's Spirit (the same Spirit the Son poured out \'97 Acts 2:33).\
\
**(3)** That **Christ may dwell in their hearts** through faith. The same indwelling Christ promised in John 14:23.\
\
**(4)** That they may **know the love of Christ** that surpasses knowledge \'97 the very love we noted in John 17:26.\
\
**(5)** Climactic petition: **\uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u960 \u955 \u951 \u961 \u969 \u952 \u8134 \u964 \u949  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u960 \u8118 \u957  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u955 \u942 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"that ye may be filled with all the fullness of God."*\
\
**The believer is to be FILLED WITH ALL THE FULLNESS OF GOD.**\
\
What does this mean? The believer is not made God; but the believer is so indwelt by the Father (Spirit), through the Son (in the heart by faith), that the **fullness of God's own life, love, presence, and being** comes to **fill** the believer.\
\
This is the same reality John 17:26 describes \'97 the Father's love and the Son Himself in the believer. **Paul's prayer in Eph 3 is the apostolic equivalent of Jesus' prayer in John 17.**\
