# **GALATIANS 2:20 \'97 THE FOUNDATIONAL DECLARATION**\
\
## **The Context**\
\
Paul has just rebuked Peter at Antioch for compromising the Gospel by drawing back from table fellowship with Gentile believers (Gal 2:11-14). He has declared that justification is by faith in Christ, not by works of the law (vv. 15-16). And then, in vv. 19-20, he gives the most personal and profound statement of the believer's union with Christ in the entire NT.\
\
---\
\
## **Galatians 2:19-20**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u965  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u8179  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u950 \u942 \u963 \u969 . \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u973 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u953 \'b7 \u950 \u8182  \u948 \u8050  \u959 \u8016 \u954 \u941 \u964 \u953  \u7952 \u947 \u974 , \u950 \u8135  \u948 \u8050  \u7952 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8054  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u962 \'b7 \u8003  \u948 \u8050  \u957 \u8166 \u957  \u950 \u8182  \u7952 \u957  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u943 , \u7952 \u957  \u960 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u953  \u950 \u8182  \u964 \u8135  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u933 \u7985 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u972 \u962  \u956 \u949  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u948 \u972 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u8166 ."*\
