## **CLAUSE-BY-CLAUSE EXAMINATION**\
\
Let me unfold this carefully \'97 phrase by phrase \'97 for it contains, in compressed form, the entire doctrine of identification with Christ.\
\
---\
\
### **Clause 1: \uc0\u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u965  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u8179  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u950 \u942 \u963 \u969 **\
\
*"For I through the law died to the law, that I might live unto God."*\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u948 \u953 \u8048  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u965 ** \'97 *"through the law."* The law itself was the means by which Paul died to the law. How?\
- The law condemned him as a sinner (Rom 3:19-20; 7:7-13).\
- The law's curse fell on Christ as our substitute (Gal 3:13).\
- In Christ, the law's demand was met and its condemnation exhausted.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u957 \u972 \u956 \u8179  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u957 ** \'97 *"I died to the law."* Paul's relationship to the law as a means of righteousness was terminated. The law no longer has claim upon him as the basis of his standing before God.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u950 \u942 \u963 \u969 ** \'97 *"that I might live unto God."* The purpose of dying to the law is **to live unto God**. The law's killing function led to a new resurrection life **for God** \'97 a life oriented toward the Father, lived in His presence and for His glory.\
\
---\
\
### **Clause 2: \uc0\u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u973 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u953 **\
\
*"I have been crucified with Christ."*\
\
**This is the foundational declaration of identification.** Let us examine every element.\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183 ** \'97 dative case \'97 *"with Christ"* or *"in Christ."* The dative of association.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u973 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u953 ** \'97 perfect passive of **\u963 \u965 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u965 \u961 \u972 \u969 ** \'97 *"I have been co-crucified."*\
\
The prefix **\uc0\u963 \u973 \u957 -** means *"together with."* The believer is **crucified together with Christ.**\
\
The tense is **perfect** \'97 a completed past action with continuing present effect. **It happened, and its effects remain in force.** Paul did not say *"I am being crucified"* (present) or *"I will be crucified"* (future). He says *"I have been crucified, and remain in that crucified state."*\
\
The voice is **passive** \'97 *"I was crucified"* \'97 i.e., **God did this to me.** The Father, through the Son's cross, included me in the Son's death. I did not crucify myself; the Father united me with the Son's cross.\
\
**(3) What does this mean \'97 that the believer was crucified with Christ?**\
\
It does not mean Paul was historically nailed to Christ's cross. It means **the believer's old life \'97 his identity in Adam, his identity as a sinner, his identity under condemnation \'97 was put to death when Christ died.** The Father reckoned the believer into the Son's death.\
\
This is what theologians have called **federal headship** or **representative union** \'97 but Scripture's own language is **identification**: the believer is **identified with Christ** in His death so completely that what happened to Christ happened to him.\
\
**Cross-witness \'97 Romans 6:6 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u8001  \u960 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u953 \u8056 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u965 \u961 \u974 \u952 \u951 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u961 \u947 \u951 \u952 \u8135  \u964 \u8056  \u963 \u8182 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 , \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u956 \u951 \u954 \u941 \u964 \u953  \u948 \u959 \u965 \u955 \u949 \u973 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115 \'b7"*\
\
**1599 Geneva:** *"Knowing this, that our old man is crucified with him, that the body of sin might be destroyed, that henceforth we should not serve sin."*\
\
The same verb \'97 **\uc0\u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u965 \u961 \u974 \u952 \u951 ** \'97 *"was crucified together with."* Paul's individual testimony in Galatians 2:20 is universalized in Romans 6: **our old man is crucified with Christ.** Two witnesses establish: **every believer was co-crucified with Christ at the cross.**\
\
