*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8004 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u960 \u964 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u950 \u969 \u959 \u960 \u959 \u943 \u951 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \'97 \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u964 \u943  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u949  \u963 \u949 \u963 \u8179 \u963 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u953  \'97 \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u942 \u947 \u949 \u953 \u961 \u949 \u957 ..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Even when we were dead by sins, hath quickened us together in Christ, by whose grace ye are saved, And hath raised us up together..."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
The believer has been **raised with Christ.** This is a present spiritual reality (not merely future bodily resurrection). **Three witnesses (Rom 6, Col 2-3, Eph 2) establish:** by the same power that raised Christ from the dead, the Father has raised us up *with* Christ.\
\
This means:\
- **We have new life now** \'97 the resurrection life of the Son (Rom 6:4).\
- **Our orientation is now upward** \'97 toward where Christ is (Col 3:1).\
- **The Father has co-resurrected us with His Son** (Eph 2:6) \'97 by the same power.\
\
---\
\
## **POINT 5 \'97 SEATED WITH CHRIST AT THE FATHER'S RIGHT HAND**\
\
### **Ephesians 2:6 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u942 \u947 \u949 \u953 \u961 \u949 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u954 \u940 \u952 \u953 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u7952 \u960 \u959 \u965 \u961 \u945 \u957 \u943 \u959 \u953 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 ,"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"...And hath raised us up together, and made us sit together in the heavenly places in Christ Jesus,"*\
\
### **Colossians 3:1, 3** \'97 already cited; the believer's life is hidden with Christ in God, where Christ sits at the right hand.\
\
---\
\
### Observation of remarkable importance\
\
**\uc0\u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u954 \u940 \u952 \u953 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u7952 \u960 \u959 \u965 \u961 \u945 \u957 \u943 \u959 \u953 \u962 ** \'97 *"He has made [us] sit together in the heavenly places."*\
\
The Father has not only raised us with Christ; **He has seated us with Christ in the heavenly places.** Where Christ sits \'97 at the Father's right hand \'97 **we sit with Him.**\
\
This is breathtaking. The very session of the Son at the Father's right hand \'97 which we examined under Part A as the central reality of His present ministry \'97 **includes us by identification.** We are not merely beneficiaries of His enthronement; we are **co-seated with Him.**\
\
This corresponds with:\
- **Revelation 3:21** \'97 *"To him that overcometh will I grant to sit with me in my throne, even as I also overcame, and am set down with my Father in his throne."*\
- **2 Timothy 2:12** \'97 *"if we suffer, we shall also reign with him."*\
- **Romans 8:17** \'97 *"and if children, then heirs; heirs of God, and joint-heirs with Christ; if so be that we suffer with him, that we may be also glorified together."*\
\
**The believer's seat is with the Son, at the Father's right hand.** Not in our own merit, but **in Christ Jesus** (\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \'97 the controlling phrase).\
\
---\
\
## **POINT 6 \'97 IN CHRIST: THE GREAT PAULINE PHRASE**\
\
The phrase **\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183 ** (in Christ) and its variants (\u7952 \u957  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \'97 in the Lord; \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \'97 in Him) appear over 200 times in Paul. It is **the controlling concept** of his theology. Let me survey the major facets.\
\
---\
\
### **In Christ \'97 Chosen Before the Foundation of the World**\
\
### **Ephesians 1:4 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u7952 \u958 \u949 \u955 \u941 \u958 \u945 \u964 \u959  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u960 \u961 \u8056  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u946 \u959 \u955 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u965 , \u949 \u7990 \u957 \u945 \u953  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u7937 \u947 \u943 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u956 \u974 \u956 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u949 \u957 \u974 \u960 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u957  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u8131 ,"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"As he hath chosen us in him, before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy, and without blame before him in love:"*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
**\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 ** \'97 *"in Him"* \'97 **before the foundation of the world.** The Father chose us **in His Son** before creation itself. Our identification with Christ does not begin at our conversion; **it was decided in eternity past in the Father's purpose.**\
\
---\
\
### **In Christ \'97 Accepted in the Beloved**\
\
### **Ephesians 1:6 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7956 \u960 \u945 \u953 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u951 \u962  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7975 \u962  \u7952 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u964 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u7968 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u951 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u8179 ,"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"To the praise of the glory of his grace, wherewith he hath made us accepted in his beloved,"*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
**\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u7968 \u947 \u945 \u960 \u951 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u8179 ** \'97 *"in the Beloved."* The Father has **accepted us in His Beloved Son.** Our acceptance with the Father is **not in ourselves**, but **in the Beloved One**. The Father loves Him; therefore He loves us as we are *in Him*. This corresponds with John 17:23 \'97 *"hast loved them as Thou hast loved Me."*\
\
---\
\
