### **Ephesians 5:30 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u8005 \u964 \u953  \u956 \u941 \u955 \u951  \u7952 \u963 \u956 \u8050 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For we are members of his body, of his flesh, and of his bones."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
The believer is a **member of Christ's body.** Not merely an associate, not merely a follower \'97 but an actual **member** (\uc0\u956 \u941 \u955 \u959 \u962  \'97 a limb, an organ) of His own body. This is a real, organic union \'97 as real as the union between a hand and its body.\
\
**Ephesians 5:30** goes even further: *"members of His body, of His flesh, and of His bones"* \'97 echoing Genesis 2:23 (Adam and Eve). Paul applies the marriage union of Adam and Eve typologically: as Eve was bone of Adam's bones, so we are **of Christ's flesh and bones** \'97 partakers of His very being.\
\
