## **POINT 9 \'97 JOINED TO THE LORD AS ONE SPIRIT**\
\
### **1 Corinthians 6:17 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u8001  \u948 \u8050  \u954 \u959 \u955 \u955 \u974 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u7955 \u957  \u960 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u940  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"But he that is joined unto the Lord, is one spirit."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation of decisive importance\
\
**\uc0\u8001  \u954 \u959 \u955 \u955 \u974 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u7955 \u957  \u960 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u940  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957 ** \'97 *"He who is joined to the Lord is one spirit [with Him]."*\
\
The verb **\uc0\u954 \u959 \u955 \u955 \u940 \u959 \u956 \u945 \u953 ** means *"to be glued together, to cleave to."* It is the verb used in Gen 2:24 LXX of marriage: *"a man shall cleave to his wife, and they shall be one flesh."* Paul transposes the marital language to the spiritual: **the believer is so joined to the Lord that they are one spirit.**\
\
**This is the most intimate union conceivable.** Not merely "in" Christ as in a location; but **one spirit with Him** \'97 sharing the same spiritual life-principle.\
\
This corresponds with everything we have established:\
- The Father indwells the Son (one Spirit).\
- The Son indwells the believer (one Spirit).\
- The believer is joined to the Lord **as one spirit**.\
\
