## **WHAT THIS ESTABLISHES \'97 THE ULTIMATE COHERENCE**\
\
The believer is identified with Christ **in every redemptive act of the Son** \'97 past, present, and future. There is no facet of the Son's saving work in which we do not participate by virtue of being **in Him.**\
\
**This is not metaphor.** Paul does not say *"as if we were crucified with Him."* He says *"I have been crucified with Christ"* \'97 perfect tense, real reality. Not a legal fiction, not a poetic figure, but the **actual reckoning of the Father** that includes us in His Son's history and destiny.\
\
**The mechanism:** The Father, who is Eternal Spirit, chose us in His Beloved Son before the foundation of the world. He so identified us with His Son that what the Son did, we did in Him. The Son's death is our death; His burial is our burial; His resurrection is our resurrection; His ascension is our ascension; His seating is our seating; His glory is our glory; His inheritance is our inheritance.\
\
**Therefore:**\
- We do not need to add to His work. It is complete.\
- We do not need to fear condemnation. We are in Him who is acquitted.\
- We do not need to seek our own righteousness. We have His.\
- We do not need to seek our own glory. We are joint-heirs of His.\
- We do not need to fear death. We have already died with Him.\
- We do not need to fear judgment. We have already been justified in Him.\
\
**We are who He is \'97 not in essence, but in identification by the Father's reckoning and the Spirit's union.**\
\
---\
\
## **GALATIANS 2:20 \'97 REVISITED IN LIGHT OF THE WHOLE**\
\
Now we can hear Paul's testimony with full resonance:\
\
*"I have been crucified with Christ"* \'97 co-crucified, established by Rom 6:6.\
*"It is no longer I who live"* \'97 the old man is dead, new creation is the reality (2 Cor 5:17).\
*"But Christ lives in me"* \'97 the indwelling of the Son, established by John 14:20, 23; Col 1:27.\
*"And the life which I now live in the flesh, I live by faith in the Son of God"* \'97 by present faith we appropriate this identification daily.\
*"Who loved me and gave Himself for me"* \'97 the personal, individual love of the Beloved Son for each elect believer.\
\
**This is not Paul alone. This is every believer.** Every elect saint can say with Paul: *"I have been crucified with Christ; I no longer live; Christ lives in me; I live by faith of the Son of God who loved me and gave Himself for me."*\
\
