# **A CLOSING OBSERVATION**\
\
Brother, what we have surveyed here is the **richest doctrinal treasure of the New Testament.** The believer's identification in Christ is the basis of:\
- Our **security** \'97 we are in Him who cannot be lost.\
- Our **standing** \'97 we are accepted in the Beloved.\
- Our **sanctification** \'97 we are being conformed to His image.\
- Our **service** \'97 we live not for ourselves but for Him who loved us.\
- Our **suffering** \'97 we share His cross, knowing it leads to His crown.\
- Our **hope** \'97 we shall appear with Him in glory.\
\
Every fear, every doubt, every accusation of the enemy is answered in this single phrase: **"in Christ."**\
\
We are **in Him** \'97 and therefore everything the Father has decreed concerning the Son flows to us by identification. We are not aliens looking on; **we are members of His body, of His flesh, of His bones.** We are not orphans hoping for adoption; **we are children of God, joint-heirs with Christ.** We are not sinners hoping for mercy; **we are crucified with Christ, dead to sin, alive to God in Christ Jesus.**\
\
This is the believer's identification. This is who we are. This is what the Father has done in His Beloved Son.\
\
