\
### Observations of foundational importance\
\
**(1) The world's hatred is a settled disposition.** Jesus presents it as a constant \'97 the world has hated Him, and will hate those who are His.\
\
**(2) The reason: \uc0\u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7952 \u954  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u972 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u965  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u941 ** \'97 *"because you are not of the world."* The believer's separation from the world is the cause of the world's hostility. Identification with Christ removes us from the world's love.\
\
**(3) The principle: \uc0\u927 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u948 \u959 \u8166 \u955 \u959 \u962  \u956 \u949 \u943 \u950 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"The servant is not greater than his master."* What He endured, His servants will endure. This is a settled pattern of the Christian life, not an aberration.\
\
