\
### **2 Timothy 3:12 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u959 \u7985  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u949 \u8016 \u963 \u949 \u946 \u8182 \u962  \u950 \u8134 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u948 \u953 \u969 \u967 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Yea, and all that will live godly in Christ Jesus, shall suffer persecution."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation of decisive importance\
\
**\uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u959 \u7985  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u949 \u8016 \u963 \u949 \u946 \u8182 \u962  \u950 \u8134 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u948 \u953 \u969 \u967 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953 ** \'97 *"All who desire to live godly in Christ Jesus shall be persecuted."*\
\
**\uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962 ** \'97 *"all."* No exception. **\u948 \u953 \u969 \u967 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953 ** \'97 future passive \'97 *"will be persecuted."* A settled, prophetic certainty.\
\
This is a sobering text. Paul, writing to Timothy near the end of his own life, declares it as a universal principle: **godly living in Christ Jesus brings persecution.** The form may vary; the reality is constant.\
\
