### Observations\
\
**(1)** Bearing the Name itself can be a cause of suffering. The world's quarrel is ultimately not with the believer personally but **with the Name and the One whose Name it is** (because they do not know the Father \'97 John 15:21).\
\
**(2)** The apostles' response to this suffering is **rejoicing** \'97 counted worthy to bear shame for the Name. This is not a stoic endurance but a joyful identification: *"if this is what comes from being identified with Him, blessed are we."*\
\
**(3) 1 Peter 4 carefully distinguishes the suffering that pleases God** (suffering as a Christian, for His Name) **from suffering that does not** (suffering as a murderer, thief, evildoer, busybody \'97 v. 15). Not all suffering counts as fellowship with Christ; only suffering that arises from identification with Him and His ways.\
\
