# **THE CONTEXT \'97 Romans 5-6**\
\
Paul has just declared in Romans 5:20-21 that **where sin abounded, grace did much more abound.** He has just declared that grace reigns through righteousness unto eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.\
\
This sets up the question that opens Romans 6 \'97 the question of every shallow critic of grace: *"If grace abounds where sin abounds, shall we not sin more, that grace may abound more?"*\
\
Paul's answer to this question is the entire chapter \'97 and his answer is grounded entirely in **the believer's identification with Christ.**\
