# **ROMANS 6:3-5 \'97 THE FOUNDATIONAL INDICATIVE: BAPTIZED INTO HIS DEATH**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u7970  \u7936 \u947 \u957 \u959 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u8005 \u963 \u959 \u953  \u7952 \u946 \u945 \u960 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u952 \u951 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u957 , \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u952 \u940 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u946 \u945 \u960 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u952 \u951 \u956 \u949 \u957 ; \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u940 \u966 \u951 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u946 \u945 \u960 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u952 \u940 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u957 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u8037 \u963 \u960 \u949 \u961  \u7968 \u947 \u941 \u961 \u952 \u951  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u7952 \u954  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u948 \u972 \u958 \u951 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u972 \u962 , \u959 \u8021 \u964 \u969 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7969 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u953 \u957 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u964 \u953  \u950 \u969 \u8134 \u962  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u945 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u969 \u956 \u949 \u957 . \u949 \u7984  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u963 \u973 \u956 \u966 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u953  \u947 \u949 \u947 \u972 \u957 \u945 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u8001 \u956 \u959 \u953 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7936 \u957 \u945 \u963 \u964 \u940 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u7952 \u963 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945 \'b7"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Know ye not, that all we which have been baptized into Jesus Christ, have been baptized into his death? We are buried then with him by baptism into his death, that like as Christ was raised up from the dead to the glory of the Father, so we also should walk in newness of life. For if we be planted with him to the similitude of his death, even so shall we be to the similitude of his resurrection."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of foundational importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u7970  \u7936 \u947 \u957 \u959 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949 ** \'97 *"or are you ignorant?"* Paul appeals to knowledge they should already have. The indicative is something the believer **must know**. Ignorance of one's identification with Christ leaves the believer powerless to walk in the imperative.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u8005 \u963 \u959 \u953  \u7952 \u946 \u945 \u960 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u952 \u951 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u957 , \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u952 \u940 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u946 \u945 \u960 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u952 \u951 \u956 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"as many as were baptized into Christ Jesus, were baptized into His death."*\
\
**Baptism here is more than an outward rite** \'97 it is the visible enactment of the believer's identification with Christ. To be baptized **into Christ** is to be baptized **into His death.** The two cannot be separated. We are not joined to a sin-bearing Christ at one point and detached from His death-bearing reality at another. **To be in Him is to be in His death.**\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u940 \u966 \u951 \u956 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"we were buried together with Him."* The aorist passive \'97 completed past action done to us. **We have been buried together with Christ.** Burial is the seal of death \'97 what is buried is settled as dead.\
\
**(4)** **The purpose: \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945 ... \u7952 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u953 \u957 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u964 \u953  \u950 \u969 \u8134 \u962  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u945 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u969 \u956 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"that we should walk in newness of life."*\
\
**Here we encounter the first imperative implied \'97 though stated as purpose.** The believer's burial with Christ has a stated purpose: that we should walk in newness of life. The indicative serves a practical end.\
\
**The walk is grounded in the resurrection** \'97 *"like as Christ was raised up from the dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in newness of life."* Our walk corresponds to His resurrection. As He was raised to a new mode of life, so we walk in a new mode of life.\
\
**(5)** **\uc0\u963 \u973 \u956 \u966 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u953  \u947 \u949 \u947 \u972 \u957 \u945 \u956 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"we have become grown-together / united / planted together."* The word **\u963 \u973 \u956 \u966 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u962 ** is striking \'97 it means *"grown together"* (as a graft grows together with its stock). **The believer is grown-together with Christ \'97 in the likeness of His death, and also in the likeness of His resurrection.**\
\
This is the indicative reality: we are organically united with Christ in both His death and His resurrection. The resurrection-union is as certain as the death-union.\
\
