# **ROMANS 6:6-7 \'97 THE OLD MAN CRUCIFIED**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u8001  \u960 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u953 \u8056 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u965 \u961 \u974 \u952 \u951 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u961 \u947 \u951 \u952 \u8135  \u964 \u8056  \u963 \u8182 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 , \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u956 \u951 \u954 \u941 \u964 \u953  \u948 \u959 \u965 \u955 \u949 \u973 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115 \'b7 \u8001  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u8060 \u957  \u948 \u949 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u943 \u969 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Knowing this, that our old man is crucified with him, that the body of sin might be destroyed, that henceforth we should not serve sin. For he that is dead, is freed from sin."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of supreme importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962 ** \'97 *"knowing this."* Again, the appeal to knowledge. The indicative must be known before it can be lived.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u8001  \u960 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u953 \u8056 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u965 \u961 \u974 \u952 \u951 ** \'97 *"our old man was crucified together [with Him]."*\
\
**The "old man"** (\uc0\u8001  \u960 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u953 \u8056 \u962  \u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962 ) is the person we were in Adam \'97 the sinner, the rebel, the bondservant of sin, the one under condemnation. **That person was crucified with Christ.** The verb is aorist passive \'97 a definite past action done to us by the Father at the cross.\
\
**This is one of the most liberating truths in all Scripture.** The person who lived before conversion \'97 who was a slave to sin, dominated by the flesh, alienated from God \'97 **does not exist anymore.** He was crucified. The believer is not the old man trying to be good; the believer is **a new man** in whom **the old man no longer lives.**\
\
**(3) The purpose:** **\uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u961 \u947 \u951 \u952 \u8135  \u964 \u8056  \u963 \u8182 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 , \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u956 \u951 \u954 \u941 \u964 \u953  \u948 \u959 \u965 \u955 \u949 \u973 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115 ** \'97 *"that the body of sin might be rendered powerless, that we should no longer serve sin."*\
\
**\uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u961 \u947 \u941 \u969 ** \'97 *"to render inoperative, to nullify, to deprive of power."* The body of sin (the entire structure of sinful patterns, habits, and identity that ruled the old man) **has been rendered powerless** by the crucifixion of the old man with Christ.\
\
**The result:** **\uc0\u964 \u959 \u8166  \u956 \u951 \u954 \u941 \u964 \u953  \u948 \u959 \u965 \u955 \u949 \u973 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115 ** \'97 *"that we should no longer be slaves to sin."*\
\
**This is the foundation of Christian freedom from sin's dominion.** Not that sin is gone (we will see it can still be yielded to), but that **the slavery is broken.** The old chains have been severed. We are no longer compelled to obey sin's commands. We are now free to obey righteousness.\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u8001  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u8060 \u957  \u948 \u949 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u943 \u969 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 ** \'97 *"For he who has died has been justified / set free from sin."*\
\
A legal principle: death pays sin's claim and ends sin's jurisdiction. A dead man cannot be summoned to obey his old master. The believer, having died with Christ, **has been judicially set free** from sin's claim. The court has no jurisdiction over a corpse.\
\
