# **ROMANS 6:8-10 \'97 LIVING WITH HIM**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u949 \u7984  \u948 \u8050  \u7936 \u960 \u949 \u952 \u940 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u963 \u8058 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183 , \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u963 \u965 \u950 \u942 \u963 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 , \u949 \u7984 \u948 \u972 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u7952 \u947 \u949 \u961 \u952 \u949 \u8054 \u962  \u7952 \u954  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u954 \u941 \u964 \u953  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u952 \u957 \u8132 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u953 , \u952 \u940 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u959 \u8016 \u954 \u941 \u964 \u953  \u954 \u965 \u961 \u953 \u949 \u973 \u949 \u953 \'b7 \u8003  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u966 \u940 \u960 \u945 \u958 \'b7 \u8003  \u948 \u8050  \u950 \u8135  \u950 \u8135  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Wherefore, if we be dead with Christ, we believe that we shall live also with him, Knowing that Christ being raised from the dead, dieth no more: death hath no more dominion over him. For in that he died, he died once to sin: but in that he liveth, he liveth to God."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u949 \u7984  \u948 \u8050  \u7936 \u960 \u949 \u952 \u940 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u963 \u8058 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183 , \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u963 \u965 \u950 \u942 \u963 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183 ** \'97 *"If we died with Christ, we believe we shall also live with Him."*\
\
The death-union guarantees the life-union. Paul presents this as an article of faith \'97 **\uc0\u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 we *believe* this. The believer's confidence in his new life with Christ is grounded in his death with Christ.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u7952 \u947 \u949 \u961 \u952 \u949 \u8054 \u962  \u7952 \u954  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u954 \u941 \u964 \u953  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u952 \u957 \u8132 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u953 ** \'97 *"Christ, having been raised from the dead, dies no more."*\
\
The risen Christ is in a **once-for-all** state. He will never die again. Death has no more dominion over Him. **And we are in Him.** Therefore, the believer's new life, like Christ's, is one over which death has no more dominion. Sin cannot kill us again; we are alive forever in Him.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u8003  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115  \u7936 \u960 \u941 \u952 \u945 \u957 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u966 \u940 \u960 \u945 \u958 \'b7 \u8003  \u948 \u8050  \u950 \u8135  \u950 \u8135  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 ** \'97 *"What He died, He died to sin once for all; what He lives, He lives to God."*\
\
Christ's death was a death **to sin** \'97 not that He sinned, but that He died in relation to sin (bearing it, exhausting its claim, ending its power over Him as our representative). Christ's life now is **a life unto God** \'97 entirely oriented to the Father.\
\
**This is the pattern for the believer.** As Christ died once for all to sin and now lives unto God, so we, in Him, died once for all to sin and now live unto God. The pattern of His existence is the pattern of ours.\
\
