# **ROMANS 6:11 \'97 THE FIRST IMPERATIVE: RECKON!**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u959 \u8021 \u964 \u969 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8017 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962  \u955 \u959 \u947 \u943 \u950 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u949 \u7990 \u957 \u945 \u953  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u956 \u8050 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115  \u950 \u8182 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Likewise think ye also, that ye are dead to sin, but are alive to God in Jesus Christ our Lord."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of supreme importance\
\
**Here is the first explicit imperative of the chapter \'97 and it is breathtakingly precise.**\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u959 \u8021 \u964 \u969 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8017 \u956 \u949 \u8150 \u962 ** \'97 *"so also you."* The pattern that has just been established for Christ (died to sin, lives to God) is now applied to the believer.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u955 \u959 \u947 \u943 \u950 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949 ** \'97 present imperative \'97 *"reckon, count, calculate, consider."* This is a continuing, present action. **Keep on reckoning yourselves.**\
\
The word **\uc0\u955 \u959 \u947 \u943 \u950 \u959 \u956 \u945 \u953 ** is a bookkeeping term. It means *to make a careful calculation and act on it as true.* The believer is commanded to **add up the facts of his identification with Christ** and treat the resulting reality as the operative truth of his life.\
\
**The reckoning does not create the reality.** The reality is already true (vv. 1-10 have established it). The reckoning is the believer's daily, moment-by-moment **agreement** with the reality the Father has already established.\
\
**(3) Two facts to be reckoned:**\
\
**\uc0\u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u956 \u8050 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115 ** \'97 *"dead to sin."* The believer is to count himself as dead to sin. When sin makes its claim \'97 "obey me, you have always obeyed me" \'97 the believer says: *"You speak to a dead man. I am dead to your claims."*\
\
**\uc0\u950 \u8182 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"alive to God in Christ Jesus."* The believer is to count himself as alive \'97 to the Father \'97 in Christ Jesus. **The new identity is Godward.** The orientation of the new life is toward the Father, through the Son.\
\
**(4) This is the heart of the indicative-to-imperative pattern.** The reality has been established by the Father at the cross and resurrection. The believer's task is to *reckon it true* and walk accordingly.\
\
This is **faith applied to identity.** It is not pretending; it is agreeing with the truth. The Father reckons us dead with Christ \'97 we reckon ourselves dead with Christ. Our reckoning aligns with His.\
\
---\
\
# **ROMANS 6:12-13 \'97 THE PRACTICAL IMPERATIVES**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u924 \u8052  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u941 \u964 \u969  \u7969  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u952 \u957 \u951 \u964 \u8183  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u8017 \u960 \u945 \u954 \u959 \u973 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8135  \u964 \u945 \u8150 \u962  \u7952 \u960 \u953 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u943 \u945 \u953 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 , \u956 \u951 \u948 \u8050  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u955 \u951  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8005 \u960 \u955 \u945  \u7936 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u949  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u8033 \u963 \u949 \u8054  \u7952 \u954  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u950 \u8182 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u955 \u951  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8005 \u960 \u955 \u945  \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u959 \u963 \u973 \u957 \u951 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Let not sin reign therefore in your mortal body, that ye should obey it in the lusts thereof: Neither give ye your members, as weapons of unrighteousness unto sin: but give yourselves unto God, as they that are alive from the dead, and give your members as weapons of righteousness unto God."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of decisive importance\
\
**Now the imperatives multiply.** Note the careful logic: because v. 11 has been reckoned (the indicative agreed to), now the practical commands follow.\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u924 \u8052  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u941 \u964 \u969  \u7969  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 ** \'97 *"Let sin not reign."* Present imperative \'97 a continuing prohibition. **Stop letting sin reign. Do not allow it to take the throne.**\
\
The verb is **\uc0\u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u949 \u973 \u969 ** \'97 *to reign as king.* Sin **wants to reign.** Sin's ambition is dominion. **And the believer's task is to refuse it the throne.**\
\
Notice: Paul does not say *"sin cannot be present in you."* He says *"do not let it reign."* Sin may still attempt to assert itself; the question is whether you grant it sovereignty. The believer has the standing to refuse \'97 because he died to sin's slavery (v. 6).\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u952 \u957 \u951 \u964 \u8183  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 ** \'97 *"in your mortal body."* This is honest. The body remains mortal \'97 still subject to its passions, its appetites, its weariness, its corruption. The body has not yet been redeemed (Rom 8:23). But sin's dominion in the body is to be refused.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u8017 \u960 \u945 \u954 \u959 \u973 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8135  \u964 \u945 \u8150 \u962  \u7952 \u960 \u953 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u943 \u945 \u953 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"so as to obey it in its desires."* Sin reigns through the body's desires when we obey them. To refuse sin's reign is to refuse to obey the body's sinful desires.\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u956 \u951 \u948 \u8050  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u955 \u951  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8005 \u960 \u955 \u945  \u7936 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u964 \u8135  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u8115 ** \'97 *"nor present your members as weapons of unrighteousness to sin."*\
\
**\uc0\u8005 \u960 \u955 \u945 ** \'97 *weapons / instruments.* The body's members (hands, feet, eyes, tongue, mind) are tools that can be used as **weapons** \'97 for sin or for righteousness. The believer is commanded **not to make his members available to sin as weapons against God and against righteousness.**\
\
**(5)** **\uc0\u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u949  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 ** \'97 *"but present yourselves to God."*\
\
Now the **positive command:** present yourselves **to God.** The verb is **\uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u951 \u956 \u953 ** \'97 *to present, to hand over, to place at someone's disposal.* The aorist tense here suggests a definitive presentation \'97 make this transfer.\
\
**\uc0\u8033 \u963 \u949 \u8054  \u7952 \u954  \u957 \u949 \u954 \u961 \u8182 \u957  \u950 \u8182 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u962 ** \'97 *"as those alive from the dead."* The basis of the self-presentation: **you are alive from the dead.** Your reckoning of vv. 11 informs your presentation of vv. 13.\
\
**(6)** **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8048  \u956 \u941 \u955 \u951  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u8005 \u960 \u955 \u945  \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u959 \u963 \u973 \u957 \u951 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 ** \'97 *"and your members as weapons of righteousness to God."*\
\
The same members that were weapons of unrighteousness are now presented as **weapons of righteousness to God.** The hands that took are now hands that give. The tongue that lied is now the tongue that speaks truth. The mind that imagined evil is now the mind that meditates on what is true, honorable, just, pure, lovely, and of good report (cf. Phil 4:8).\
\
