# **ROMANS 6:14 \'97 THE PROMISE THAT SUSTAINS THE COMMANDS**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u959 \u8016  \u954 \u965 \u961 \u953 \u949 \u973 \u963 \u949 \u953 , \u959 \u8016  \u947 \u940 \u961  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u949  \u8017 \u960 \u8056  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u8017 \u960 \u8056  \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For sin shall not have dominion over you: for ye are not under the Law, but under grace."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of foundational importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u959 \u8016  \u954 \u965 \u961 \u953 \u949 \u973 \u963 \u949 \u953 ** \'97 *"For sin shall not have dominion over you."*\
\
**This is a promise, not merely a command.** Future indicative \'97 **shall not.** Paul declares that sin **will not** rule over the believer.\
\
But notice: this comes right after the commands of vv. 12-13. The order is profound:\
- The believer is commanded to refuse sin's reign (v. 12).\
- The believer is commanded to present himself to God (v. 13).\
- And then: sin **shall not** have dominion (v. 14).\
\
**The promise is grounded in the obedience to the command \'97 and the obedience to the command is grounded in the indicative reality of co-crucifixion and resurrection.** The Christian life flows like this:\
1. **What is true** (indicative \'97 vv. 1-10).\
2. **What we reckon** (v. 11).\
3. **How we act** (vv. 12-13).\
4. **What is then experientially real** (v. 14).\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u959 \u8016  \u947 \u940 \u961  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u949  \u8017 \u960 \u8056  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u8017 \u960 \u8056  \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u957 ** \'97 *"For you are not under law but under grace."*\
\
This is the foundation of the promise. Under the law, sin had power because the law condemned the sinner and provoked the flesh (Rom 7:8-11). Under grace, the believer stands in the favor of God, possessing the righteousness of Christ, indwelt by the Spirit, free from condemnation. **Sin cannot rule a person who stands in grace** \'97 for grace has broken sin's grip and provided the resources for victory.\
\
---\
\
# **ROMANS 6:15-23 \'97 THE SLAVERY MOTIF**\
\
The chapter continues with Paul addressing a second objection \'97 *"Shall we sin because we are not under law but under grace?"* \'97 with a parallel structure: indicative, then imperative.\
\
### **Romans 6:15-18 (Greek, selections):**\
*"\uc0\u932 \u943  \u959 \u8022 \u957 ; \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u969 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7952 \u963 \u956 \u8050 \u957  \u8017 \u960 \u8056  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u8017 \u960 \u8056  \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u957 ; \u956 \u8052  \u947 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u953 \u964 \u959 . \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u959 \u7988 \u948 \u945 \u964 \u949  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u8103  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u948 \u959 \u973 \u955 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u8017 \u960 \u945 \u954 \u959 \u942 \u957 , \u948 \u959 \u8166 \u955 \u959 \u943  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u949  \u8103  \u8017 \u960 \u945 \u954 \u959 \u973 \u949 \u964 \u949 ... \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7974 \u964 \u949  \u948 \u959 \u8166 \u955 \u959 \u953  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u8017 \u960 \u951 \u954 \u959 \u973 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u949  \u948 \u8050  \u7952 \u954  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u8003 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u949 \u948 \u972 \u952 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u973 \u960 \u959 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u948 \u945 \u967 \u8134 \u962 , \u7952 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u952 \u949 \u961 \u969 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u7952 \u948 \u959 \u965 \u955 \u974 \u952 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u8135  \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u959 \u963 \u973 \u957 \u8131 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"What then? shall we sin, because we are not under the Law, but under grace? God forbid. Know ye not, that to whomsoever ye give yourselves as servants to obey, his servants ye are to whom ye obey... But God be thanked, that ye have been the servants of sin, but ye have obeyed from the heart unto the form of the doctrine, whereunto ye were delivered. Being then made free from sin, ye are made the servants of righteousness."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
Paul presents two slaveries: slavery to sin (which leads to death) and slavery to righteousness/God (which leads to sanctification and eternal life). The believer has been **set free** from the first and **made a slave** to the second.\
\
**The indicative:** You **were** slaves of sin; you **have been** set free; you **are now** slaves of righteousness (v. 18). These are settled facts.\
\
**The imperative implied:** Therefore present your members to righteousness, just as before you presented them to sin (v. 19).\
\
