# **ROMANS 6:23 \'97 THE CONCLUDING TRUTH**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u964 \u8048  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u8000 \u968 \u974 \u957 \u953 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u952 \u940 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u8050  \u967 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u950 \u969 \u8052  \u945 \u7984 \u974 \u957 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8183  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For the wages of sin is death: but the gift of God is eternal life, through Jesus Christ our Lord."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
The chapter closes with the great contrast. Sin **pays wages** \'97 and its wage is death. God **gives** \'97 and His gift is eternal life. Sin earns; grace gives. The two paths are utterly different in source and destination.\
\
And the gift is **\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8183  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ** \'97 *"in Christ Jesus our Lord."* Once again, the locus of the new life is identification with Christ.\
\
