\
# **THE GOVERNING PATTERN: INDICATIVE \uc0\u8594  RECKON \u8594  ACT**\
\
Romans 6 establishes the fundamental Christian operation:\
\
1. **Know what God has done** (the indicative \'97 vv. 1-10).\
2. **Reckon it true of yourself** (v. 11).\
3. **Act on the reckoning** (vv. 12-13).\
\
This is the precise reverse of the world's pattern, which is:\
1. *Try to act righteously.*\
2. *Hope to become righteous through your acts.*\
3. *Believe in your status only after performance.*\
\
**The Gospel pattern is the opposite:**\
1. *You ARE righteous in Christ (indicative).*\
2. *Reckon it true (faith).*\
3. *Act consistently with what is true (obedience).*\
\
The Christian does not act in order to become; he acts because he has become.\
\
---\
\
# **CROSS-WITNESSES \'97 THE PATTERN ELSEWHERE**\
\
This indicative-to-imperative pattern is not unique to Romans 6 \'97 it is the fundamental pattern of all NT ethics. Let us confirm by examining the most explicit parallels.\
\
---\
\
## **EPHESIANS \'97 THE INDICATIVE OF CHAPTERS 1-3, THE IMPERATIVE OF 4-6**\
\
The entire epistle to the Ephesians displays this pattern on a grand scale.\
\
**Chapters 1-3 are pure indicative:**\
- Chosen in Him before the foundation of the world (1:4).\
- Predestined to adoption (1:5).\
- Accepted in the Beloved (1:6).\
- Redeemed through His blood (1:7).\
- Sealed with the Holy Spirit (1:13).\
- Made alive together with Christ (2:5).\
- Raised up together (2:6).\
- Seated together in the heavenly places in Christ Jesus (2:6).\
- Fellow-citizens with the saints (2:19).\
- Members of God's household (2:19).\
- Built together for a habitation of God (2:22).\
- Filled with the fullness of God (3:19).\
\
**Chapters 4-6 are pure imperative \'97 and they begin with the pivot word.**\
\
### **Ephesians 4:1 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u928 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u8182  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u8001  \u948 \u941 \u963 \u956 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u7936 \u958 \u943 \u969 \u962  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u945 \u964 \u8134 \u963 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u955 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u7975 \u962  \u7952 \u954 \u955 \u942 \u952 \u951 \u964 \u949 ,"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"I therefore, being prisoner in the Lord, pray you that ye walk worthy of the vocation whereunto ye are called,"*\
\
The word **\uc0\u959 \u8022 \u957 ** \'97 *"therefore"* \'97 is the pivot. Three chapters of indicative produce one *"therefore"* that launches three chapters of imperative.\
\
**The imperative of Ephesians 4-6 is grounded entirely in the indicative of Ephesians 1-3.** Walk worthy of the calling \'97 *because of all that Christ has already accomplished in you.*\
\
