# **THE TRANSITION: WHY ROMANS 8 IS NECESSARY**\
\
Romans 6 established that the believer is **dead to sin and alive to God in Christ Jesus** \'97 and that on this basis, the believer must **reckon** the truth and **walk** accordingly.\
\
Romans 7 then confronts a question that any honest believer must face: **if I am dead to sin and freed from the law, why do I still struggle so painfully with sin?**\
\
Paul's answer in Romans 7 \'97 and we will not exposit it fully here \'97 is profound. The law is good, holy, and spiritual (7:12, 14). But the law cannot give life. The believer who tries to fight sin through self-effort, even from his new position in Christ, **discovers his own helplessness:**\
\
### **Romans 7:18-19 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u959 \u7990 \u948 \u945  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u959 \u7984 \u954 \u949 \u8150  \u7952 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u959 \u943 , \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u8125  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u943  \u956 \u959 \u965 , \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u952 \u972 \u957 \'b7 \u964 \u8056  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u940 \u954 \u949 \u953 \u964 \u945 \u943  \u956 \u959 \u953 , \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u8050  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u947 \u940 \u950 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8056  \u954 \u945 \u955 \u8056 \u957  \u959 \u8020 \'b7 \u959 \u8016  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u8003  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u969  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u8182  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u952 \u972 \u957 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u8003  \u959 \u8016  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u969  \u954 \u945 \u954 \u8056 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u960 \u961 \u940 \u963 \u963 \u969 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For I know, that in me, that is, in my flesh, dwelleth no good thing: for to will is present with me: but I find no means to perform that which is good. For I do not the good thing, which I would, but the evil, which I would not, that do I."*\
\
### **Romans 7:24 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u964 \u945 \u955 \u945 \u943 \u960 \u969 \u961 \u959 \u962  \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962 \'b7 \u964 \u943 \u962  \u956 \u949  \u8165 \u973 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u954  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u959 \u965 ;"*\
