\
### The Crisis Romans 7 Establishes\
\
The believer who tries to walk out his new identity **by self-effort, even with the help of the law, fails.** The flesh \'97 that remaining principle of sin in our mortal members \'97 frustrates every attempt at self-generated righteousness. The will is willing; the flesh is unable.\
\
**Romans 7 ends with a cry of helpless desperation:** *"Who shall deliver me?"*\
\
And **Romans 8 is the answer.** The deliverance comes not through more effort, not through better law-keeping, not through stricter discipline \'97 but through **the indwelling Spirit who imparts the very life of Christ to the believer.**\
\
This is critical to understand: **Romans 8 does not contradict Romans 6; it provides the operating mechanism by which the reality of Romans 6 becomes lived experience.** Romans 6 gives the position; Romans 8 gives the power.\
\
