# **ROMANS 8:1-2 \'97 NO CONDEMNATION; THE SPIRIT'S LAW**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u927 \u8016 \u948 \u8050 \u957  \u7940 \u961 \u945  \u957 \u8166 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u940 \u954 \u961 \u953 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 . \u8001  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u950 \u969 \u8134 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u7968 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u952 \u941 \u961 \u969 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949  \u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Now then there is no condemnation to them that are in Christ Jesus, which walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit. For the law of the Spirit of life which is in Christ Jesus, hath freed me from the law of sin and of death."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of foundational importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u927 \u8016 \u948 \u8050 \u957  \u7940 \u961 \u945  \u957 \u8166 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u940 \u954 \u961 \u953 \u956 \u945 ** \'97 *"Therefore now no condemnation."*\
\
The word **\uc0\u7940 \u961 \u945 ** (*therefore*) connects back to all that has preceded \'97 both the established reality of Romans 6 and the demonstrated helplessness of Romans 7. The conclusion: **there is no condemnation for those who are in Christ Jesus.**\
\
The word **\uc0\u957 \u8166 \u957 ** \'97 *now* \'97 is significant. **At this present time**, the believer stands without condemnation. Not someday, not after enough good works, not when sanctification is complete. **Now.** This is the believer's present standing.\
\
The phrase **\uc0\u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"to those in Christ Jesus"* \'97 is the qualifier. The freedom from condemnation belongs to those who are **in Him.** This is the same identification we have traced throughout \'97 being in Christ is the basis of every blessing.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u8001  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u950 \u969 \u8134 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"For the law of the Spirit of life in Christ Jesus..."*\
\
Paul uses the word **\uc0\u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u962 ** (*law*) in a different sense here \'97 not the Mosaic Law, but **a governing principle, an operating order.** The "law of the Spirit of life" is **the principle by which the Spirit operates in the believer to produce life.**\
\
This stands in contrast to the **\uc0\u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u940 \u964 \u959 \u965 ** \'97 *"the law of sin and death"* \'97 the principle by which sin operates in the flesh to produce death (described in Romans 7).\
\
Two competing principles, two competing operations. The Spirit's law is liberating; the flesh's law is enslaving. **And in Christ Jesus, the Spirit's law has freed the believer from the flesh's law.**\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7968 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u952 \u941 \u961 \u969 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u956 \u949 ** \'97 *"has freed me."* Aorist tense \'97 completed past action. The freedom has been accomplished. The believer does not need to *achieve* this freedom \'97 he stands in it.\
\
