# **ROMANS 8:3-4 \'97 WHAT THE LAW COULD NOT DO, GOD DID**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u964 \u8056  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7936 \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u965 , \u7952 \u957  \u8103  \u7968 \u963 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u972 \u962 , \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u933 \u7985 \u8056 \u957  \u960 \u941 \u956 \u968 \u945 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u8001 \u956 \u959 \u953 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u941 \u954 \u961 \u953 \u957 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u943 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u943 \u969 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u965  \u960 \u955 \u951 \u961 \u969 \u952 \u8135  \u7952 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u956 \u8052  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u963 \u940 \u961 \u954 \u945  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For that that was impossible to the Law, inasmuch as it was weak, because of the flesh, God sending his own Son, in the similitude of sinful flesh, and for sin, condemned sin in the flesh, That that righteousness of the Law might be fulfilled in us, which walk not after the flesh, but after the Spirit."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of decisive importance\
\
**(1)** The law was **weak through the flesh.** The law was righteous (Rom 7:12), but it could not produce righteousness in fallen humanity because the flesh resisted it.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u933 \u7985 \u8056 \u957  \u960 \u941 \u956 \u968 \u945 \u962 ** \'97 *"God, sending His own Son."* The Father is the actor. He sent His own Son.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u8001 \u956 \u959 \u953 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 ** \'97 *"in the likeness of sinful flesh."* The Son took on **the likeness** of sinful flesh \'97 true humanity, but without sin (Heb 4:15). He was made like His brethren in all things, yet without sin.\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u941 \u954 \u961 \u953 \u957 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u943 ** \'97 *"condemned sin in the flesh."* At the cross, the Father **condemned sin** \'97 passed judicial sentence on it \'97 **in the flesh** of His Son. Sin's claim on humanity was exhausted in the body of the Son who bore it.\
\
**(5)** **The purpose: \uc0\u7989 \u957 \u945  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u943 \u969 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u965  \u960 \u955 \u951 \u961 \u969 \u952 \u8135  \u7952 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u8150 \u957 ** \'97 *"that the righteous requirement of the law might be fulfilled in us."*\
\
**This is profound.** The law's righteous demand \'97 which the law itself could not produce \'97 **is now fulfilled IN US.** Not by our effort. Not by our discipline. Not by our resolution. **But by the Spirit's work in those who walk after the Spirit.**\
\
The believer who walks by the Spirit fulfills the righteous demand of the law \'97 not by trying to keep the law, but by being indwelt by the One who fulfilled it. **The Spirit produces in us what the law could only demand.**\
\
This is the transition from Romans 7 to Romans 8 in compressed form: the law's demand, which the flesh could not meet, is now met by the Spirit's life in those who are in Christ Jesus.\
\
