---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1)** Paul presents **two fundamental orientations of life:**\
- **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u963 \u940 \u961 \u954 \u945 ** \'97 *"according to the flesh"* \'97 the orientation that lives by the principles, desires, and operations of the unregenerate human nature.\
- **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945 ** \'97 *"according to the Spirit"* \'97 the orientation that lives by the principles, desires, and operations of the indwelling Holy Spirit.\
\
These are not two zones the believer moves between casually; they are two fundamentally different operating systems for life.\
\
**(2) The key word: \uc0\u966 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u951 \u956 \u945 ** \'97 *"mind-set, way of thinking, what one is set on."* This is more than intellectual thought; it is the deep orientation of one's affections, values, and pursuits. Where one's mind is set.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u964 \u8056  \u966 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u951 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u952 \u940 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"the mind-set of the flesh is death."* Not produces death \'97 *is* death. The very orientation of the flesh-life is already in the realm of death.\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u964 \u8056  \u966 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u951 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u950 \u969 \u8052  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u949 \u7984 \u961 \u942 \u957 \u951 ** \'97 *"the mind-set of the Spirit is life and peace."* The Spirit's orientation **is** life and peace. The believer's Spirit-orientation is itself the experience of life and peace, not merely a means to it.\
\
**(5)** Paul is sobering: those who are in the flesh **cannot** please God. Not "find it difficult to please" \'97 **cannot.** The flesh, by its very nature, is unable to please God. It is enmity against God.\
\
This sharpens the practical implication: **the believer must not attempt to please God in the energy of the flesh.** All such attempts are doomed. The believer pleases God only as he walks by the Spirit.\
