# **ROMANS 8:12-13 \'97 THE OBLIGATION AND THE OPERATION**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u7948 \u961 \u945  \u959 \u8022 \u957 , \u7936 \u948 \u949 \u955 \u966 \u959 \u943 , \u8000 \u966 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u941 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u963 \u956 \u941 \u957 , \u959 \u8016  \u964 \u8135  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u963 \u940 \u961 \u954 \u945  \u950 \u8134 \u957 \'b7 \u949 \u7984  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u963 \u940 \u961 \u954 \u945  \u950 \u8134 \u964 \u949 , \u956 \u941 \u955 \u955 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u952 \u957 \u8132 \u963 \u954 \u949 \u953 \u957 \'b7 \u949 \u7984  \u948 \u8050  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u960 \u961 \u940 \u958 \u949 \u953 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u949 , \u950 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Therefore brethren, we are debtors not to the flesh, to live after the flesh: For if ye live after the flesh, ye shall die: but if ye mortify the deeds of the body by the Spirit, ye shall live."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of decisive practical importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u8000 \u966 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u941 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7952 \u963 \u956 \u941 \u957 , \u959 \u8016  \u964 \u8135  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u943 ** \'97 *"we are debtors, not to the flesh."*\
\
**We owe nothing to the flesh.** The flesh has done nothing for us; we owe it no allegiance. It is a tyrant we have been freed from, not a benefactor we must honor. The believer has **no debt** to the flesh \'97 and therefore no obligation to live according to its dictates.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u949 \u7984  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u960 \u961 \u940 \u958 \u949 \u953 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u952 \u945 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u949 ** \'97 *"if by the Spirit you put to death the deeds of the body."*\
\
**Here is the practical command and its mechanism.**\
\
**The command:** *"Put to death the deeds of the body."* This is the believer's responsibility. The verb **\uc0\u952 \u945 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u949 ** (present active) means *"keep on putting to death."* This is ongoing, daily mortification.\
\
**The mechanism: \uc0\u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 ** \'97 *"by the Spirit."* Not by the flesh's own effort. Not by self-discipline alone. Not by law-keeping. **By the indwelling Spirit's power.**\
\
**This is the practical answer to Romans 7's crisis.** Where the law could not produce victory because of the flesh's weakness, the indwelling Spirit produces what is impossible to the flesh.\
\
The pattern is:\
1. **The Spirit indwells (indicative, vv. 9-11).**\
2. **The believer, by the Spirit, puts to death the deeds of the body (imperative, v. 13).**\
3. **Life follows (promise, v. 13).**\
\
This is parallel to the Romans 6 pattern but with the Spirit's empowering work made explicit. The believer is responsible to act (*put to death*), but the power for the action comes from the indwelling Spirit, not from self-effort.\
\
