# **ROMANS 8:18-27 \'97 THE PRESENT SUFFERING AND THE SPIRIT'S INTERCESSION**\
\
We have already examined the suffering theme (Rom 8:17-18) and the groaning of creation (8:18-25) in our earlier discussion. Let us now focus on what is critical for life in the Spirit:\
\
### **Romans 8:26-27 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u8041 \u963 \u945 \u973 \u964 \u969 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u953 \u955 \u945 \u956 \u946 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8135  \u7936 \u963 \u952 \u949 \u957 \u949 \u943 \u8115  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 \'b7 \u964 \u8056  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u964 \u943  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u949 \u965 \u958 \u974 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8056  \u948 \u949 \u8150  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u959 \u7988 \u948 \u945 \u956 \u949 \u957 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056  \u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u8017 \u960 \u949 \u961 \u949 \u957 \u964 \u965 \u947 \u967 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u963 \u964 \u949 \u957 \u945 \u947 \u956 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u7936 \u955 \u945 \u955 \u942 \u964 \u959 \u953 \u962 \'b7 \u8001  \u948 \u8050  \u7952 \u961 \u945 \u965 \u957 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u959 \u7990 \u948 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u943  \u964 \u8056  \u966 \u961 \u972 \u957 \u951 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u957  \u7952 \u957 \u964 \u965 \u947 \u967 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u7937 \u947 \u943 \u969 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Likewise the Spirit also helpeth our infirmities: for we know not what to pray as we ought: but the Spirit itself maketh request for us with sighs, which cannot be expressed. But he that searcheth the hearts, knoweth what is the meaning of the Spirit: for he maketh request for the Saints, according to the will of God."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of supreme practical importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u953 \u955 \u945 \u956 \u946 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8135  \u7936 \u963 \u952 \u949 \u957 \u949 \u943 \u8115  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ** \'97 *"the Spirit helps our weakness."*\
\
**\uc0\u963 \u965 \u957 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u953 \u955 \u945 \u956 \u946 \u940 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u945 \u953 ** is a vivid word: *"to take hold of together with one against something."* The Spirit takes hold of our weakness *alongside us* \'97 as one who helps us bear what we cannot bear alone.\
\
**The believer's weakness is honestly acknowledged.** We do not pretend to strength we do not have. We are weak. And the Spirit takes hold with us in our weakness.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u964 \u8056  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u964 \u943  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u949 \u965 \u958 \u974 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8056  \u948 \u949 \u8150  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u959 \u7988 \u948 \u945 \u956 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"for we do not know what we ought to pray for as we should."*\
\
**A profound admission.** Even in prayer \'97 perhaps especially in prayer \'97 we do not know how to pray rightly. The believer is honest about this ignorance.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056  \u964 \u8056  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u8017 \u960 \u949 \u961 \u949 \u957 \u964 \u965 \u947 \u967 \u940 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u963 \u964 \u949 \u957 \u945 \u947 \u956 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u7936 \u955 \u945 \u955 \u942 \u964 \u959 \u953 \u962 ** \'97 *"the Spirit Himself intercedes with groanings that cannot be uttered."*\
\
The Spirit Himself intercedes for us **with groanings beyond articulation.** When we do not know how to pray, the Spirit takes our inarticulate longings and presents them to the Father in accordance with His will.\
\
This is a tremendous comfort. Even when the believer is overwhelmed, perplexed, grieved beyond words \'97 the Spirit prays for him in groanings that perfectly accord with the Father's will. **No prayer of the believer is wasted, even when he himself cannot find words.**\
\
