\
### Observations\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u961 \u947 \u949 \u8150  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u952 \u972 \u957 ** \'97 *"all things work together for good."*\
\
For those who love God, **all things** \'97 joys and sorrows, victories and defeats, gains and losses \'97 work together (\uc0\u963 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u961 \u947 \u949 \u8150 ) **for good.** The Father is sovereign over the whole tapestry of the believer's life, weaving every thread toward His purpose.\
\
**(2) The Father's purpose: \uc0\u963 \u965 \u956 \u956 \u972 \u961 \u966 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u949 \u7984 \u954 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u933 \u7985 \u959 \u8166  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"conformed to the image of His Son."*\
\
**This is the Father's eternal purpose for every believer:** to be conformed to the image of His Beloved Son. Everything that happens to the believer \'97 every blessing, every trial, every joy, every sorrow \'97 is being used by the Father toward this end. We will examine this more fully shortly.\
\
**(3) The golden chain:** **foreknew \uc0\u8594  predestined \u8594  called \u8594  justified \u8594  glorified.** Five aorist verbs \'97 five completed actions in the Father's purpose. **And note: glorified is past tense.** In the Father's eternal purpose, the believer is already glorified. The future is so certain it is reckoned as past.\
\
