# **PART 1 \'97 ROMANS 12: THE LIVING SACRIFICE AND THE RENEWED MIND**\
\
## **The Transition**\
\
Paul has just concluded eleven chapters of doctrinal foundation \'97 sin, justification, sanctification, life in the Spirit, the Father's sovereign plan in Israel and the nations. Then comes the great **\uc0\u959 \u8022 \u957 ** (*therefore*) at Romans 12:1 \'97 the pivot from indicative to imperative on a grand scale.\
\
---\
\
## **Romans 12:1 \'97 THE LIVING SACRIFICE**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u928 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u8182  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962 , \u7936 \u948 \u949 \u955 \u966 \u959 \u943 , \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u959 \u7984 \u954 \u964 \u953 \u961 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u964 \u8134 \u963 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8048  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u945  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u952 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u950 \u8182 \u963 \u945 \u957  \u7937 \u947 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u949 \u8016 \u940 \u961 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 , \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u955 \u959 \u947 \u953 \u954 \u8052 \u957  \u955 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957 \'b7"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"I beseech you therefore brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye give up your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable serving of God."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of foundational importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u928 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u8182  \u959 \u8022 \u957 ** \'97 *"I therefore beseech you."* The word **\u959 \u8022 \u957 ** (*therefore*) gathers up all eleven preceding chapters. The imperative is grounded in everything Paul has established. The believer is being asked to act **on the basis of all that God has done.**\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u948 \u953 \u8048  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u959 \u7984 \u954 \u964 \u953 \u961 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"by the mercies of God."* The motivation for the imperative is **the Father's mercies** \'97 the entire chain of mercy Paul has unfolded (chosen, called, justified, indwelt, sealed, secured). The believer is not motivated by fear or by the threat of loss, but by gratitude for mercy received.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u964 \u8134 \u963 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u8048  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u945  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ** \'97 *"present your bodies."* This is the same verb **\u960 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u951 \u956 \u953 ** Paul used in Romans 6:13 \'97 *"present yourselves to God."* Now he specifies: **present your bodies.** Not your minds only, not your spirits only \'97 your bodies. The physical, mortal, fleshly bodies in which we live our daily lives.\
\
**This is striking after Romans 7-8.** Paul has just established that the body is mortal, weak, and the seat of competing desires. Yet **this very body** is to be presented as a sacrifice. The Father does not despise the body; He receives it as a holy offering.\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u952 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u950 \u8182 \u963 \u945 \u957 ** \'97 *"a living sacrifice."* A paradox. OT sacrifices were dead. The believer's sacrifice is **alive** \'97 continually being offered, not slain once and consumed. The believer's life itself is the offering.\
\
**(5)** **\uc0\u7937 \u947 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u949 \u8016 \u940 \u961 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 ** \'97 *"holy, well-pleasing to God."* The sacrifice is **holy** (set apart, dedicated) and **well-pleasing** to the Father. This is the believer's life when wholly given to the Father \'97 a fragrant offering received with delight.\
\
**(6)** **\uc0\u964 \u8052 \u957  \u955 \u959 \u947 \u953 \u954 \u8052 \u957  \u955 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ** \'97 *"your reasonable service / spiritual worship."*\
\
**\uc0\u955 \u959 \u947 \u953 \u954 \u972 \u962 ** can mean *"rational, reasonable"* (related to **\u955 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 reason, word) or *"spiritual."* The Geneva translates *"reasonable serving."* Either way, the meaning converges: in light of God's mercies, this whole-life presentation is the **only reasonable response.** It is not extreme; it is not optional; it is the proper, fitting, rational service of those who have received what the believer has received.\
\
---\
\
### Practical Implications\
\
**(1) The believer's body is the place of worship.** Not the church building. Not a sacred space. **The body itself, presented to God, is the temple of acceptable worship.** This dovetails with what we established in Part F \'97 the believer's body is the temple of the Holy Spirit (1 Cor 6:19).\
\
**(2) Worship is comprehensive, not compartmentalized.** What we eat, what we wear, what we do with our hands, where we go with our feet, what we say with our tongues, what we think with our minds \'97 **all of this is the sphere of worship.** There is no secular/sacred division in the believer's life. **Every act of the body is potentially an act of worship.**\
\
**(3) The presentation is to be definite.** The aorist infinitive **\uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u964 \u8134 \u963 \u945 \u953 ** suggests a decisive act. The believer is to make a deliberate, conscious presentation of his body to God \'97 not as a vague aspiration, but as a settled transaction. *"Father, this body is Yours. Use it as You will."*\
\
---\
\
## **Romans 12:2 \'97 THE RENEWED MIND**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u956 \u8052  \u963 \u965 \u963 \u967 \u951 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u943 \u950 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u964 \u8183  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u8179 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u956 \u959 \u961 \u966 \u959 \u8166 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u964 \u8135  \u7936 \u957 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u957 \u959 \u972 \u962 , \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u959 \u954 \u953 \u956 \u940 \u950 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u964 \u943  \u964 \u8056  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u951 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 , \u964 \u8056  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u952 \u8056 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u949 \u8016 \u940 \u961 \u949 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u941 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u959 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And fashion not yourselves like unto this world, but be ye changed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what that good, that acceptable and perfect will of God is."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of decisive practical importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u956 \u8052  \u963 \u965 \u963 \u967 \u951 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u943 \u950 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u964 \u8183  \u945 \u7984 \u8182 \u957 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u8179 ** \'97 *"do not be conformed to this age."*\
\
The verb **\uc0\u963 \u965 \u963 \u967 \u951 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u943 \u950 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949 ** is from **\u963 \u967 \u8134 \u956 \u945 ** \'97 *outward form, fashion, appearance.* Present passive imperative \'97 *"stop being shaped to fit the pattern of this age."*\
\
The believer is **shaped by something** \'97 the question is what. The world (this age) is constantly pressing its mold upon the believer through media, education, culture, fashion, expectation, ideology, advertising, conversation. To live without resistance is to be molded into the world's shape.\
\
Paul commands: **do not conform.** Refuse the world's mold. Do not let this age dictate your outward form \'97 your values, your priorities, your habits, your appearance, your patterns.\
\
**(2)** **\uc0\u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u956 \u959 \u961 \u966 \u959 \u8166 \u963 \u952 \u949 ** \'97 *"but be transformed."*\
\
**\uc0\u956 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u956 \u959 \u961 \u966 \u959 \u8166 \u963 \u952 \u949 ** is from **\u956 \u959 \u961 \u966 \u942 ** \'97 *inward, essential form.* This is the same root as the **\u956 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u956 \u972 \u961 \u966 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u962 ** (*metamorphosis*) of the caterpillar to butterfly. **A complete inward transformation of essential form.** Present passive imperative \'97 *"keep being transformed."*\
\
The contrast is precise: do not let your outward **\uc0\u963 \u967 \u8134 \u956 \u945 ** be shaped by the world; let your inward **\u956 \u959 \u961 \u966 \u942 ** be transformed by God. **Outward form follows inward form.** When the inner being is being transformed, the outer life is increasingly conformed not to this age but to Christ.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u964 \u8135  \u7936 \u957 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u957 \u959 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 *"by the renewing of the mind."*\
\
**The mechanism of transformation is the renewing of the mind (\uc0\u957 \u959 \u8166 \u962 ).**\
\
The **\uc0\u957 \u959 \u8166 \u962 ** is the believer's faculty of understanding, reasoning, perceiving, evaluating. **It is the mind, but not in a narrow intellectual sense \'97 it is the seat of one's whole orientation, values, and worldview.**\
\
The mind is renewed (**\uc0\u7936 \u957 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u943 \u957 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u962 **) \'97 made new, fresh, reconstituted \'97 by the Spirit working through the Word. As the believer feeds on Scripture, meditates on the Father's truth, beholds the Son's glory (2 Cor 3:18), and walks in the Spirit, his mind is progressively renewed.\
\
**The renewed mind is the inner mechanism of outer transformation.** As the believer thinks differently \'97 sees the world differently, evaluates differently, desires differently \'97 his outward life is correspondingly transformed.\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u959 \u954 \u953 \u956 \u940 \u950 \u949 \u953 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u964 \u943  \u964 \u8056  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u951 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166 ** \'97 *"that you may prove / discern what the will of God is."*\
\
The result of the renewed mind: **the ability to discern the Father's will.** The unrenewed mind cannot discern God's will \'97 it is set on the things of the flesh (Rom 8:5-7). The renewed mind, oriented by the Spirit, can recognize, evaluate, and confirm what is the Father's good, well-pleasing, and perfect will.\
\
**This is critically important for practical decision-making.** The believer does not need a special revelation for every decision \'97 though he must be open to such. **The renewed mind, saturated with Scripture and yielded to the Spirit, can discern the Father's will in the ordinary course of life.**\
\
---\
\
### Practical Implications\
\
**(1) The believer must be actively engaged in mind-renewal.** This requires:\
\
- **Saturation in Scripture** \'97 reading, meditating, memorizing, studying the Word so that the renewed mind has the material from which to think God's thoughts after Him.\
- **Resistance to worldly inputs** \'97 being discerning about what media, entertainment, conversation, and influences shape the mind.\
- **Cultivation of holy thought patterns** \'97 *"Whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report... think on these things"* (Phil 4:8 Geneva).\
- **Walking in the Spirit** \'97 for it is the Spirit who applies the Word to renew the mind.\
- **Fellowship with the saints** \'97 being shaped by godly community rather than by worldly community.\
\
**(2) The renewing of the mind is an ongoing process.** The present tense **\uc0\u956 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u956 \u959 \u961 \u966 \u959 \u8166 \u963 \u952 \u949 ** suggests continuous action. The believer never reaches a point of completion in this life. He is always being transformed, always being renewed.\
\
**(3) Discernment grows.** As the mind is renewed, the believer's ability to recognize the Father's will sharpens. What was once unclear becomes clearer. What was once a difficult judgment becomes an instinctive perception. The mature believer increasingly walks in the Father's will not by anguished deliberation but by Spirit-formed instinct.\
\
