# **PART 2 \'97 GALATIANS 5: THE WALK BY THE SPIRIT AND THE WAR WITH THE FLESH**\
\
## **The Context**\
\
Paul has spent the first four chapters of Galatians defending the Gospel of grace against the Judaizers who insisted that Gentile believers must keep the Mosaic Law to be saved. Now, in chapters 5-6, he turns to the practical implications: **how is the believer to live who is free from the law?**\
\
The answer is not antinomianism (lawlessness) but **walking by the Spirit.** The believer is free from the law as a system of justification, but he is by no means free to indulge the flesh. He is freed *from* law and sin *into* the Spirit's lordship.\
\
---\
\
## **Galatians 5:1 \'97 STAND FAST IN FREEDOM**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u964 \u8135  \u7952 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u952 \u949 \u961 \u943 \u8115  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u7968 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u952 \u941 \u961 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957 \'b7 \u963 \u964 \u942 \u954 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u959 \u8022 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u956 \u8052  \u960 \u940 \u955 \u953 \u957  \u950 \u965 \u947 \u8183  \u948 \u959 \u965 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u7952 \u957 \u941 \u967 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Christ hath made us free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
**\uc0\u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u7968 \u955 \u949 \u965 \u952 \u941 \u961 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"Christ has freed us."* Aorist tense \'97 the freedom is accomplished. The believer **stands** in this freedom. He does not negotiate it, does not earn it, does not re-create it. He stands in what Christ has won.\
\
**\uc0\u963 \u964 \u942 \u954 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u959 \u8022 \u957 ** \'97 *"stand therefore."* The command is to stand firm. Not to revert to the yoke of bondage (the law as a system of justification or the flesh as a master).\
\
