## **Galatians 5:16-17 \'97 THE FOUNDATIONAL COMMAND**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u923 \u941 \u947 \u969  \u948 \u941 , \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u945 \u964 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u960 \u953 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u959 \u8016  \u956 \u8052  \u964 \u949 \u955 \u941 \u963 \u951 \u964 \u949 . \u7969  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u963 \u8048 \u961 \u958  \u7952 \u960 \u953 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u949 \u8150  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u8050  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u972 \u962 \'b7 \u964 \u945 \u8166 \u964 \u945  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u942 \u955 \u959 \u953 \u962  \u7936 \u957 \u964 \u943 \u954 \u949 \u953 \u964 \u945 \u953 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u956 \u8052  \u7939  \u7952 \u8048 \u957  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u945 \u8166 \u964 \u945  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u8134 \u964 \u949 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Then I say, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfill the lusts of the flesh. For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh: and these are contrary one to another, so that ye cannot do the same things that ye would."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of decisive importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u945 \u964 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949 ** \'97 *"walk by the Spirit."* Present imperative \'97 continuous walking. The Christian life is not a one-time decision; it is a continuous walk.\
\
**The dative \uc0\u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  is instrumental** \'97 *"by means of the Spirit."* The Spirit is both the **path** and the **power** of the walk. The believer walks **by** the Spirit's leading and **in** the Spirit's empowering.\
\
**(2) The promise:** **\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u953 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u959 \u8016  \u956 \u8052  \u964 \u949 \u955 \u941 \u963 \u951 \u964 \u949 ** \'97 *"you shall by no means fulfill the lust of the flesh."*\
\
**\uc0\u959 \u8016  \u956 \u942 ** with the aorist subjunctive is the strongest possible negation in Greek \'97 *"absolutely not, by no means, in no way."* The promise is absolute: **the believer who walks by the Spirit will not fulfill the flesh's lust.**\
\
This is the practical answer to every besetting sin. The believer does not defeat the flesh by attacking it directly; he defeats it by **walking in the Spirit** \'97 at which point the flesh's lust is bypassed.\
\
**(3)** **\uc0\u7969  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u963 \u8048 \u961 \u958  \u7952 \u960 \u953 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u949 \u8150  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u8050  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u963 \u945 \u961 \u954 \u972 \u962 ** \'97 *"the flesh lusts against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh."*\
\
**Two opposing principles within the believer.** This is honest. The flesh (the remaining principle of sin in our mortal members) does not disappear at conversion. It lusts (\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u953 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u949 \u8150  \'97 *desires, craves*) against the Spirit. And the Spirit lusts against the flesh \'97 opposes it, contradicts it, fights it.\
\
**These are contrary** (\uc0\u7936 \u955 \u955 \u942 \u955 \u959 \u953 \u962  \u7936 \u957 \u964 \u943 \u954 \u949 \u953 \u964 \u945 \u953 ). The believer cannot serve both. The believer's life is a constant choice \'97 who will I walk with today, this hour, this moment? The Spirit or the flesh?\
\
