## **Galatians 5:22-23 \'97 THE FRUIT OF THE SPIRIT**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u8001  \u948 \u8050  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u960 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u972 \u962  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 , \u967 \u945 \u961 \u940 , \u949 \u7984 \u961 \u942 \u957 \u951 , \u956 \u945 \u954 \u961 \u959 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u943 \u945 , \u967 \u961 \u951 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962 , \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u952 \u969 \u963 \u973 \u957 \u951 , \u960 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u962 , \u960 \u961 \u945 \u944 \u964 \u951 \u962 , \u7952 \u947 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u945 \'b7 \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u953 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, long suffering, gentleness, goodness, faith, Meekness, temperance: against such there is no Law."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of supreme importance\
\
**(1) Note: \uc0\u8001  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u960 \u972 \u962  \'97 singular, not "the fruits."** It is **one fruit** with nine facets. The Spirit's fruit is **a single integrated character** \'97 not a buffet from which we can select preferences.\
\
**(2)** Compare with the works of the flesh. The flesh produces "works" (\uc0\u7956 \u961 \u947 \u945  \'97 plural, fragmented, disordered acts). The Spirit produces "fruit" (\u954 \u945 \u961 \u960 \u972 \u962  \'97 singular, organic, integrated growth).\
\
**This contrast is profound:** the flesh manufactures (works); the Spirit grows (fruit). The flesh produces by effort; the Spirit produces by organic life within. **The fruit cannot be forced; it grows naturally from a healthy union with the Spirit.**\
\
**(3) The nine facets:**\
\
- **\uc0\u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 ** \'97 love (sacrificial, willed love)\
- **\uc0\u967 \u945 \u961 \u940 ** \'97 joy (the deep joy of the Lord)\
- **\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u961 \u942 \u957 \u951 ** \'97 peace (the peace of God that surpasses understanding)\
- **\uc0\u956 \u945 \u954 \u961 \u959 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u943 \u945 ** \'97 long-suffering / patience with people\
- **\uc0\u967 \u961 \u951 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962 ** \'97 kindness, useful service\
- **\uc0\u7936 \u947 \u945 \u952 \u969 \u963 \u973 \u957 \u951 ** \'97 goodness, moral excellence\
- **\uc0\u960 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u962 ** \'97 faith / faithfulness\
- **\uc0\u960 \u961 \u945 \u944 \u964 \u951 \u962 ** \'97 meekness, gentle strength\
- **\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u945 ** \'97 self-control\
\
**These are the character of Christ.** Each one was perfectly displayed in Him. As the Spirit conforms the believer to the Son's image (Rom 8:29), these qualities increasingly appear in the believer's life \'97 not by his manufacturing them, but by the Spirit's growing them.\
\
**(4)** **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u953 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"against such things there is no law."*\
\
A wonderful note. No law condemns these qualities. The believer who walks in the Spirit and produces this fruit is automatically in fulfillment of every law's righteous demand \'97 without being under the law.\
\
