## **The Modes of Prayer**\
\
The NT presents several distinct modes of prayer the believer is to practice:\
\
### **1. Petition (\uc0\u945 \u7988 \u964 \u951 \u963 \u953 \u962 ) \'97 Asking for Specific Needs**\
\
### **Matthew 7:7-11 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u913 \u7984 \u964 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u948 \u959 \u952 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 \'b7 \u950 \u951 \u964 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u949 \u8017 \u961 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u949 \'b7 \u954 \u961 \u959 \u973 \u949 \u964 \u949 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u957 \u959 \u953 \u947 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 ..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Ask, and it shall be given you: seek, and ye shall find: knock, and it shall be opened unto you..."*\
\
The Father invites our requests. **Three present imperatives** \'97 *ask, seek, knock* \'97 all in continuous tense. We are to keep asking, keep seeking, keep knocking. The Father delights to give good gifts to His children.\
\
### **2. Thanksgiving (\uc0\u949 \u8016 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u943 \u945 )**\
\
### **1 Thessalonians 5:18 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u8054  \u949 \u8016 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949 \'b7 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u951 \u956 \u945  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"In all things give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus toward you."*\
\
In **all things** \'97 not for all things in the sense of celebrating evil, but **in the midst of all things** \'97 give thanks. Thanksgiving is the will of God for the believer.\
\
### **3. Intercession (\uc0\u7956 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u965 \u958 \u953 \u962 ) \'97 Praying for Others**\
\
### **1 Timothy 2:1-2 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u928 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u8182  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u960 \u961 \u8182 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u949 \u8150 \u963 \u952 \u945 \u953  \u948 \u949 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953 \u962 , \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u949 \u965 \u967 \u940 \u962 , \u7952 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u958 \u949 \u953 \u962 , \u949 \u8016 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962 , \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u969 \u957 , \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u955 \u941 \u969 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u960 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u967 \u8135  \u8004 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957 ,"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"I exhort therefore, that first of all, supplications, prayers, intercessions, and giving of thanks be made for all men: For Kings, and for all that are in authority..."*\
\
The believer is to intercede for **all men** \'97 for the lost, for fellow believers, for rulers and authorities, for enemies, for the suffering. **Intercession is one of the highest privileges of the Christian life.**\
\
### **4. Confession (\uc0\u8001 \u956 \u959 \u955 \u959 \u947 \u943 \u945 )**\
\
We will examine this fully in its own section, but it is a major mode of prayer \'97 agreeing with God about our sin.\
\
### **5. Adoration / Worship**\
\
The lifting up of the heart in praise to the Father \'97 which we will examine more fully in the worship section.\
\
### **6. Lament**\
\
The honest expression to the Father of grief, distress, perplexity, even questioning \'97 modeled in the Psalms and by the Son in Gethsemane and on the cross. The believer is not required to pretend to feelings he does not have; he is invited to bring his real state before the Father.\
\
