\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And he spake also a parable unto them, to this end, that they ought always to pray, and not to wax faint,"*\
\
The parable of the persistent widow teaches that the believer is to pray **always** and **not faint.** Some answers require persistent asking over time. The Father is not slow; He is wise \'97 and He uses delayed answers to deepen our dependence.\
\
### **Faith**\
\
### **Mark 11:24 (Greek):**\
*"...\uc0\u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u8005 \u963 \u945  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u949 \u973 \u967 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u945 \u7984 \u964 \u949 \u8150 \u963 \u952 \u949 , \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7952 \u955 \u940 \u946 \u949 \u964 \u949 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"...Whatsoever ye desire when ye pray, believe that ye shall receive it, and it shall be done unto you."*\
\
Prayer is to be offered in faith \'97 trusting the Father's character and promises. Not faith in our prayers, but faith **in the One to whom we pray.**\
\
### **According to His Will**\
\
### **1 John 5:14-15 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u945 \u8021 \u964 \u951  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u8054 \u957  \u7969  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u961 \u951 \u963 \u943 \u945  \u7971 \u957  \u7956 \u967 \u959 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u957 , \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7952 \u940 \u957  \u964 \u953  \u945 \u7984 \u964 \u974 \u956 \u949 \u952 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u8056  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u951 \u956 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 , \u7936 \u954 \u959 \u973 \u949 \u953  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And this is that assurance, that we have in him, that if we ask anything according to his will, he heareth us..."*\
\
Prayer is to be **according to His will.** Not every request is granted \'97 but every request offered in submission to His will is heard. The believer prays *"Thy will be done"* \'97 confident that the Father's will is best, even when His will differs from our preferences.\
\
### **In Jesus' Name**\
\
### **John 14:13-14 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8005  \u964 \u953  \u7938 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u8000 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u943  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u942 \u963 \u969 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u948 \u959 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u8135  \u8001  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u8052 \u961  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u933 \u7985 \u8183 \'b7 \u7952 \u940 \u957  \u964 \u953  \u945 \u7984 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u951 \u964 \u941  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u8000 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u943  \u956 \u959 \u965 , \u7952 \u947 \u8060  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u942 \u963 \u969 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And whatsoever ye ask in my Name, that will I do, that the Father may be glorified in the Son. If ye shall ask any thing in my Name, I will do it."*\
\
Prayer is offered **in Jesus' Name** \'97 that is, on the basis of His person, His mediation, and His authority. Not as a magical formula appended to prayers, but as **the recognition that all access to the Father is through the Son.**\
\
### **With Thanksgiving**\
\
### **Philippians 4:6-7 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u956 \u951 \u948 \u8050 \u957  \u956 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u956 \u957 \u8118 \u964 \u949 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8125  \u7952 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u8054  \u964 \u8135  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u949 \u965 \u967 \u8135  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8135  \u948 \u949 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u8048  \u949 \u8016 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u964 \u8048  \u945 \u7984 \u964 \u942 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u945  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u947 \u957 \u969 \u961 \u953 \u950 \u941 \u963 \u952 \u969  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u957 \'b7 \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7969  \u949 \u7984 \u961 \u942 \u957 \u951  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u7969  \u8017 \u960 \u949 \u961 \u941 \u967 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u945  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u957 \u959 \u8166 \u957  \u966 \u961 \u959 \u965 \u961 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Be nothing careful, but in all things let your requests be showed unto God in prayer, and supplication with giving of thanks. And the peace of God which passeth all understanding, shall preserve your hearts..."*\
\
Prayer with thanksgiving is the antidote to anxiety. The promise: **peace that surpasses understanding will guard the heart.**\
\
---\
\
## **Practical Implications for the Modern Believer**\
\
**1. Establish a regular time of prayer** \'97 daily, ideally in the morning. Not as legalistic duty, but as joyful communion. The believer who waits to "feel like" praying will rarely pray.\
\
**2. Use the Lord's Prayer pattern** \'97 let Jesus' template shape the architecture of your daily prayer. Adoration \uc0\u8594  Kingdom \u8594  Surrender \u8594  Provision \u8594  Confession \u8594  Deliverance.\
\
**3. Pray Scripture back to the Father** \'97 pray through the Psalms, pray through Paul's prayers (Eph 1:15-23; 3:14-21; Phil 1:9-11; Col 1:9-12). Let the Word shape your prayers.\
\
**4. Pray with persistence** \'97 do not abandon prayer when answers delay. The Father uses delay to deepen us.\
\
**5. Pray for others** \'97 keep a list of those for whom you intercede: family, brethren, enemies, rulers, missionaries, the lost.\
\
**6. Pray throughout the day** \'97 *"pray without ceasing"* (1 Thess 5:17) means maintaining a continuous attitude of God-consciousness, with frequent brief turning of the heart to Him.\
\
**7. Pray with thanksgiving** \'97 even in trial, give thanks for what you have received, for who He is, for the hope set before you.\
\
**8. Pray honestly** \'97 bring your real state. The Father does not need pious phrases; He desires the honest heart.\
\
---\
\
# **PART 2 \'97 THE WORD OF GOD: THE RENEWING OF THE MIND**\
\
We established under Romans 12:2 that the believer is transformed **by the renewing of the mind.** The primary instrument of this renewal is **the Word of God** applied by the Spirit.\
\
## **The Nature of Scripture**\
\
### **2 Timothy 3:16-17 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u960 \u8118 \u963 \u945  \u947 \u961 \u945 \u966 \u8052  \u952 \u949 \u972 \u960 \u957 \u949 \u965 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8032 \u966 \u941 \u955 \u953 \u956 \u959 \u962  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u948 \u953 \u948 \u945 \u963 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u943 \u945 \u957 , \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u7952 \u955 \u949 \u947 \u956 \u972 \u957 , \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u7952 \u960 \u945 \u957 \u972 \u961 \u952 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957 , \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u953 \u948 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u959 \u963 \u973 \u957 \u8131 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u7940 \u961 \u964 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u8086  \u8001  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962 , \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u960 \u8118 \u957  \u7956 \u961 \u947 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u952 \u8056 \u957  \u7952 \u958 \u951 \u961 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u959 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For the whole Scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable to teach, to convince, to correct, and to instruct in righteousness, That the man of God may be absolute, being made perfect unto all good works."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations of foundational importance\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u952 \u949 \u972 \u960 \u957 \u949 \u965 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"God-breathed."* Scripture is the very breath of God \'97 proceeding from Him as our own breath proceeds from us. This single word establishes the divine origin and authority of the Word.\
\
**(2) Four practical uses:**\
- **\uc0\u948 \u953 \u948 \u945 \u963 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u943 \u945 \u957 ** \'97 *teaching* (showing what is true).\
- **\uc0\u7952 \u955 \u949 \u947 \u956 \u972 \u957 ** \'97 *convicting / reproof* (showing what is wrong).\
- **\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u945 \u957 \u972 \u961 \u952 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957 ** \'97 *correction / setting straight* (showing how to get right).\
- **\uc0\u960 \u945 \u953 \u948 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u959 \u963 \u973 \u957 \u8131 ** \'97 *training in righteousness* (showing how to stay right).\
\
**The Word makes the believer complete** \'97 **\uc0\u7940 \u961 \u964 \u953 \u959 \u962 ** (*fit, complete, fitted*) \'97 equipped for every good work.\
\
---\
\
## **The Word's Active Power**\
\
### **Hebrews 4:12 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u918 \u8182 \u957  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957 \u949 \u961 \u947 \u8052 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u956 \u974 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u959 \u962  \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u960 \u8118 \u963 \u945 \u957  \u956 \u940 \u967 \u945 \u953 \u961 \u945 \u957  \u948 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u956 \u959 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u948 \u953 \u970 \u954 \u957 \u959 \u973 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u7940 \u967 \u961 \u953  \u956 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u8166  \u968 \u965 \u967 \u8134 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u7937 \u961 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u949  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u956 \u965 \u949 \u955 \u8182 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u954 \u961 \u953 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8056 \u962  \u7952 \u957 \u952 \u965 \u956 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957 \u957 \u959 \u953 \u8182 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u945 \u962 \'b7"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For the word of God is lively, and mighty in operation, and sharper than any two edged sword, and entereth through, even unto the dividing asunder of the soul and the spirit, and of the joints, and the marrow, and is a discerner of the thoughts, and the intents of the heart."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
The Word of God is **\uc0\u950 \u8182 \u957 ** (*living*) \'97 alive, active, not merely a printed text. It is **\u7952 \u957 \u949 \u961 \u947 \u942 \u962 ** (*energetically working*) \'97 accomplishing what God sends it to do. It penetrates beyond the surface to **discern thoughts and intents** of the heart.\
\
This is why the Word renews the mind. The Spirit uses the living Word to penetrate, expose, instruct, and transform.\
\
---\
\
## **The Modes of Engaging the Word**\
\
### **1. Reading**\
\
The believer should read the Word regularly \'97 substantial portions, not merely scattered verses. The whole counsel of God comes through engagement with the whole text.\
\
### **2. Hearing**\
\
### **Romans 10:17 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u7940 \u961 \u945  \u7969  \u960 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u962  \u7952 \u958  \u7936 \u954 \u959 \u8134 \u962 , \u7969  \u948 \u8050  \u7936 \u954 \u959 \u8052  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u8165 \u942 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Then faith is by hearing, and hearing by the word of God."*\
\
Faith comes by hearing the Word. The believer benefits from preaching, teaching, and the audible reading of Scripture \'97 both privately (reading aloud) and corporately (in the assembly).\
\
### **3. Meditating**\
\
### **Psalm 1:1-2 LXX (Ps 1:1-2 MT):**\
*"\uc0\u924 \u945 \u954 \u940 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u7936 \u957 \u942 \u961 ... \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8125  \u7970  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u8179  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u964 \u8056  \u952 \u941 \u955 \u951 \u956 \u945  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u957 \u972 \u956 \u8179  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u956 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u7969 \u956 \u941 \u961 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u957 \u965 \u954 \u964 \u972 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Blessed is the man... But his delight is in the Law of the Lord, and in his Law doth he meditate day and night."*\
\
**\uc0\u956 \u949 \u955 \u949 \u964 \u940 \u969 ** \'97 to meditate, ponder, chew over, mutter to oneself. **The blessed man meditates on the Law day and night.** Meditation is the slow, deliberate pondering of a text \'97 turning it over, asking what it means, applying it to one's life, allowing it to penetrate.\
\
### **4. Memorizing**\
\
### **Psalm 118:11 LXX (Ps 119:11 MT):**\
*"\uc0\u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u8115  \u956 \u959 \u965  \u7956 \u954 \u961 \u965 \u968 \u945  \u964 \u8048  \u955 \u972 \u947 \u953 \u940  \u963 \u959 \u965 , \u8005 \u960 \u969 \u962  \u7938 \u957  \u956 \u8052  \u7937 \u956 \u940 \u961 \u964 \u969  \u963 \u959 \u953 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"I have hid thy promise in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee."*\
\
The Word hidden in the heart guards against sin. Memorized Scripture becomes available to the Spirit's recall in moments of temptation, trial, and decision.\
\
### **5. Studying**\
\
The serious examination of Scripture \'97 comparing passage with passage, examining the Greek and Hebrew where helpful, considering context. Per our maxims, this is the discipline of letting Scripture interpret itself by two or more witnesses.\
\
### **6. Applying / Obeying**\
\
### **James 1:22-25 (Greek, selections):**\
*"\uc0\u915 \u943 \u957 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u948 \u8050  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u951 \u964 \u945 \u8054  \u955 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u956 \u8052  \u956 \u972 \u957 \u959 \u957  \u7936 \u954 \u961 \u959 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u955 \u959 \u947 \u953 \u950 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u953  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u973 \u962 ..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves..."*\
\
The Word is given **to be done**, not merely heard. The believer who hears but does not do **deceives himself.** The renewing of the mind issues in renewed living.\
\
---\
\
## **Practical Implications**\
\
**1. Establish a regular reading plan** \'97 daily, substantial portions. Many find systematic reading through the entire Bible over a year or two beneficial.\
\
**2. Meditate on key passages** \'97 slow down. Read less, think more. Let the Spirit illuminate.\
\
**3. Memorize strategic passages** \'97 psalms, key NT verses on identification with Christ, promises, exhortations.\
\
**4. Study with the LXX where you are able** \'97 per our maxims, this is the text Jesus and the Apostles used.\
\
**5. Apply what you read** \'97 ask: what does this mean? what does it require? how does it call me to walk?\
\
**6. Read in community** \'97 the Word is read in the assembly, and small-group study deepens understanding.\
\
**7. Pray Scripture** \'97 let the Word shape your prayers. The Psalms are especially helpful.\
\
**8. Beware of substituting commentary for text** \'97 read the Bible itself first. Commentaries can help, but they are servants of the text, not replacements for it.\
\
---\
\
# **PART 3 \'97 WORSHIP AND PRAISE**\
\
Worship is the believer's response of adoration to the Father, through the Son, in the Spirit. It is both an inward attitude and outward expression.\
\
## **The Foundation: Worship in Spirit and Truth**\
\
### **John 4:23-24 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u7956 \u961 \u967 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u8037 \u961 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u957 \u8166 \u957  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957 , \u8005 \u964 \u949  \u959 \u7985  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u953 \u957 \u959 \u8054  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u954 \u965 \u957 \u951 \u964 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u954 \u965 \u957 \u942 \u963 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u8054  \u7952 \u957  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u949 \u943 \u8115 \'b7 \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u8001  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u8052 \u961  \u964 \u959 \u953 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u950 \u951 \u964 \u949 \u8150  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u954 \u965 \u957 \u959 \u8166 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u972 \u957 . \u928 \u957 \u949 \u8166 \u956 \u945  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u954 \u965 \u957 \u959 \u8166 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7936 \u955 \u951 \u952 \u949 \u943 \u8115  \u948 \u949 \u8150  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u954 \u965 \u957 \u949 \u8150 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"But the hour cometh, and now is, when the true worshippers shall worship the Father in spirit, and truth: for the Father requireth even such to worship him. God is a Spirit, and they that worship him, must worship him in spirit and truth."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
We already examined this passage extensively under Part E (the Father as Eternal Spirit). Let us now note its implications for worship:\
\
**(1) Worship is to the Father.** Jesus identifies the Father as the recipient of true worship. This honors our foundation.\
\
**(2) Worship is in Spirit and truth.**\
- **In Spirit** \'97 in the believer's regenerated spirit, indwelt by the Holy Spirit, not merely outward observance.\
- **In truth** \'97 in conformity with the truth God has revealed, not in falsehood or self-invented worship.\
\
**(3) The Father seeks such worshippers.** The Father is not indifferent. He **seeks** those who worship Him truly.\
\
---\
\
## **The Sacrifice of Praise**\
\
### **Hebrews 13:15 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u916 \u953 \u8125  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u7936 \u957 \u945 \u966 \u941 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u952 \u965 \u963 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u945 \u7984 \u957 \u941 \u963 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u948 \u953 \u8048  \u960 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 , \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u8125  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u960 \u8056 \u957  \u967 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u941 \u969 \u957  \u8001 \u956 \u959 \u955 \u959 \u947 \u959 \u973 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u8000 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Let us therefore by him offer the sacrifice of praise always to God, that is the fruit of the lips, which confess his Name."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
Praise is **a sacrifice** \'97 offered **through Him** (the Son) **to God** (the Father). The "fruit of the lips" confessing His Name is acceptable to the Father through the Son.\
\
This is the new covenant fulfillment of the OT sacrificial system: not animals on an altar, but praise from the heart of the redeemed, offered through the Mediator.\
\
---\
\
## **The Modes of Worship**\
\
### **Ephesians 5:18-20 (Greek):**\
*"...\uc0\u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u960 \u955 \u951 \u961 \u959 \u8166 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 , \u955 \u945 \u955 \u959 \u8166 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u968 \u945 \u955 \u956 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8021 \u956 \u957 \u959 \u953 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8096 \u948 \u945 \u8150 \u962  \u960 \u957 \u949 \u965 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u8150 \u962 , \u8068 \u948 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u968 \u940 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u964 \u8135  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u8115  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179 , \u949 \u8016 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u964 \u949  \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u969 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u8000 \u957 \u972 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u943 ,"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"...but be filled with the Spirit, Speaking unto yourselves in psalms, and hymns, and spiritual songs, singing, and making melody to the Lord in your hearts, Giving thanks always for all things unto God even the Father, in the Name of our Lord Jesus Christ,"*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1) Worship is a fruit of being filled with the Spirit.** The Spirit-filled believer naturally speaks in spiritual songs, sings, gives thanks.\
\
**(2) Three categories of song:**\
- **\uc0\u968 \u945 \u955 \u956 \u959 \u943 ** \'97 psalms (the OT Psalter).\
- **\uc0\u8021 \u956 \u957 \u959 \u953 ** \'97 hymns (compositions of praise).\
- **\uc0\u8096 \u948 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u957 \u949 \u965 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u943 ** \'97 spiritual songs (Spirit-prompted songs).\
\
**(3) Singing is to the Lord \'97 in the heart.** External singing is the overflow of internal melody. **The heart sings first; the lips follow.**\
\
**(4) Thanksgiving in all things, in His Name, to the Father.** The pattern again: **through the Son, to the Father.**\
\
---\
\
## **Worship in Daily Life**\
\
Worship is not confined to formal services. The whole of life is worship, as Romans 12:1 established. But there are particular acts of worship:\
\
- **Daily morning thanksgiving** \'97 beginning the day with adoration.\
- **Singing throughout the day** \'97 psalms, hymns, spiritual songs as the Spirit prompts.\
- **Acknowledging God in all decisions** \'97 *"In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths"* (Prov 3:6 Geneva).\
- **Gathering with the saints** \'97 corporate worship in the assembly.\
- **The Lord's Supper** \'97 the great act of remembering and communing.\
- **Acts of service** \'97 service rendered to others as worship to the Father.\
\
---\
\
# **PART 4 \'97 FELLOWSHIP WITH THE SAINTS**\
\
The believer is not designed for isolation. The Father has placed him in the Body of Christ, where he both ministers to others and is ministered to.\
\
## **The Foundation: We Belong to One Another**\
\
### **Romans 12:5 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u959 \u8021 \u964 \u969 \u962  \u959 \u7985  \u960 \u959 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u8054  \u7955 \u957  \u963 \u8182 \u956 \u940  \u7952 \u963 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183 , \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u8050  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8125  \u949 \u7991 \u962  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u942 \u955 \u969 \u957  \u956 \u941 \u955 \u951 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"So we being many, are one body in Christ, and every one, one another's members."*\
\
The believer is **a member of the Body** \'97 and **members of one another.** The body image insists on mutual interdependence.\
\
---\
\
## **The Necessity of Assembling**\
\
### **Hebrews 10:24-25 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u8182 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u942 \u955 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u959 \u958 \u965 \u963 \u956 \u8056 \u957  \u7936 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u954 \u945 \u955 \u8182 \u957  \u7956 \u961 \u947 \u969 \u957 , \u956 \u8052  \u7952 \u947 \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u955 \u949 \u943 \u960 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u960 \u953 \u963 \u965 \u957 \u945 \u947 \u969 \u947 \u8052 \u957  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u8182 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u7956 \u952 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u953 \u963 \u943 \u957 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u945 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u959 \u8166 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u963 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u8179  \u956 \u8118 \u955 \u955 \u959 \u957  \u8005 \u963 \u8179  \u946 \u955 \u941 \u960 \u949 \u964 \u949  \u7952 \u947 \u947 \u943 \u950 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u945 \u957  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7969 \u956 \u941 \u961 \u945 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"And let us consider one another, to provoke unto love, and to good works, Not forsaking the fellowship that we have among ourselves, as the manner of some is: but let us exhort one another, and that so much the more, because ye see that the day draweth near."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1)** The believers are to **consider one another** \'97 paying attention to one another's needs.\
\
**(2)** The purpose is **to stir up love and good works** \'97 to provoke one another (\uc0\u960 \u945 \u961 \u959 \u958 \u965 \u963 \u956 \u972 \u962  \'97 a sharp stirring up) toward what is good.\
\
**(3) Negative command:** *"Not forsaking the assembling of ourselves together."* Some were already abandoning the gathering. The author warns against this.\
\
**(4) Positive command:** *"Exhorting one another."* The believers are to encourage and admonish one another.\
\
**(5) Urgency:** *"As ye see the day approaching."* The Lord's return makes faithful gathering more urgent, not less.\
\
---\
\
## **The "One Another" Commands**\
\
The NT contains over fifty "one another" commands \'97 instructions for how believers are to relate to one another in the Body. Major examples:\
\
- **Love one another** (John 13:34; Rom 12:10; 13:8; 1 Thess 4:9; 1 Pet 1:22; 1 John 3:11, 23; 4:7, 11-12).\
- **Forgive one another** (Eph 4:32; Col 3:13).\
- **Bear with one another** (Eph 4:2; Col 3:13).\
- **Bear one another's burdens** (Gal 6:2).\
- **Comfort one another** (1 Thess 4:18; 5:11).\
- **Encourage / exhort one another** (1 Thess 5:11; Heb 3:13; 10:25).\
- **Build up one another** (Rom 14:19; 1 Thess 5:11).\
- **Serve one another** (Gal 5:13; 1 Pet 4:10).\
- **Submit to one another** (Eph 5:21; 1 Pet 5:5).\
- **Honor one another** (Rom 12:10).\
- **Be hospitable to one another** (1 Pet 4:9).\
- **Pray for one another** (James 5:16).\
- **Confess sins to one another** (James 5:16).\
- **Teach and admonish one another** (Col 3:16).\
- **Greet one another** (Rom 16:16; 1 Cor 16:20; 2 Cor 13:12; 1 Pet 5:14).\
- **Do not bite and devour one another** (Gal 5:15).\
- **Do not lie to one another** (Col 3:9).\
- **Do not speak evil of one another** (James 4:11).\
\
**This is the texture of biblical fellowship.** Christianity is not a solitary pursuit; it is a body life.\
\
---\
\
## **Practical Implications**\
\
**1. Be committed to a local assembly.** The believer needs the regular gathering of the saints \'97 for teaching, worship, fellowship, the Lord's Supper, prayer, and mutual encouragement.\
\
**2. Develop deep relationships with a few fellow believers** \'97 those with whom you can pray, confess sin, bear burdens, exhort.\
\
**3. Use your gifts to serve the Body** \'97 every believer has gifts (Rom 12; 1 Cor 12; Eph 4; 1 Pet 4:10-11). Discover yours and use them.\
\
**4. Be a source of encouragement.** In a world of discouragement, the believer who consistently encourages is a deep gift to the Body.\
\
**5. Bear with weaknesses.** Every believer has weaknesses, immaturities, and failures. Bear with one another in patience.\
\
**6. Resist factionalism, gossip, and divisive speech.** These are the work of the flesh and destroy the Body's unity.\
\
**7. Submit to godly leaders** (Heb 13:17). The Father has appointed shepherds for the flock; submit to their oversight as those who watch for your souls.\
\
---\
\
# **PART 5 \'97 THE LORD'S SUPPER**\
\
The Lord's Supper is the appointed act of remembrance and communion that the Lord Himself instituted on the night of His betrayal.\
\
## **The Institution**\
\
### **1 Corinthians 11:23-26 (Greek):**\
*"...\uc0\u8001  \u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u962  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8135  \u957 \u965 \u954 \u964 \u8054  \u8087  \u960 \u945 \u961 \u949 \u948 \u943 \u948 \u949 \u964 \u959  \u7956 \u955 \u945 \u946 \u949 \u957  \u7940 \u961 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u949 \u8016 \u967 \u945 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u962  \u7956 \u954 \u955 \u945 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u949 \u7990 \u960 \u949 \u957 \'b7 \u932 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u972  \u956 \u959 \u973  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u964 \u8056  \u963 \u8182 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8056  \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957 \'b7 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u8052 \u957  \u7936 \u957 \u940 \u956 \u957 \u951 \u963 \u953 \u957 . \u8033 \u963 \u945 \u973 \u964 \u969 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u959 \u964 \u942 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u956 \u949 \u964 \u8048  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u949 \u953 \u960 \u957 \u8134 \u963 \u945 \u953  \u955 \u941 \u947 \u969 \u957 \'b7 \u932 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u959 \u964 \u942 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u7969  \u954 \u945 \u953 \u957 \u8052  \u948 \u953 \u945 \u952 \u942 \u954 \u951  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u8054 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u7952 \u956 \u8183  \u945 \u7989 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \'b7 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u949 \u8150 \u964 \u949 , \u8001 \u963 \u940 \u954 \u953 \u962  \u7952 \u8048 \u957  \u960 \u943 \u957 \u951 \u964 \u949 , \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u8052 \u957  \u7936 \u957 \u940 \u956 \u957 \u951 \u963 \u953 \u957 . \u8001 \u963 \u940 \u954 \u953 \u962  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7952 \u8048 \u957  \u7952 \u963 \u952 \u943 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7940 \u961 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u959 \u964 \u942 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u960 \u943 \u957 \u951 \u964 \u949 , \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u952 \u940 \u957 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u947 \u947 \u941 \u955 \u955 \u949 \u964 \u949 , \u7940 \u967 \u961 \u953  \u959 \u8023  \u7956 \u955 \u952 \u8131 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"...That the Lord Jesus in the night when he was betrayed, took bread: And when he had given thanks, he brake it, and said, Take, eat: this is my body, which is broken for you: this do ye in remembrance of me. After the same manner also he took the cup, when he had supped, saying, This cup is the New Testament in my blood: this do as oft as ye drink it, in remembrance of me. For as often as ye shall eat this bread, and drink this cup, ye show the Lord's death till he come."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1) Three elements:**\
- **The Bread** \'97 representing His body **broken for us.**\
- **The Cup** \'97 representing **the New Covenant in His blood.**\
- **The Remembrance** \'97 *"in remembrance of Me"* (\uc0\u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7952 \u956 \u8052 \u957  \u7936 \u957 \u940 \u956 \u957 \u951 \u963 \u953 \u957 ).\
\
**(2) The proclamation** \'97 *"you show the Lord's death till He come."* The Supper is both a remembrance of the past (His death) and a proclamation toward the future (until He comes).\
\
**(3) The frequency** \'97 *"as often as you drink it."* The NT does not prescribe a specific frequency. The early church appears to have observed it frequently \'97 perhaps weekly (Acts 20:7).\
\
---\
\
## **The Self-Examination**\
\
### **1 Corinthians 11:27-29 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u8045 \u963 \u964 \u949  \u8003 \u962  \u7938 \u957  \u7952 \u963 \u952 \u943 \u8131  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7940 \u961 \u964 \u959 \u957  \u7970  \u960 \u943 \u957 \u8131  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u959 \u964 \u942 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u7936 \u957 \u945 \u958 \u943 \u969 \u962 , \u7956 \u957 \u959 \u967 \u959 \u962  \u7956 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u963 \u974 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u945 \u7989 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965 . \u948 \u959 \u954 \u953 \u956 \u945 \u950 \u941 \u964 \u969  \u948 \u8050  \u7940 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u969 \u960 \u959 \u962  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u972 \u957 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u959 \u8021 \u964 \u969 \u962  \u7952 \u954  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7940 \u961 \u964 \u959 \u965  \u7952 \u963 \u952 \u953 \u941 \u964 \u969  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u954  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u960 \u959 \u964 \u951 \u961 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u960 \u953 \u957 \u941 \u964 \u969 \'b7 \u8001  \u947 \u8048 \u961  \u7952 \u963 \u952 \u943 \u969 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u943 \u957 \u969 \u957  \u954 \u961 \u943 \u956 \u945  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u8183  \u7952 \u963 \u952 \u943 \u949 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u960 \u943 \u957 \u949 \u953  \u956 \u8052  \u948 \u953 \u945 \u954 \u961 \u943 \u957 \u969 \u957  \u964 \u8056  \u963 \u8182 \u956 \u945 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Wherefore whosoever shall eat this bread, and drink the cup of the Lord unworthily, shall be guilty of the body and blood of the Lord. Let every man therefore examine himself, and so let him eat of this bread, and drink of this cup. For he that eateth and drinketh unworthily, eateth and drinketh his own damnation, because he discerneth not the Lord's body."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1) Self-examination is commanded** \'97 **\uc0\u948 \u959 \u954 \u953 \u956 \u945 \u950 \u941 \u964 \u969  \u7953 \u945 \u965 \u964 \u972 \u957 ** \'97 *"let a man examine himself."* Before partaking, the believer is to examine his own heart.\
\
**(2) Eating unworthily** is the danger \'97 not because the believer is worthy in himself (none are), but because **the manner** of partaking can be unworthy \'97 without faith, without discernment, in unconfessed sin, in division from the brethren.\
\
**(3) Discerning the body** \'97 recognizing the significance of the broken body of the Lord, and (in context of 1 Cor 11) recognizing the Body of Christ which is the Church (the Corinthians were divided and treating one another shamefully at the Supper).\
\
---\
\
## **Practical Implications**\
\
**1. Approach the Supper with reverence.** It is not a casual meal but a sacred remembrance.\
\
**2. Examine yourself before partaking.** Confess known sin. Reconcile with brethren. Come with faith.\
\
**3. Use the Supper as an occasion of fresh consecration.** Each remembrance is an opportunity to renew your dedication to the One who died for you.\
\
**4. Look both backward and forward.** Backward to His death; forward to His return.\
\
**5. Recognize the Body.** The Supper is a corporate act \'97 celebrated with the Body of Christ.\
\
---\
