# **PART 6 \'97 WATCHFULNESS AND RESISTANCE OF TEMPTATION**\
\
The believer is in spiritual conflict. The Christian life requires vigilance.\
\
## **The Reality of the Conflict**\
\
### **1 Peter 5:8-9 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u925 \u942 \u968 \u945 \u964 \u949 , \u947 \u961 \u951 \u947 \u959 \u961 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u949 . \u8001  \u7936 \u957 \u964 \u943 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u959 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u948 \u953 \u940 \u946 \u959 \u955 \u959 \u962  \u8033 \u962  \u955 \u941 \u969 \u957  \u8032 \u961 \u965 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u962  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u945 \u964 \u949 \u8150  \u950 \u951 \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u953 \u957 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u945 \u960 \u953 \u949 \u8150 \u957 \'b7 \u8103  \u7936 \u957 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u963 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u949 \u959 \u8054  \u964 \u8135  \u960 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u953 ..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Be sober, and watch: for your adversary the devil as a roaring lion walketh about, seeking whom he may devour: Whom resist steadfast in the faith..."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1) Two commands:** **be sober** (\uc0\u957 \u942 \u968 \u945 \u964 \u949  \'97 clear-minded, self-controlled) and **watch** (\u947 \u961 \u951 \u947 \u959 \u961 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u949  \'97 alert, vigilant).\
\
**(2) The adversary is real** \'97 the devil prowls like a roaring lion seeking prey.\
\
**(3) The response: resist him steadfast in the faith.** The believer **resists** \'97 does not flee or surrender. The resistance is **in the faith** \'97 grounded in the truths of who Christ is and who the believer is in Him.\
\
---\
\
## **The Armor of God**\
\
### **Ephesians 6:10-18 (Greek, selections):**\
*"\uc0\u932 \u959 \u8166  \u955 \u959 \u953 \u960 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u957 \u948 \u965 \u957 \u945 \u956 \u959 \u8166 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u922 \u965 \u961 \u943 \u8179  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u954 \u961 \u940 \u964 \u949 \u953  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7984 \u963 \u967 \u973 \u959 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166 . \u7952 \u957 \u948 \u973 \u963 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u960 \u955 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u920 \u949 \u959 \u8166  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u945 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u963 \u964 \u8134 \u957 \u945 \u953  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u956 \u949 \u952 \u959 \u948 \u949 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u948 \u953 \u945 \u946 \u972 \u955 \u959 \u965 ..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might. Put on the whole armor of God, that ye may be able to stand against the assaults of the devil..."*\
\
The full armor:\
- **Belt of truth** (v. 14).\
- **Breastplate of righteousness** (v. 14).\
- **Feet shod with the preparation of the Gospel of peace** (v. 15).\
- **Shield of faith** (v. 16).\
- **Helmet of salvation** (v. 17).\
- **Sword of the Spirit, which is the Word of God** (v. 17).\
- **All prayer and supplication in the Spirit** (v. 18).\
\
The believer is to **put on** the full armor and **stand.**\
\
---\
\
## **Resisting Temptation**\
\
### **James 4:7 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u8017 \u960 \u959 \u964 \u940 \u947 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u920 \u949 \u8183 \'b7 \u7936 \u957 \u964 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u948 \u8050  \u964 \u8183  \u948 \u953 \u945 \u946 \u972 \u955 \u8179 , \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u966 \u949 \u973 \u958 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u7936 \u966 \u8125  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Submit yourselves to God: resist the devil, and he will flee from you."*\
\
**Two commands in order:**\
1. **Submit to God.**\
2. **Resist the devil.**\
\
The order matters. Submission to God is the foundation; resistance to the devil is the result. **The believer who submits to God can resist the devil; the devil will flee.**\
\
### **1 Corinthians 10:13 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u960 \u949 \u953 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u956 \u8056 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u949 \u7988 \u955 \u951 \u966 \u949 \u957  \u949 \u7984  \u956 \u8052  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u953 \u957 \u959 \u962 \'b7 \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 , \u8003 \u962  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7952 \u940 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u960 \u949 \u953 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u8134 \u957 \u945 \u953  \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u8003  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u949 , \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u8048  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u942 \u963 \u949 \u953  \u963 \u8058 \u957  \u964 \u8183  \u960 \u949 \u953 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u956 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u8052 \u957  \u7956 \u954 \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u948 \u973 \u957 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u945 \u953  \u8017 \u960 \u949 \u957 \u949 \u947 \u954 \u949 \u8150 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"There hath no temptation taken you, but such as appertaineth to man: and God is faithful, which will not suffer you to be tempted above that you be able: but will even give the issue with the temptation, that ye may be able to bear it."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1) Temptation is common to humanity** \'97 no temptation is unique or unprecedented.\
\
**(2) God is faithful** \'97 He will not allow temptation beyond your ability to bear.\
\
**(3) He provides the way of escape** \'97 *"\uc0\u7956 \u954 \u946 \u945 \u963 \u953 \u962 "* \'97 the exit. With every temptation, the Father provides a way out, that the believer may be able to bear it.\
\
The believer's responsibility is to **look for the way of escape** and **take it.**\
\
---\
\
## **Practical Implications**\
\
**1. Be alert.** Recognize you are in conflict. The devil seeks to devour. Be watchful.\
\
**2. Put on the armor daily.** Through prayer, Scripture, and conscious dependence on the Lord, equip yourself for battle.\
\
**3. Flee youthful lusts** (2 Tim 2:22). Some temptations are to be resisted; others are to be fled. Sexual temptation, especially, is to be fled. Joseph fled Potiphar's wife (Gen 39:12). The believer does not stay to debate temptation; he flees.\
\
**4. Look for the way of escape.** When temptation comes, ask: *"Father, show me the way of escape."* And then take it.\
\
**5. Submit before resisting.** Submission to God precedes resistance to the devil.\
\
**6. Be especially watchful in seasons of weakness** \'97 fatigue, hunger, isolation, success (which can produce pride), failure (which can produce despair).\
\
**7. Have accountability partners.** Other believers who will ask hard questions and pray with you in your struggles.\
\
---\
\
# **PART 7 \'97 CONFESSION OF SIN**\
\
The believer is not sinless. Failure occurs. The discipline of confession is the means by which fellowship with the Father is maintained.\
\
## **The Foundation: 1 John 1:9**\
\
### **Greek:**\
*"\uc0\u7952 \u8048 \u957  \u8001 \u956 \u959 \u955 \u959 \u947 \u8182 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u7969 \u956 \u8182 \u957 , \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u972 \u962  \u7952 \u963 \u964 \u953 \u957  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u948 \u943 \u954 \u945 \u953 \u959 \u962 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u7936 \u966 \u8135  \u7969 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u8131  \u7969 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u7936 \u960 \u8056  \u960 \u940 \u963 \u951 \u962  \u7936 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u943 \u945 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"If we acknowledge our sins, he is faithful and just, to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1)** **\uc0\u8001 \u956 \u959 \u955 \u959 \u947 \u8182 \u956 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *"confess"* \'97 literally *"to say the same thing"* (\u8001 \u956 \u972  + \u955 \u941 \u947 \u969 ). To confess sin is to **agree with God about it** \'97 naming it for what He calls it, not minimizing or excusing.\
\
**(2)** The promise is twofold:\
- **\uc0\u7936 \u966 \u8135 ** \'97 *forgive* \'97 the legal release from the debt of sin.\
- **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u952 \u945 \u961 \u943 \u963 \u8131 ** \'97 *cleanse* \'97 the removal of the stain from the conscience and life.\
\
**(3) The basis** \'97 *"He is faithful and just."* Forgiveness is not because God is sentimental or lenient, but because **He is faithful to His promise** and **just toward the propitiation Christ made.**\
\
---\
\
## **The Distinction: Position vs. Fellowship**\
\
A vital theological distinction must be held:\
\
**Positionally**, the believer's sins \'97 past, present, and future \'97 were dealt with at the cross. He is forgiven, justified, accepted in the Beloved. This is not undone by daily sin.\
\
**Practically (in fellowship)**, daily sin grieves the indwelling Spirit (Eph 4:30) and disrupts the believer's experiential communion with the Father. Confession restores the experiential fellowship.\
\
**1 John 1:9 addresses the practical/fellowship dimension** \'97 the believer's daily walk, his conscience, his communion. The position is secure; the fellowship requires confession.\
\
---\
\
## **The Pattern of Daily Confession**\
\
The believer should make confession a daily, regular practice:\
\
1. **At the close of the day** \'97 review the day before the Lord, confessing known sin.\
2. **At the moment of conviction** \'97 when the Spirit convicts of specific sin, confess immediately.\
3. **Before the Lord's Supper** \'97 self-examination per 1 Cor 11.\
4. **Before significant prayer** \'97 clearing the channels.\
\
---\
\
## **Confession to Other Believers**\
\
### **James 5:16 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u7952 \u958 \u959 \u956 \u959 \u955 \u959 \u947 \u949 \u8150 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u942 \u955 \u959 \u953 \u962  \u964 \u8048 \u962  \u7937 \u956 \u945 \u961 \u964 \u943 \u945 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u949 \u8020 \u967 \u949 \u963 \u952 \u949  \u8017 \u960 \u8050 \u961  \u7936 \u955 \u955 \u942 \u955 \u969 \u957 , \u8005 \u960 \u969 \u962  \u7984 \u945 \u952 \u8134 \u964 \u949 . \u960 \u959 \u955 \u8058  \u7984 \u963 \u967 \u973 \u949 \u953  \u948 \u941 \u951 \u963 \u953 \u962  \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u7952 \u957 \u949 \u961 \u947 \u959 \u965 \u956 \u941 \u957 \u951 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Acknowledge your faults one to another, and pray one for another, that ye may be healed: for the prayer of a righteous man availeth much, if it be fervent."*\
\
---\
\
### Observation\
\
Some sins should be confessed to other trusted believers \'97 for prayer, accountability, and healing. This is not the priestly confessional of Rome (per maxim #3), but the genuine confession of brethren to one another for mutual support.\
\
This is particularly helpful for besetting sins, sins of pride that need to be exposed in humility, or sins against specific persons that require their forgiveness.\
\
---\
\
## **Practical Implications**\
\
**1. Confess sin promptly** \'97 do not let unconfessed sin accumulate.\
\
**2. Be specific in confession** \'97 name the sin clearly, not in vague generalities.\
\
**3. Receive forgiveness by faith** \'97 believe the promise of 1 John 1:9. Do not wallow in self-condemnation after God has forgiven.\
\
**4. Make restitution where required** \'97 confession may need to be accompanied by reconciliation with those wronged.\
\
**5. Confess corporate sin** \'97 sometimes the believer confesses on behalf of his nation, family, or community (as Daniel did in Dan 9).\
\
**6. Do not let the enemy use confession against you** \'97 once forgiven, you are forgiven. The accuser will try to bring back what God has remembered no more.\
\
