# **PART 8 \'97 THE BELIEVER'S RESPONSE TO TRIALS**\
\
The believer encounters varied trials. The Christian's response is distinct from the world's.\
\
## **The General Pattern: Joy in Trial**\
\
### **James 1:2-4 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u928 \u8118 \u963 \u945 \u957  \u967 \u945 \u961 \u8048 \u957  \u7969 \u947 \u942 \u963 \u945 \u963 \u952 \u949 , \u7936 \u948 \u949 \u955 \u966 \u959 \u943  \u956 \u959 \u965 , \u8005 \u964 \u945 \u957  \u960 \u949 \u953 \u961 \u945 \u963 \u956 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u941 \u963 \u951 \u964 \u949  \u960 \u959 \u953 \u954 \u943 \u955 \u959 \u953 \u962 , \u947 \u953 \u957 \u974 \u963 \u954 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u8005 \u964 \u953  \u964 \u8056  \u948 \u959 \u954 \u943 \u956 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u960 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u969 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u949 \u961 \u947 \u940 \u950 \u949 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u8017 \u960 \u959 \u956 \u959 \u957 \u942 \u957 \'b7 \u7969  \u948 \u8050  \u8017 \u960 \u959 \u956 \u959 \u957 \u8052  \u7956 \u961 \u947 \u959 \u957  \u964 \u941 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u7952 \u967 \u941 \u964 \u969 , \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u7974 \u964 \u949  \u964 \u941 \u955 \u949 \u953 \u959 \u953  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u8001 \u955 \u972 \u954 \u955 \u951 \u961 \u959 \u953 , \u7952 \u957  \u956 \u951 \u948 \u949 \u957 \u8054  \u955 \u949 \u953 \u960 \u972 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u953 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"My brethren, count it exceeding joy, when ye fall into divers temptations, Knowing that the trying of your faith bringeth forth patience. And let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, lacking nothing."*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1) Count it all joy** \'97 not because trials are pleasant, but because of what they accomplish.\
\
**(2) Trials produce \uc0\u8017 \u960 \u959 \u956 \u959 \u957 \u942 ** \'97 *patience, endurance, steadfast perseverance.* The believer's character is forged through trial.\
\
**(3) Patience produces maturity** \'97 *"perfect and entire, lacking nothing."*\
\
The believer's response: **joy**, because the Father is using the trial for His perfecting work.\
\
---\
\
## **The Different Kinds of Trials**\
\
### **Persecution for Righteousness**\
\
We examined this fully in our earlier discussion of suffering with Christ. The response: **rejoice** (Matt 5:11-12), **bless** (Rom 12:14), **count it joy** to be counted worthy to suffer for the Name (Acts 5:41).\
\
### **Affliction in the Body**\
\
Illness, weakness, pain, the limitations of mortal life. The response: **trust the Father's purpose**, **seek prayer** (James 5:14-16), **submit to the Father's wisdom**, **endure with hope** of the resurrection (Rom 8:23).\
\
### **Loss and Bereavement**\
\
The death of loved ones, the loss of relationships, the breaking of dear things. The response: **grieve, but not as those without hope** (1 Thess 4:13). Christian grief is real; it is also held within the certainty of resurrection.\
\
### **Economic Hardship**\
\
Job loss, financial pressure, poverty. The response: **trust the Father's provision** (Matt 6:25-34), **work diligently** (2 Thess 3:10-12), **be content** (Phil 4:11-13), **seek the kingdom first** (Matt 6:33).\
\
### **Relational Trials**\
\
Conflict, betrayal, loneliness, marital difficulty. The response: **pray for those who hurt you** (Matt 5:44), **forgive as Christ forgave** (Col 3:13), **seek peace as far as it depends on you** (Rom 12:18), **trust the Lord for outcomes you cannot control.**\
\
### **Inner Trials**\
\
Depression, anxiety, doubt, dryness in prayer. The response: **bring it honestly before the Lord** (the Psalms model this), **rest in His unchanging promises** even when feelings vary, **seek the help of trusted brethren**, **be patient with the slow work of the Spirit in dark seasons.**\
\
### **Temptation**\
\
Already discussed. The response: flee or resist as appropriate; look for the way of escape.\
\
---\
\
## **The Sustaining Truths**\
\
In every trial, the believer holds fast to certain truths:\
\
1. **The Father is sovereign** \'97 nothing reaches you outside His permission.\
2. **The Father is loving** \'97 He does not afflict from caprice or cruelty.\
3. **All things work for good** (Rom 8:28) \'97 even this.\
4. **Christ has been there** \'97 He sympathizes with our weaknesses (Heb 4:15).\
5. **The Spirit indwells** \'97 strengthening, comforting, interceding.\
6. **The trial is temporary** \'97 *"light affliction which is but for a moment"* (2 Cor 4:17).\
7. **The glory is coming** \'97 incomparably greater than the present sufferings (Rom 8:18).\
8. **Nothing separates us from His love** (Rom 8:38-39).\
\
---\
\
## **Practical Implications**\
\
**1. Do not be surprised by trials** (1 Pet 4:12). They are normal in the Christian life.\
\
**2. Bring trials to the Father in prayer.** Do not bear them alone.\
\
**3. Look for the lessons the Father is teaching.** What patience is He growing? What dependence? What conformity to the Son?\
\
**4. Seek the help of the Body.** Bear one another's burdens.\
\
**5. Use the trial as an opportunity to witness.** Many have come to faith through observing Christians under trial.\
\
**6. Keep eternal perspective.** This life is not the end of the story.\
\
**7. Be honest with God in your grief.** The Psalms model this. You do not have to pretend.\
\
---\
\
# **PART 9 \'97 WITNESS AND PROCLAMATION**\
\
The believer is called to bear witness to the Son before the world.\
\
## **The Mandate**\
\
### **Matthew 28:19-20 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u960 \u959 \u961 \u949 \u965 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u956 \u945 \u952 \u951 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u949  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u964 \u8048  \u7956 \u952 \u957 \u951 , \u946 \u945 \u960 \u964 \u943 \u950 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u964 \u8056  \u8004 \u957 \u959 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u933 \u7985 \u959 \u8166  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u7945 \u947 \u943 \u959 \u965  \u928 \u957 \u949 \u973 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u962 , \u948 \u953 \u948 \u940 \u963 \u954 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u964 \u951 \u961 \u949 \u8150 \u957  \u960 \u940 \u957 \u964 \u945  \u8005 \u963 \u945  \u7952 \u957 \u949 \u964 \u949 \u953 \u955 \u940 \u956 \u951 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957 ..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Go therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the Name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the holy Ghost, Teaching them to observe all things, whatsoever I have commanded you..."*\
\
The Great Commission belongs to every believer, in its various spheres of application.\
\
---\
\
## **The Posture of the Witness**\
\
### **1 Peter 3:15 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u922 \u973 \u961 \u953 \u959 \u957  \u948 \u8050  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7937 \u947 \u953 \u940 \u963 \u945 \u964 \u949  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u945 \u8150 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u961 \u948 \u943 \u945 \u953 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957 , \u7957 \u964 \u959 \u953 \u956 \u959 \u953  \u7936 \u949 \u8054  \u960 \u961 \u8056 \u962  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u955 \u959 \u947 \u943 \u945 \u957  \u960 \u945 \u957 \u964 \u8054  \u964 \u8183  \u945 \u7984 \u964 \u959 \u8166 \u957 \u964 \u953  \u8017 \u956 \u8118 \u962  \u955 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u957  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u8054  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8150 \u957  \u7952 \u955 \u960 \u943 \u948 \u959 \u962 , \u956 \u949 \u964 \u8048  \u960 \u961 \u945 \u944 \u964 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u966 \u972 \u946 \u959 \u965 ,"*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"But sanctify the Lord God in your hearts: and be ready always to give an answer to every man that asketh you a reason of the hope that is in you, with meekness and reverence,"*\
\
---\
\
### Observations\
\
**(1) Sanctify the Lord in your hearts** \'97 give Him the place of supremacy first internally. This is the foundation of all witness.\
\
**(2) Be ready** \'97 be prepared to give an answer. The believer should know the Gospel well enough to articulate it.\
\
**(3) For the hope that is in you** \'97 the witness centers on **the hope** \'97 the certain expectation of glory through Christ.\
\
**(4) With meekness and reverence** \'97 not arrogantly, not combatively. The witness is winsome, humble, reverent.\
\
---\
\
## **The Believer's Witness**\
\
The believer witnesses in multiple ways:\
\
### **By Life**\
\
### **Matthew 5:16 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u959 \u8021 \u964 \u969 \u962  \u955 \u945 \u956 \u968 \u940 \u964 \u969  \u964 \u8056  \u966 \u8182 \u962  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u7956 \u956 \u960 \u961 \u959 \u963 \u952 \u949 \u957  \u964 \u8182 \u957  \u7936 \u957 \u952 \u961 \u974 \u960 \u969 \u957 , \u8005 \u960 \u969 \u962  \u7988 \u948 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u8048  \u954 \u945 \u955 \u8048  \u7956 \u961 \u947 \u945  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u948 \u959 \u958 \u940 \u963 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u928 \u945 \u964 \u941 \u961 \u945  \u8017 \u956 \u8182 \u957  \u964 \u8056 \u957  \u7952 \u957  \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u959 \u8016 \u961 \u945 \u957 \u959 \u8150 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven."*\
\
The believer's life \'97 his integrity, his love, his joy in trial, his honesty, his faithfulness \'97 is itself a witness to the world.\
\
### **By Word**\
\
### **Romans 10:14-15 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u928 \u8182 \u962  \u959 \u8022 \u957  \u7952 \u960 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u941 \u963 \u969 \u957 \u964 \u945 \u953  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u8003 \u957  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7952 \u960 \u943 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u965 \u963 \u945 \u957 ; \u960 \u8182 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u960 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u949 \u973 \u963 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u959 \u8023  \u959 \u8016 \u954  \u7972 \u954 \u959 \u965 \u963 \u945 \u957 ; \u960 \u8182 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u7936 \u954 \u959 \u973 \u963 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u967 \u969 \u961 \u8054 \u962  \u954 \u951 \u961 \u973 \u963 \u963 \u959 \u957 \u964 \u959 \u962 ; \u960 \u8182 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u954 \u951 \u961 \u973 \u958 \u969 \u963 \u953 \u957  \u7952 \u8048 \u957  \u956 \u8052  \u7936 \u960 \u959 \u963 \u964 \u945 \u955 \u8182 \u963 \u953 \u957 ;..."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"But how shall they call on him, in whom they have not believed? and how shall they believe in him, of whom they have not heard? and how shall they hear without a preacher? And how shall they preach, except they be sent?..."*\
\
Faith comes by hearing (Rom 10:17). The Gospel must be proclaimed verbally. **Lives alone are insufficient** \'97 the explicit Gospel must be spoken.\
\
### **By Service**\
\
Acts of mercy, compassion, and service open doors for the Gospel and embody it visibly.\
\
---\
\
## **The Content of the Witness**\
\
The Gospel itself \'97 the good news that:\
- The Father loved the world and sent His Beloved Son.\
- The Son died for our sins and rose again the third day.\
- He is now at the Father's right hand, the appointed Lord and Christ.\
- Whoever believes in Him receives forgiveness and eternal life.\
- He will return to judge the living and the dead.\
- All who are in Him are children of God, indwelt by the Spirit, destined for glory.\
\
This is the core. The believer should know how to articulate it briefly and clearly.\
\
---\
\
## **Practical Implications**\
\
**1. Live a life consistent with your message.** Hypocrisy nullifies witness.\
\
**2. Be ready to speak when opportunities arise.** Pray for opportunities; recognize them; take them.\
\
**3. Be honest about your own journey.** Personal testimony is powerful \'97 *"I was blind, now I see"* (John 9:25).\
\
**4. Be patient with the lost.** Conversion is the Father's work; you are a faithful witness.\
\
**5. Pray for the lost.** Especially those near to you \'97 family, neighbors, coworkers.\
\
**6. Support the proclamation of the Gospel** \'97 pray for and give to those engaged in missions and evangelism beyond your immediate reach.\
\
**7. Do not be ashamed of the Gospel** (Rom 1:16). It is the power of God unto salvation.\
\
