Given all the maxims as the governing precepts in our study, does the WORD instruct us to pray to Jesus?\
\
\
This is a piercingly important question, and it strikes at the very heart of our maxims. Let me address it with the utmost honesty and rigor, letting the whole counsel of the God-breathed Word speak \'97 being unflinching where Scripture is clear, and honest where Scripture is more nuanced.\
\
Per maxim #1, **we let God be true and every man a liar** \'97 including every man's inherited tradition on this question. Per maxim #2, **we let every doctrinal point be established by two or more witnesses.** Per maxim #3, **we ignore ensuing ideas from Babylonian Talmudic Rabbis and Early Church Fathers.**\
\
Let us proceed.\
\
