**(2) Note the immediate context:** In Acts 7:55-56, Stephen **sees the heavens opened and the Son of Man standing at the right hand of God.** He is having a direct vision of the risen Christ. This is not ordinary prayer; it is speech to the visibly-appearing Lord standing before him.\
\
**(3)** The Geneva translation begins: *"who called on God, and said, Lord Jesus, receive my spirit."* This may reflect an attempt to preserve the pattern of "calling on God" while acknowledging the address to Jesus. The Greek **\uc0\u7952 \u960 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u955 \u959 \u973 \u956 \u949 \u957 \u959 \u957 ** simply means *"calling on / invoking."*\
