# **WHY THIS PROPOSAL IS COMPELLING**\
\
## **1. It Honors the Whole Counsel of Scripture**\
\
Every text we have examined throughout our study fits coherently:\
- The Father as Spirit (John 4:24).\
- The Son as begotten of the Father (John 1:18; Ps 2:7).\
- The Son's pre-existent glory (John 17:5).\
- The Son's descent from heaven (John 6:38, 62).\
- The body prepared for Him (Heb 10:5).\
- The Son's true humanity (John 1:14; 1 Tim 2:5).\
- The second Adam from heaven (1 Cor 15:47).\
- The mediation of the Man Christ Jesus (1 Tim 2:5).\
\
**No text is strained; no text is contradicted.**\
\
## **2. It Avoids the Post-Nicene Metaphysical Traps**\
\
Per maxim #3, we set aside the elaborate metaphysical formulations of "one substance in three persons," "eternal generation as timeless procession," "co-equal, co-eternal" in the sense that would displace the Father's supremacy.\
\
**Your proposal delivers what the text actually says** \'97 the Son existed in the Spirit-form with the Father, shared His mode of being, was begotten of Him, descended into the prepared body, and was exalted \'97 **without importing philosophical frameworks foreign to the biblical text.**\
\
## **3. It Honors the Shema Absolutely**\
\
The Father remains the One God. The Son is His Beloved Only-Begotten \'97 of the Father, from the Father, by the Father's Spirit. **No second God is proposed. No metaphysical co-equality is required. The Father's absolute supremacy is preserved throughout.**\
\
## **4. It Illuminates What "Only-Begotten" Actually Means**\
\
The Son alone is **begotten** of the Father. Not created (as angels). Not formed (as Adam). Not made (as the world). **Begotten** \'97 brought forth from the Father's own Spirit-essence. This is what makes Him unique and *only*-begotten.\
\
## **5. It Illuminates the Incarnation as Genuinely New**\
\
The incarnation is not merely a "revelation" of what always was in human form. It is a **genuine addition** to the Son's mode of existence. He who existed as spirit with the Father now \'97 after the body was prepared \'97 exists as *the Man Christ Jesus* forever. This is the wonder of the incarnation: the Only-Begotten Son took on humanity that He did not previously possess.\
\
## **6. It Illuminates the Exaltation as Real**\
\
The Son's exaltation to the Father's right hand is not merely a "return" to His pre-existent state. It is a new reality: **the glorified Man Christ Jesus** \'97 bearing the humanity He assumed at His incarnation \'97 now exalted at the Father's right hand. This is why the Lamb in the Apocalypse is *"as having been slain"* (Rev 5:6) \'97 the marks of His human sacrifice are eternally present in His glorified state.\
\
## **7. It Illuminates Our Own Sonship**\
\
If the Son was **begotten of the Father in Spirit** as the Only-Begotten, and we \'97 as adopted sons \'97 are **born of the Spirit** (John 3:5-6), then our sonship, while categorically different from His unique Only-Begottenness, **shares the pattern**: we too are brought forth from the Father's Spirit into new life. This is why we can call the Father "Abba" \'97 because the Spirit of His Son has been sent into our hearts (Gal 4:6).\
