## **Examining Under Our Proposal**\
\
### **Phrase 1: \uc0\u7960 \u957  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8135  \u7974 \u957  \u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 ** \'97 *"In the beginning was the Word"*\
\
**Under your proposal:**\
\
*"In the beginning"* points back to Gen 1:1 LXX (**\uc0\u7960 \u957  \u7936 \u961 \u967 \u8135 **) \'97 the beginning of creation. **The Word (\u8001  \u923 \u972 \u947 \u959 \u962 ) was already existing at that beginning.** Not created at that beginning \'97 **already there.**\
\
The imperfect verb **\uc0\u7974 \u957 ** (*was existing*) denotes continuous existence at that point. When creation began, the Word already **was.**\
\
**This coheres with your proposal:** The Son, begotten of the Father in Spirit, existed with the Father before creation. When "the beginning" of Gen 1:1 dawned, He was already there \'97 the Only-Begotten, existing in the Spirit-mode of being with the Father.\
