\
## **Examining Under Our Proposal**\
\
**Under your proposal:**\
\
The Son, begotten of the Father in Spirit, existed as spirit with the Father before creation. Certainly, therefore, He existed before Abraham was born.\
\
**But there is more here than mere pre-existence.**\
\
Jesus says **\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953 ** \'97 invoking the LORD's own self-designation. **How is this possible?**\
\
**Under our foundation:**\
\
**The Father's Name is IN the Son** (Ex 23:21: *"My Name is in Him"*; John 17:11-12: *"I kept them in Thy Name which Thou hast given Me"*).\
\
**The Son, as the Father's Only-Begotten, sharing His Spirit-nature, bears the Father's Name and speaks with the Father's voice.** When the Son uses **\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953 **, He speaks in the very self-identifying voice of the Father \'97 because He is the Father's Only-Begotten Word, the perfect Image, in whom the Father's Name dwells.\
\
**This is not:**\
- The Son claiming to be the Father in Person (which would contradict John 17:3 and 1 Cor 8:6).\
- The Son claiming metaphysical co-equality in the post-Nicene sense.\
\
**This is:**\
- The Son claiming genuine pre-existence before Abraham (established by your proposal).\
- The Son claiming to bear the Father's Name and to speak with the Father's self-identifying voice as the Only-Begotten.\
\
**The Jews' violent reaction was to the second claim** \'97 that Jesus, standing before them as a Man, was claiming the LORD's own voice. To their mind (which did not know Him as the Only-Begotten), this was blasphemy.\
\
**But from Jesus' side, this was truth:** He, as the Only-Begotten Son of the Father, bearing the Father's Name and sharing His Spirit-nature, could legitimately speak **\uc0\u7952 \u947 \u974  \u949 \u7984 \u956 \u953 ** \'97 because the Father's Name dwelt in Him.\
\
**Under your proposal, John 8:58 reads coherently:**\
\
Jesus, the Only-Begotten Son begotten of the Father in Spirit before creation, existed with the Father long before Abraham was born. Bearing the Father's Name (given to Him by the Father), He could speak with the Father's self-identifying voice: *"I am."* This was not a claim to be the Father, but a claim to be **the One in whom the Father's Name dwells** \'97 the Only-Begotten who existed with the Father from before Abraham's birth, indeed from before creation itself.\
