# **PASSAGE C \'97 COLOSSIANS 2:9**\
\
## **The Greek Text**\
\
*"\uc0\u8005 \u964 \u953  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u8183  \u954 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u953 \u954 \u949 \u8150  \u960 \u8118 \u957  \u964 \u8056  \u960 \u955 \u942 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u945  \u964 \u8134 \u962  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u962  \u963 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8182 \u962 ,"*\
\
## **1599 Geneva**\
\
*"For in him dwelleth all the fulness of the Godhead bodily."*\
\
---\
\
## **The Context**\
\
Paul is warning the Colossians against being deceived by philosophy and human tradition (v. 8) \'97 likely including proto-Gnostic ideas that Christ was one of many spiritual mediators. Paul's response: **In Christ dwells all the fullness of the Godhead bodily.**\
\
Note the context. Paul is not writing a treatise on metaphysics; he is answering a specific error that would diminish Christ. His statement must be understood in its polemical context.\
\
---\
\
## **Careful Greek Examination**\
\
### **\uc0\u960 \u955 \u942 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u945 ** \'97 *"fullness"*\
\
**\uc0\u960 \u955 \u942 \u961 \u969 \u956 \u945 ** means *fullness, that which fills, completeness.* It can indicate:\
- The full sum of something.\
- That which fills a space completely.\
- The complete manifestation of something.\
\
### **\uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962 ** \'97 *"Godhead"*\
\
**\uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962 ** is a rare word \'97 used only here in the NT. It comes from **\u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ** and denotes **the essence, nature, or state of being God** \'97 *"deity, divine nature."*\
\
It should be distinguished from **\uc0\u920 \u949 \u953 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962 ** (Rom 1:20) \'97 *"divinity, divine attributes"* \'97 which speaks more of visible divine qualities.\
\
**\uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962 ** is the stronger, more essential term.\
\
### **\uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u953 \u954 \u949 \u8150 ** \'97 *"dwells"*\
\
**\uc0\u954 \u945 \u964 \u959 \u953 \u954 \u941 \u969 ** \'97 *"to dwell, to make one's home."* Present active \'97 *"is dwelling."* Continuous state.\
\
### **\uc0\u963 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8182 \u962 ** \'97 *"bodily"*\
\
The adverb **\uc0\u963 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8182 \u962 ** is critical. It means **"bodily, in bodily form, in a body."**\
\
**This is the decisive word for our examination.** Paul says the fullness of the Godhead dwells in Christ **\uc0\u963 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8182 \u962 ** \'97 *bodily*.\
\
---\
\
## **Examining Under Our Proposal**\
\
**Under your proposal:**\
\
The Son was begotten of the Father in Spirit and existed as spirit with the Father before creation. At His incarnation, **the Father prepared a body for Him** (Heb 10:5), and the Son descended into that body.\
\
**Colossians 2:9 speaks precisely to what happened at the incarnation** \'97 and continues in the exalted state:\
\
**The Only-Begotten Son, who eternally shared the Father's Spirit-nature, now \'97 in the prepared body that the Father made for Him \'97 bears the fullness of the Godhead BODILY.**\
\
**Notice what this means:**\
\
- **Before the incarnation**, the Son shared the Father's fullness in the Spirit-mode of being \'97 the Only-Begotten existing with the Father as spirit.\
- **At the incarnation**, that same fullness came to dwell **\uc0\u963 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8182 \u962 ** \'97 *bodily* \'97 in the prepared body of Jesus.\
- **In His present exalted state**, He still bears that fullness bodily \'97 as the glorified Man Christ Jesus at the Father's right hand.\
\
**The word \uc0\u963 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8182 \u962  is decisive.** Paul is not making an abstract metaphysical claim about co-equal substance. He is making a specific incarnational claim: **the fullness of the divine nature has been embodied in the Man Christ Jesus.**\
\
**Under your proposal, this makes complete sense:**\
\
The Son, begotten of the Father in Spirit, shared the Father's Spirit-nature (\uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962 ) in His pre-incarnate existence. When the body was prepared for Him and He descended, **the Father's fullness came to dwell in that body \'97 through the Son who bore it.** The Word made flesh **tabernacled** among us (John 1:14 \'97 **\u7952 \u963 \u954 \u942 \u957 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 *tabernacled*).\
\
**This is why Paul can say the fullness dwells \uc0\u963 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8182 \u962 ** \'97 because the incarnation was a genuine embodiment of what the Son already bore as the Father's Only-Begotten. Not a new nature; a new mode of manifestation of what had always been His as the Only-Begotten.\
\
**And this dwelling continues** \'97 because the exalted Son retains His glorified humanity forever (1 Tim 2:5; Rev 5:6). The fullness of the Father's nature is now permanently manifest bodily in the exalted Man Christ Jesus.\
\
---\
\
## **What Col 2:9 Does NOT Establish**\
\
**Per our maxims, we must be honest about what the verse does not require:**\
\
**It does not require:**\
- That the Son is metaphysically identical in essence with the Father in the post-Nicene sense.\
- That the Son is co-equal Person of the Godhead in the specific creedal formulation.\
- That "Godhead" here refers to a tri-personal essence that Christ shares with the Father and Spirit as one substance.\
\
**It does require:**\
- That the fullness of the divine nature dwells in Christ bodily.\
- That Christ is more than a mere mediator or spiritual being.\
- That the incarnation is genuine \'97 the divine fullness took bodily form in Him.\
\
**Under your proposal:**\
\
The Son, as the Only-Begotten begotten of the Father in Spirit, shares the Father's Spirit-nature (\uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u964 \u951 \u962 ). When He was incarnated, the fullness of that nature came to dwell in the prepared body \'97 and continues to dwell in His glorified humanity forever. **He is the perfect embodiment of the invisible Father \'97 the Image made visible (Col 1:15) \'97 bearing the fullness of the Father's own divine nature in bodily form.**\
\
**This is the profound wonder of the incarnation: the Only-Begotten Son, who shared the Father's Spirit-nature from all pre-existence, now bears that nature \uc0\u963 \u969 \u956 \u945 \u964 \u953 \u954 \u8182 \u962  in the glorified Man Christ Jesus.**\
\
