The Son, as the Father's Only-Begotten begotten in Spirit and bearing the Father's Name, can be called **\uc0\u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ** in the qualitative sense \'97 because He shares the Father's Spirit-nature and is the perfect embodiment of the Father's divine essence (per Col 2:9). This does not make Him identical Person with the Father, but it does mean He can be addressed with divine titles as the Father's Only-Begotten who bears His Name.\
