## **2. It Explains the Jews' Reaction Without Requiring a Metaphysical Claim**\
\
The Jews were correct that Jesus was invoking the LORD's Name. But they were wrong in concluding this was blasphemy \'97 because they did not recognize Him as the One in whom the Father's Name legitimately dwells.\
\
**Jesus was not claiming to be the Father.** He was claiming to be the One who bears the Father's Name \'97 the Only-Begotten sent with the Father's authority.\
