2. **"My God"** \'97 Acknowledging that in the risen Jesus, the Father's Name and fullness are manifest. As the Only-Begotten who bears the Father's Name and in whom the fullness of Godhead dwells bodily (Col 2:9), Jesus can be addressed with the divine designation.\
\
**Thomas is NOT confessing:**\
- That Jesus is identical Person with the Father.\
- That Jesus is the sole God to the exclusion of the Father.\
\
**Thomas is confessing that the risen Christ is the visible manifestation of the Father** \'97 the One in whom the Father's Name dwells, the Image of the invisible God, the fullness of Godhead bodily \'97 and therefore addressable with divine titles.\
