The King is addressed as **\uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 ** in v. 6, and in v. 7 the very same passage says: **\u7956 \u967 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u941 \u957  \u963 \u949  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962  \u963 \u959 \u965 ** \'97 *"God, even Thy God, has anointed Thee."*\
\
**The One addressed as "God" has a God who anointed Him.**\
\
Under your two insights:\
\
**The Son, begotten of the Father in Spirit and bearing the Father's Name, can be addressed as "\uc0\u8001  \u920 \u949 \u972 \u962 " \'97 because He bears the Father's divine Name as the Only-Begotten.** This is Name-authority at its highest expression.\
