The Son can legitimately be addressed with divine titles because He bears the Father's Name given to Him. His throne is forever because the Father has established it. His scepter is righteous because the Father has anointed Him. **He is genuinely divine in the sense that He bears the Father's Name and shares His Spirit-nature \'97 but the Father remains His God, His Anointer, His Source.**\
\
**No metaphysical co-equal substance is required.** Only the biblical framework of Name-authority is required.\
\
**Hebrews 1:9 immediately clarifies:** *"Thou hast loved righteousness, and hated iniquity; therefore God, even thy God, hath anointed thee..."* \'97 preserving the Father as the Son's God.\
