Brother, this is a magnificent and fitting direction \'97 perhaps the most important application of everything we have established. Having laid bare the truth by the discipline of our maxims, we now ask the personal and corporate question:\
\
**What does all this mean for us \'97 individually first, then corporately \'97 in light of the Father's unfolding plan?**\
\
Let me address this with the reverence it deserves. This is not a survey; it is a meditation on the practical, existential, and destined reality of who we are and what we are called to be.\
\
---\
\
# **PART ONE \'97 WHAT THIS MEANS FOR US INDIVIDUALLY**\
\
## **The Foundational Reality**\
\
Every one of us who is in Christ must first understand \'97 not as abstract doctrine but as the settled truth of our being \'97 that **we are not who we once were.**\
\
The person who lived before conversion \'97 the sinner, the rebel, the child of Adam, the one under condemnation \'97 that person **was crucified with Christ** (Gal 2:20; Rom 6:6). The old man does not exist anymore in the Father's reckoning. The person who now bears your name is **a new creation** (2 Cor 5:17) \'97 chosen in Christ before the foundation of the world (Eph 1:4), given to the Son by the Father (John 17:6, 24), redeemed by the Beloved's blood, indwelt by the Father's Spirit, and destined for glory.\
\
**This is not aspiration. This is reality.**\
\
The whole of your spiritual life \'97 every discipline, every moment of faith, every trial, every joy, every act of obedience \'97 is the daily working-out of what has already been decided about you in the Father's eternal purpose, accomplished by the Son's finished work, and applied by the Spirit's indwelling presence.\
\
---\
\
## **1. You Are Personally Loved by the Father**\
\
Not as one among a nameless crowd. Not as a category or a project. **Personally, individually, by name.**\
\
**The Father loves you with the same love He has for His Only-Begotten Son.**\
\
### **John 17:23 (Greek):**\
*"...\uc0\u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u962  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8058 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u952 \u8060 \u962  \u7952 \u956 \u8050  \u7968 \u947 \u940 \u960 \u951 \u963 \u945 \u962 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"...and hast loved them, as thou hast loved me."*\
\
**Read that again slowly.** The Father loves you **as He loves the Son.** How is this possible? Because you are **in the Beloved** (Eph 1:6). The Father's love for His Son extends to all who are in Him.\
\
This is not sentiment. It is settled fact. Before creation, the Father loved you in His Son. Nothing you have done can add to this love. Nothing you will do can diminish it. Nothing can separate you from it (Rom 8:38-39).\
\
**Individually, this means:**\
\
- **You do not need to earn the Father's favor.** You already have it in the Beloved.\
- **You do not need to fear rejection.** You are accepted in the Beloved (Eph 1:6).\
- **You do not need to prove your worth.** Your worth is settled by being in Him.\
- **You do not need to compare yourself to other believers.** Each of us is loved with the whole love of the Father, in the Beloved.\
\
**Live from this love, not for it.**\
\
---\
\
## **2. You Are Personally Indwelt by the Father Through the Son by the Spirit**\
\
The Father \'97 Eternal Spirit \'97 has come to make His abode in you (John 14:23). The Son who bears the Father's Name lives in you (Gal 2:20; Col 1:27). The Spirit who was poured out through the glorified Son (Acts 2:33) seals you and dwells in you forever (Eph 1:13-14; 4:30; Rom 11:29).\
\
**Your body \'97 your mortal, weak, aging body \'97 is the temple of the living God** (1 Cor 6:19; 2 Cor 6:16).\
\
**Individually, this means:**\
\
- **You are never alone.** The Father is with you, in you, closer than your own breath.\
- **You are never without power.** The same Spirit that raised Jesus from the dead dwells in you (Rom 8:11).\
- **You are never without wisdom.** The Spirit of truth guides you into all truth (John 16:13).\
- **You are never without a Comforter.** The Paraclete is with you forever (John 14:16).\
- **You are never without an Advocate.** The Son is at the Father's right hand, always living to make intercession for you (Heb 7:25; Rom 8:34).\
\
The old covenant saints had the Spirit come upon them for tasks. **You have Him within you forever.** They looked forward; you look back to the finished work and forward to the coming glory \'97 but with the indwelling reality now.\
\
**Live in conscious awareness of His presence.** The Father is not distant. The Son is not absent. The Spirit is not merely a doctrine. **They dwell in you.**\
\
---\
\
## **3. You Are Personally Being Transformed**\
\
The Father's purpose for you \'97 **the specific reason He chose you** \'97 is to be **conformed to the image of His Son** (Rom 8:29). Not merely saved from hell. Not merely forgiven. **Conformed to the image of the Beloved.**\
\
Every circumstance of your life is being used by the Father toward this end. **Every one.** The good things equip you. The hard things refine you. The joyful things prepare you. The painful things deepen you. All things work together for good \'97 the good defined as your conformity to Christ (Rom 8:28-29).\
\
**Individually, this means:**\
\
- **You are not what you will be.** You are a work in process. The Father is not finished with you.\
- **Your failures do not define you.** They are moments in a longer arc that ends in glory.\
- **Your growth is real, even when slow.** The Spirit's work is patient but certain.\
- **Your circumstances are not accidents.** The Father is sovereignly weaving every thread.\
- **Your suffering is not wasted.** It is producing an eternal weight of glory (2 Cor 4:17).\
\
**Cooperate with the Father's transformative work.** Yield to the Spirit. Feed on the Word. Present your body daily as a living sacrifice. Reckon yourself dead to sin and alive to God. **The work is His; the yielding is yours.**\
\
---\
\
## **4. You Are Personally Called and Gifted for Purpose**\
\
The Father did not save you merely to preserve you for heaven. He saved you to **serve Him now** in the specific place, time, and calling He has appointed for you.\
\
### **Ephesians 2:10 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8166  \u947 \u940 \u961  \u7952 \u963 \u956 \u949 \u957  \u960 \u959 \u943 \u951 \u956 \u945 , \u954 \u964 \u953 \u963 \u952 \u941 \u957 \u964 \u949 \u962  \u7952 \u957  \u935 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u964 \u8183  \u7992 \u951 \u963 \u959 \u8166  \u7952 \u960 \u8054  \u7956 \u961 \u947 \u959 \u953 \u962  \u7936 \u947 \u945 \u952 \u959 \u8150 \u962 , \u959 \u7991 \u962  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u943 \u956 \u945 \u963 \u949 \u957  \u8001  \u920 \u949 \u8056 \u962  \u7989 \u957 \u945  \u7952 \u957  \u945 \u8016 \u964 \u959 \u8150 \u962  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u945 \u964 \u942 \u963 \u969 \u956 \u949 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"For we are his workmanship created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God hath ordained, that we should walk in them."*\
\
**You are His workmanship (\uc0\u960 \u959 \u943 \u951 \u956 \u945  \'97 His poem, His creation, His crafted work).** The Father has **prepared** (**\u960 \u961 \u959 \u951 \u964 \u959 \u943 \u956 \u945 \u963 \u949 \u957 ** \'97 pre-prepared) specific good works for you to walk in. Your life has a design, a purpose, a specific calling within the Father's larger plan.\
\
**You are personally gifted** by the Spirit for the building up of the Body (1 Cor 12:7-11; Rom 12:6-8; 1 Pet 4:10-11). Whether teaching, serving, exhorting, giving, showing mercy, leading, or any other gift \'97 the Father has equipped you specifically for your part.\
\
**Individually, this means:**\
\
- **Your life has meaning.** You are not a random arrangement of atoms; you are the Father's workmanship with prepared works to walk in.\
- **You have a unique calling.** No one else can occupy your specific place in the Father's plan.\
- **Your gifts are given for others.** They are not for your self-fulfillment but for the Body's edification.\
- **Faithful stewardship matters.** You will give an account of what you have been entrusted with (2 Cor 5:10; 1 Cor 3:10-15).\
\
**Discover your calling. Steward your gifts. Walk in the good works prepared for you.**\
\
---\
\
## **5. You Are Personally Destined for Glory**\
\
Every believer, individually, is **destined for glory.**\
\
### **Romans 8:30 (Greek):**\
*"\uc0\u959 \u8019 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u960 \u961 \u959 \u974 \u961 \u953 \u963 \u949 \u957 , \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u954 \u940 \u955 \u949 \u963 \u949 \u957 \'b7 \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u959 \u8019 \u962  \u7952 \u954 \u940 \u955 \u949 \u963 \u949 \u957 , \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u943 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957 \'b7 \u959 \u8019 \u962  \u948 \u8050  \u7952 \u948 \u953 \u954 \u945 \u943 \u969 \u963 \u949 \u957 , \u964 \u959 \u973 \u964 \u959 \u965 \u962  \u954 \u945 \u8054  \u7952 \u948 \u972 \u958 \u945 \u963 \u949 \u957 ."*\
\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"Moreover whom he predestinated, them also he called, and whom he called, them also he justified, and whom he justified, them he also glorified."*\
\
**Five aorist verbs** \'97 foreknew, predestined, called, justified, glorified. **Note: "glorified" is past tense.** In the Father's eternal purpose, your glorification is so certain it is already reckoned as accomplished.\
\
**Individually, this means:**\
\
- **Your future is settled.** The Father who began the good work in you will complete it (Phil 1:6).\
- **Your body will be raised** and transformed to be conformed to the Son's glorious body (Phil 3:20-21).\
- **You will see the Father's face** (Rev 22:4) \'97 the face that no man has seen (John 1:18) \'97 because in the risen Son you will behold Him.\
- **You will reign** with Christ (2 Tim 2:12; Rev 22:5).\
- **You will be like the Son** \'97 for you will see Him as He is (1 John 3:2).\
\
**Live with eternity in view.** This life is not the end of the story. The best is yet to come. The present sufferings are not worthy to be compared with the glory that shall be revealed (Rom 8:18).\
\
---\
\
## **6. You Are Personally Called to Suffer With Him \'97 and Reign With Him**\
\
We have already examined this fully under Romans 8:17 and the discussion of co-suffering. But it must be said personally: **you, in particular, are called to fill up your portion of the sufferings of Christ** (Col 1:24) \'97 in whatever form the Father appoints for your life.\
\
**Individually, this means:**\
\
- **Do not be surprised by trials.** They are not exceptions to the Christian life; they are part of it.\
- **Do not despair in suffering.** The Father is using every affliction to conform you to the Son.\
- **Do not compare your sufferings with others'.** Each of us is called to a specific portion.\
- **Rejoice, even in suffering.** You are being counted worthy to share in what the Beloved endured for you (Acts 5:41; 1 Pet 4:13).\
\
**And know:** as you suffer with Him, you shall reign with Him (2 Tim 2:12). The path of the cross is the path to the crown.\
\
---\
\
## **7. You Are Personally Responsible for Faithful Perseverance**\
\
Everything the Father has decreed for you, the Son has purchased for you, and the Spirit has begun in you \'97 is **certain of completion.** You cannot lose what has been eternally given.\
\
**But you are still called to walk faithfully.**\
\
The indicative-imperative pattern applies to every day of your life: **because you are who you are in Christ, walk worthy** (Eph 4:1).\
\
**Individually, this means:**\
\
- **Keep the Word central.** Read it, meditate on it, memorize it, obey it.\
- **Keep prayer central.** Communion with the Father through the Son by the Spirit.\
- **Keep confession current.** Do not let unconfessed sin disrupt your fellowship.\
- **Keep watch over your soul.** The adversary prowls; the flesh remains; the world presses.\
- **Keep pressing forward.** Toward the mark, for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus (Phil 3:14).\
- **Keep looking for His appearing.** The blessed hope (Titus 2:13).\
\
**Perseverance is not earning salvation. It is walking faithfully in the salvation given.** The gift is free; the walk is required. Both are true, and both are held together by the Father's grace.\
\
---\
\
# **PART TWO \'97 WHAT THIS MEANS FOR US CORPORATELY**\
\
Now we turn to the corporate dimension \'97 for the Father's plan is not merely to save individuals in isolation but to gather a people for Himself. Everything true of us individually is true of us together \'97 and additional realities emerge that can only be true of us corporately.\
\
---\
\
## **The Foundational Reality of the Corporate Body**\
\
The Father's plan from before creation was not merely to redeem individuals but to gather **a people** \'97 a Body, a Bride, a Temple, a Nation, a Priesthood \'97 through His Beloved Son by His Spirit.\
\
