\
### **1599 Geneva:**\
*"But ye are a chosen generation, a royal Priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people, that ye should show forth the virtues of him that hath called you out of darkness into his marvelous light,"*\
\
**Corporately, this means:**\
\
- **We are a nation.** A people bound together not by borders or blood but by the New Covenant in the Beloved's blood.\
- **We are royal priests.** Every believer serves as priest \'97 offering sacrifices of praise, of prayer, of service (Heb 13:15-16).\
- **We are holy \'97 set apart.** For the Father's exclusive purposes, distinct from the world's patterns.\
- **We are peculiar (**\uc0\u955 \u945 \u8056 \u962  \u949 \u7984 \u962  \u960 \u949 \u961 \u953 \u960 \u959 \u943 \u951 \u963 \u953 \u957 ** \'97 "a people for God's own possession").** We belong to Him uniquely.\
- **We have a mission.** *"That you should show forth the virtues"* \'97 the excellencies \'97 *"of Him who called you out of darkness into His marvelous light."*\
\
**Our corporate life is missional.** We exist as a witness to the world of the Father's character, of the Son's saving work, and of the Spirit's transforming power. **The nations see the true God through the life of His people.**\
